1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:20,000
<font color="#00FF00">{\an8}Downloaded from MoviesMod.at</font>

2
00:00:30,490 --> 00:00:33,134
[popping]

3
00:00:46,400 --> 00:00:48,125
[soft rustling]

4
00:00:59,705 --> 00:01:02,026
[KAGAYA]
Within the next five days,

5
00:01:02,232 --> 00:01:03,725
Muzan will come.

6
00:01:10,091 --> 00:01:12,965
I will be the bait you use.

7
00:01:13,717 --> 00:01:17,077
When he comes,
I need you to behead him.

8
00:01:20,216 --> 00:01:24,284
Master, what leads you
to believe he'll find you?

9
00:01:25,124 --> 00:01:27,290
[Kagaya chuckles weakly]

10
00:01:27,511 --> 00:01:30,119
My intuition. That's all.

11
00:01:30,871 --> 00:01:32,596
Nothing beyond that.

12
00:01:33,170 --> 00:01:36,220
But listen,
the others can't know.

13
00:01:36,795 --> 00:01:41,526
They would never agree
to using me as bait like this.

14
00:01:41,748 --> 00:01:43,913
They would sooner die
than do it.

15
00:01:44,754 --> 00:01:48,514
You're the only one
that I can ask, Gyomei.

16
00:01:50,897 --> 00:01:54,517
Even if you behead him,
he won't die.

17
00:01:54,737 --> 00:01:56,106
♪

18
00:01:56,459 --> 00:02:00,210
There's likely only one way
to destroy Muzan.

19
00:02:00,432 --> 00:02:03,962
Trapping him in place
until sunlight shines upon him.

20
00:02:04,712 --> 00:02:07,582
If beheading isn't enough
to kill him,

21
00:02:07,803 --> 00:02:09,657
there's only one option left.

22
00:02:10,672 --> 00:02:14,512
You all must endure a battle
until the sun rises.

23
00:02:15,704 --> 00:02:16,703
Yes, sir.

24
00:02:17,934 --> 00:02:20,940
If that is your wish,
then so be it, Master.

25
00:02:24,814 --> 00:02:25,814
[KAGAYA] Thank goodness.

26
00:02:31,737 --> 00:02:35,185
Gyomei, after I have perished,

27
00:02:35,892 --> 00:02:38,677
please do not let
any more of my children

28
00:02:38,897 --> 00:02:40,224
be sent to their graves.

29
00:02:41,019 --> 00:02:43,186
That is my wish.

30
00:02:58,569 --> 00:03:00,735
[♪ tense music playing]

31
00:03:00,956 --> 00:03:03,078
[MUZAN] You think
you've driven me into a corner

32
00:03:03,298 --> 00:03:04,713
with your little plan?

33
00:03:06,393 --> 00:03:09,930
But you are all about to be
going straight to hell!

34
00:03:10,150 --> 00:03:12,140
Mark my words, Demon Slayers.

35
00:03:12,360 --> 00:03:15,853
I'll massacre every one of you
before sunrise!

36
00:03:16,073 --> 00:03:17,178
[grunts angrily]

37
00:03:17,400 --> 00:03:18,770
[Nakime plucking biwa strings]

38
00:03:20,097 --> 00:03:22,837
You're the only one
going to hell!

39
00:03:23,058 --> 00:03:24,605
And you won't get away!

40
00:03:25,622 --> 00:03:27,787
Oh, is that so?

41
00:03:27,965 --> 00:03:29,910
Let's see you try.

42
00:03:30,264 --> 00:03:31,424
Tanjiro Kamado!

43
00:03:31,743 --> 00:03:34,457
[rumbling]

44
00:03:34,855 --> 00:03:36,755
I will defeat you!

45
00:03:38,594 --> 00:03:39,594
Muzan Kibutsuji!

46
00:03:39,815 --> 00:03:44,965
DEMON SLAYER: KIMETSU NO YAIBA
THE MOVIE: INFINITY CASTLE

47
00:03:46,164 --> 00:03:48,961
[♪ opening theme song playing]

48
00:03:52,114 --> 00:03:53,114
What is this place?

49
00:03:53,709 --> 00:03:55,814
Everything's upside down.

50
00:03:57,142 --> 00:03:58,880
KILL

51
00:03:58,881 --> 00:04:01,216
Was all of this made using
the enemy's Blood Demon Art?

52
00:04:03,963 --> 00:04:06,251
I don't understand
what's happening,

53
00:04:06,434 --> 00:04:09,456
except that Ms. Tamayo
was restraining Muzan.

54
00:04:10,875 --> 00:04:14,170
Even so, how long
can she keep that up?

55
00:04:14,399 --> 00:04:16,826
[screaming]

56
00:04:17,054 --> 00:04:18,656
[IGURO] Calm down, Kanroji.

57
00:04:19,115 --> 00:04:20,115
[gasps] Yes!

58
00:04:20,637 --> 00:04:22,114
[IGURO] Stay with me.

59
00:04:34,632 --> 00:04:35,675
[gasps]

60
00:04:38,804 --> 00:04:41,107
[Gyomei grunts]

61
00:04:55,363 --> 00:04:56,798
[effort grunts]

62
00:04:57,233 --> 00:04:58,536
[effort grunts]

63
00:05:16,965 --> 00:05:19,573
[TANJIRO] I need to reach Muzan
as soon as possible

64
00:05:19,746 --> 00:05:22,616
and defeat him
by whatever means!

65
00:05:26,397 --> 00:05:28,222
[grunts]

66
00:05:29,917 --> 00:05:31,090
[♪ Gregorian chanting]

67
00:05:31,308 --> 00:05:32,655
That's the bottom!

68
00:05:32,873 --> 00:05:34,568
I'll be killed at this speed!

69
00:05:35,046 --> 00:05:36,785
I'll use a move
to change directions.

70
00:05:37,001 --> 00:05:39,045
Then find something
to grab on to.

71
00:05:39,261 --> 00:05:40,261
DESTROY

72
00:05:40,479 --> 00:05:42,000
[♪ music intensifies]

73
00:05:42,739 --> 00:05:46,607
It didn't work. I can't
break away from this free fall.

74
00:05:49,649 --> 00:05:50,736
DESTROYER OF DEMONS

75
00:06:05,905 --> 00:06:08,078
[♪ low tense music playing]

76
00:06:19,465 --> 00:06:21,030
[♪ music fades]

77
00:06:28,202 --> 00:06:30,331
[Tanjiro panting]

78
00:06:35,765 --> 00:06:36,765
[GIYU] You all right?

79
00:06:38,214 --> 00:06:40,841
Yes. Thanks for your help.

80
00:06:41,340 --> 00:06:42,517
[sighs in relief]

81
00:06:43,016 --> 00:06:44,374
You really saved--

82
00:06:46,413 --> 00:06:49,267
Water Breathing, First Form:

83
00:06:49,493 --> 00:06:50,943
Water Surface Slash.

84
00:06:53,254 --> 00:06:54,254
[GIYU] Tanjiro!

85
00:06:56,862 --> 00:06:58,863
[♪ intense music playing]

86
00:07:00,602 --> 00:07:02,603
[hinges creaking]

87
00:07:04,603 --> 00:07:05,864
[snarling]

88
00:07:16,344 --> 00:07:17,866
[BOTH] Water Breathing.

89
00:07:18,300 --> 00:07:19,692
[TANJIRO] Sixth Form.

90
00:07:19,866 --> 00:07:21,171
[GIYU] Third Form.

91
00:07:22,737 --> 00:07:24,475
[TANJIRO] Whirlpool!

92
00:07:24,693 --> 00:07:26,085
[GIYU] Flowing Dance.

93
00:07:31,738 --> 00:07:32,955
[Tanjiro groans nervously]

94
00:07:33,868 --> 00:07:35,782
Mr. Giyu's amazing.

95
00:07:36,782 --> 00:07:39,261
He can tell exactly which move
I'm gonna use.

96
00:07:39,740 --> 00:07:41,043
Then he follows up with one

97
00:07:41,261 --> 00:07:43,478
that prevents
any kind of friendly fire.

98
00:07:44,175 --> 00:07:45,957
He's unbelievable.

99
00:07:47,001 --> 00:07:49,045
Just what's behind those eyes?

100
00:07:49,263 --> 00:07:51,219
[stifled whimpering]

101
00:07:51,741 --> 00:07:53,306
If I'm not mistaken...

102
00:07:53,742 --> 00:07:54,959
this is the place

103
00:07:55,177 --> 00:07:57,177
that Shinazugawa and Iguro
mentioned.

104
00:07:57,394 --> 00:07:59,264
[♪ Gregorian chanting]

105
00:08:00,655 --> 00:08:01,917
Which means

106
00:08:02,134 --> 00:08:05,047
Kibutsuji's plan
was to gather everyone here,

107
00:08:05,265 --> 00:08:07,700
then kill us all
in one fell swoop.

108
00:08:09,483 --> 00:08:13,093
From here on out, we'll need
to be even more vigilant.

109
00:08:13,962 --> 00:08:15,093
Right.

110
00:08:17,180 --> 00:08:18,658
- Let's go.
- Right!

111
00:08:18,833 --> 00:08:19,833
PITTER PATTER

112
00:08:19,963 --> 00:08:21,920
[♪ dramatic music playing]

113
00:08:34,096 --> 00:08:35,705
[demons snarling]

114
00:08:41,358 --> 00:08:44,315
[IGURO]
Serpent Breathing, Fifth Form:

115
00:08:51,273 --> 00:08:53,534
Slithering Serpent!

116
00:08:56,013 --> 00:08:59,796
You demon scum!
Stay away from Kanroji!

117
00:09:00,013 --> 00:09:01,622
[squealing]

118
00:09:01,796 --> 00:09:04,014
Mr. Iguro is so cool!

119
00:09:05,101 --> 00:09:07,015
- Are you hurt?
- No, not at all!

120
00:09:07,231 --> 00:09:08,971
- Then, let's go.
- Okay!

121
00:09:09,493 --> 00:09:11,929
[Kanroji squealing]

122
00:09:21,060 --> 00:09:22,321
[grunts]

123
00:09:29,801 --> 00:09:30,932
Tokito!

124
00:09:31,148 --> 00:09:33,497
[demons snarling]

125
00:09:37,933 --> 00:09:40,107
[MUICHIRO] There's a whole lot
of demons, huh?

126
00:09:40,324 --> 00:09:41,803
[GYOMEI] It would seem
they've been given

127
00:09:42,020 --> 00:09:43,760
the strength of the Lower Ranks.

128
00:09:43,934 --> 00:09:47,021
It's clear that they're being
used to try and exhaust us.

129
00:09:48,891 --> 00:09:50,804
[metallic rattling]

130
00:09:51,022 --> 00:09:52,022
[MUICHIRO] Hmm.

131
00:09:52,761 --> 00:09:54,196
What of the Master?

132
00:09:55,283 --> 00:09:58,153
[GYOMEI] He has departed
from this world.

133
00:09:58,718 --> 00:10:01,197
It was a truly noble end.

134
00:10:02,414 --> 00:10:03,980
Knowing him,

135
00:10:04,198 --> 00:10:07,328
he never would have allowed
himself to be caught unawares.

136
00:10:08,068 --> 00:10:10,199
Did he sacrifice himself?

137
00:10:10,894 --> 00:10:14,982
[GYOMEI] Indeed. The Master
did not have much time left.

138
00:10:21,983 --> 00:10:23,244
[MUICHIRO] Master.

139
00:10:29,984 --> 00:10:32,768
Back when I was mortally wounded
by a demon

140
00:10:32,985 --> 00:10:34,855
and found myself
teetering on the edge

141
00:10:35,072 --> 00:10:36,507
between life and death...

142
00:10:37,377 --> 00:10:39,247
...he stayed by my side.

143
00:10:41,943 --> 00:10:44,857
He did the same
for every Corps member

144
00:10:45,074 --> 00:10:46,682
who was on the brink of death.

145
00:10:48,858 --> 00:10:50,335
Like a father.

146
00:10:52,554 --> 00:10:53,954
[GYOMEI] Yes, I know.

147
00:10:54,566 --> 00:10:57,496
[MUICHIRO] Muzan not only
took my brother from me,

148
00:10:58,064 --> 00:10:59,638
but our father as well.

149
00:11:00,644 --> 00:11:02,218
That bastard.

150
00:11:02,437 --> 00:11:03,618
Damn him!

151
00:11:04,011 --> 00:11:06,241
I swear I'll make him suffer.

152
00:11:06,460 --> 00:11:08,383
I'll send him straight to hell!

153
00:11:09,565 --> 00:11:11,138
[GYOMEI] You're not alone.

154
00:11:15,423 --> 00:11:18,529
Trust me, we all feel the same.

155
00:11:23,294 --> 00:11:25,569
DESTROY

156
00:11:25,787 --> 00:11:27,843
[SHINAZUGAWA]
Forgive me, Master.

157
00:11:29,504 --> 00:11:31,085
I couldn't protect you.

158
00:11:34,046 --> 00:11:36,382
[distorted grunting]

159
00:11:37,926 --> 00:11:39,553
[blade rasps]

160
00:11:42,515 --> 00:11:44,101
[♪ upbeat music playing]

161
00:11:45,351 --> 00:11:48,730
There's no end
to you lowlifes, huh?

162
00:11:49,273 --> 00:11:51,401
[demon cackling]

163
00:11:51,609 --> 00:11:53,695
That's just fine by me.

164
00:11:53,904 --> 00:11:56,484
I'll kill all of you!

165
00:12:04,778 --> 00:12:06,265
[INOSUKE] Hyah!

166
00:12:06,851 --> 00:12:09,870
Make way! I'm coming through!

167
00:12:10,412 --> 00:12:12,170
[chuckles]

168
00:12:12,395 --> 00:12:15,145
Whole lotta falling
happening here!

169
00:12:16,046 --> 00:12:20,329
Hyah! Pretty rude to just
drop me in here out of nowhere!

170
00:12:20,509 --> 00:12:23,033
Though I've been itching to see
how my training's paying off.

171
00:12:23,258 --> 00:12:27,271
So with that in mind,
let's test it out on you chubs!

172
00:12:27,495 --> 00:12:28,623
[chuckles]

173
00:12:28,848 --> 00:12:31,012
Let's go!

174
00:12:31,237 --> 00:12:33,807
[grunting]

175
00:12:35,249 --> 00:12:37,593
[Genya panting]

176
00:12:38,134 --> 00:12:40,839
Where am I?
The Demon Headquarters?

177
00:12:41,065 --> 00:12:42,375
Where are the others?

178
00:12:43,031 --> 00:12:44,605
Big Brother.

179
00:12:45,670 --> 00:12:47,803
I hope you're safe, too.

180
00:12:52,514 --> 00:12:53,514
[ZENITSU] I just heard a sound.

181
00:12:54,894 --> 00:12:56,174
Could it be that
he's somewhere nearby?

182
00:12:56,695 --> 00:12:59,091
[demons snarling]

183
00:13:00,620 --> 00:13:01,835
You'll regret this.

184
00:13:03,225 --> 00:13:04,225
I won't forgive you.

185
00:13:04,455 --> 00:13:06,383
Not in a million years.

186
00:13:17,634 --> 00:13:19,975
♪

187
00:13:32,191 --> 00:13:33,752
[SHINOBU] I smell blood.

188
00:13:43,441 --> 00:13:45,140
What is this place?

189
00:13:53,314 --> 00:13:55,335
[chomping]

190
00:14:03,004 --> 00:14:04,004
[DEMON] Hmm?

191
00:14:05,605 --> 00:14:06,725
Oh, my. You're here.

192
00:14:07,471 --> 00:14:08,544
UPPER TWO

193
00:14:08,730 --> 00:14:10,689
Oh! And you're a girl, too!

194
00:14:11,480 --> 00:14:15,211
What a young and tasty morsel
we have. [chuckles]

195
00:14:16,004 --> 00:14:18,004
I'll have to properly thank
Nakime for this later.

196
00:14:22,795 --> 00:14:27,143
[Shinobu panting]

197
00:14:43,203 --> 00:14:47,552
[whimpers softly]

198
00:14:50,215 --> 00:14:51,215
[KANAE] Shinobu.

199
00:14:51,386 --> 00:14:53,766
You must leave
the Demon Slayer Corps.

200
00:14:55,215 --> 00:14:57,457
I know that
you've trained really hard

201
00:14:58,009 --> 00:14:59,837
and you're fighting
to make a difference.

202
00:15:00,251 --> 00:15:02,700
- [sobbing softly]
- But I don't think you'll...

203
00:15:03,051 --> 00:15:04,051
[sighs softly]

204
00:15:04,217 --> 00:15:05,424
[stifled sobbing]

205
00:15:07,218 --> 00:15:10,218
I want you to live the life
of a happy, normal girl.

206
00:15:10,735 --> 00:15:13,184
To be able to see
your own hair turn gray.

207
00:15:14,191 --> 00:15:15,191
DESTROYER OF DEMONS

208
00:15:15,323 --> 00:15:17,219
Really... you've done enough.

209
00:15:17,392 --> 00:15:19,186
[SHINOBU] No! [sobbing]
Can't stop now!

210
00:15:19,323 --> 00:15:21,669
I will avenge you
if it's the last thing I do!

211
00:15:21,841 --> 00:15:23,634
This demon! I need to know...

212
00:15:23,807 --> 00:15:25,256
I have to know
what it looked like!

213
00:15:25,670 --> 00:15:27,670
Please, Big Sister,
I'm begging you!

214
00:15:27,843 --> 00:15:29,118
Tell me!

215
00:15:29,291 --> 00:15:32,395
I could never live a normal life
knowing someone did this to you!

216
00:15:32,567 --> 00:15:33,809
[sobbing] Please!

217
00:15:34,878 --> 00:15:35,878
[sighs weakly]

218
00:15:37,534 --> 00:15:38,603
[KANAE] It was a demon

219
00:15:38,775 --> 00:15:40,948
with a blood-stained pattern
on his head.

220
00:15:42,466 --> 00:15:44,777
[DEMON] I must say, it's very
nice to meet you, miss.

221
00:15:44,950 --> 00:15:46,915
You may refer to me as Doma.

222
00:15:47,295 --> 00:15:49,014
Ah, what a wonderful night!

223
00:15:51,057 --> 00:15:55,201
[SHINOBU] Such a warm smile
and gentle voice.

224
00:15:55,901 --> 00:16:00,279
There's a soft,
benevolent presence to him.

225
00:16:02,205 --> 00:16:03,863
[woman weakly] Please, help me.

226
00:16:03,864 --> 00:16:04,945
Please help me!

227
00:16:06,004 --> 00:16:07,004
Shh.

228
00:16:07,429 --> 00:16:09,130
Can't you see that
we're talking?

229
00:16:12,455 --> 00:16:13,455
Hmm?

230
00:16:14,055 --> 00:16:15,055
[SHINOBU] Are you all right?

231
00:16:15,685 --> 00:16:16,991
[DOMA] Wow!

232
00:16:17,201 --> 00:16:19,938
That was fast.
Are you a Hashira?

233
00:16:20,149 --> 00:16:21,917
[labored breathing]

234
00:16:22,633 --> 00:16:24,064
[squelching]

235
00:16:24,780 --> 00:16:27,180
- [gasps]
- [♪ unsettling music playing]

236
00:16:28,274 --> 00:16:30,211
[DOMA]
Oh, don't worry about that.

237
00:16:30,381 --> 00:16:32,107
You can just leave her
right there.

238
00:16:32,317 --> 00:16:34,338
I'll make
a proper meal of her later.

239
00:16:34,801 --> 00:16:35,812
[exhales]

240
00:16:37,496 --> 00:16:39,011
And this demon...

241
00:16:39,474 --> 00:16:41,117
the weapon he used,

242
00:16:41,706 --> 00:16:44,232
it was a pair of sharp fans.

243
00:16:45,117 --> 00:16:46,633
[metallic scraping]

244
00:16:47,138 --> 00:16:50,085
As the founder
of the Eternal Paradise Faith,

245
00:16:50,295 --> 00:16:52,022
it is my sworn duty to see that

246
00:16:52,232 --> 00:16:54,506
all my followers
attain happiness.

247
00:16:54,969 --> 00:16:57,496
I'll be sure
to consume her completely.

248
00:16:59,348 --> 00:17:00,654
[SHINOBU] There's no doubt.

249
00:17:00,864 --> 00:17:04,024
This is the demon
who killed my sister.

250
00:17:05,530 --> 00:17:07,538
Attaining happiness?

251
00:17:07,767 --> 00:17:09,318
For who exactly?

252
00:17:09,821 --> 00:17:12,879
This girl was horrified,
crying out for help.

253
00:17:13,427 --> 00:17:15,344
- And that's why I saved her.
- [fans scraping]

254
00:17:16,029 --> 00:17:18,951
Her suffering
has come to an end.

255
00:17:19,316 --> 00:17:20,960
No more pain.

256
00:17:21,279 --> 00:17:22,694
No more fear.

257
00:17:23,743 --> 00:17:25,085
Everyone is afraid of death.

258
00:17:25,529 --> 00:17:28,155
So I help them
by consuming them.

259
00:17:28,823 --> 00:17:33,451
This way, they get to live on
within me for all eternity.

260
00:17:33,674 --> 00:17:36,343
I take in their entire being.

261
00:17:36,521 --> 00:17:38,613
Blood. Desires.

262
00:17:39,191 --> 00:17:40,927
Even the last bit of their sinew

263
00:17:41,461 --> 00:17:44,309
- and help their souls transcend.
- [♪ unsettling music playing]

264
00:17:44,532 --> 00:17:47,024
What you're spouting
is sheer nonsense.

265
00:17:47,646 --> 00:17:49,561
And to say it with such glee...

266
00:17:50,050 --> 00:17:52,008
You truly make me sick!

267
00:17:52,230 --> 00:17:54,056
Aw.

268
00:17:54,722 --> 00:17:58,461
I can't believe you'd say that
after we'd only just met.

269
00:17:58,684 --> 00:18:00,124
Oh, I see.

270
00:18:00,330 --> 00:18:02,317
Oh, you poor thing.

271
00:18:02,525 --> 00:18:04,785
Did something unfortunate
happen?

272
00:18:04,956 --> 00:18:06,058
Let's hear it.

273
00:18:06,231 --> 00:18:07,231
Go on, tell me.

274
00:18:08,297 --> 00:18:10,811
"Unfortunate" doesn't begin
to describe it!

275
00:18:10,984 --> 00:18:14,644
You are the one who killed
my big sister, weren't you?

276
00:18:16,402 --> 00:18:23,402
Does the haori I'm wearing
mean nothing to you?!

277
00:18:47,201 --> 00:18:54,201
Huh?

278
00:19:02,595 --> 00:19:09,595
♪

279
00:19:44,826 --> 00:19:51,826
[blade rasps]

280
00:20:43,331 --> 00:20:50,331
[flesh squelching]

281
00:21:01,374 --> 00:21:02,373
[DOMA] That's right.

282
00:21:02,374 --> 00:21:09,374
It belonged to the girl
who used Flower Breathing.

283
00:21:13,275 --> 00:21:20,275
Such a sweet, gentle child.

284
00:21:23,625 --> 00:21:30,625
The sun came up
and cut our time short.

285
00:21:32,596 --> 00:21:36,458
I remember.

286
00:21:37,149 --> 00:21:44,149
It's a shame I didn't get-- Her.

287
00:21:50,674 --> 00:21:51,673
[SHINOBU] Insect Breathing,

288
00:21:51,674 --> 00:21:52,516
Dance of the Bee Sting:
True Flutter.

289
00:21:52,517 --> 00:21:52,929
A marvelous thrust.

290
00:21:52,930 --> 00:21:53,676
I hardly even saw it.

291
00:21:53,677 --> 00:21:54,247
Blood Demon Art:

292
00:21:54,248 --> 00:21:54,924
Frozen Lotus.

293
00:21:54,925 --> 00:21:55,240
[Shinobu shivering] So cold.

294
00:21:55,241 --> 00:21:55,864
It feels like my lungs
are bursting.

295
00:21:55,865 --> 00:21:56,171
[DOMA] Hmm.

296
00:21:56,172 --> 00:21:56,681
Look at that. You are fast.

297
00:21:56,682 --> 00:21:57,146
Unfortunately for you,

298
00:21:57,147 --> 00:21:57,788
those thrusts aren't enough
to kill a demon.

299
00:21:57,789 --> 00:21:58,148
[slurps]

300
00:21:58,149 --> 00:21:58,420
[rattling]

301
00:21:58,421 --> 00:21:58,833
Aim for here.

302
00:21:58,834 --> 00:21:59,572
You need to chop off my head.

303
00:21:59,573 --> 00:21:59,826
DESTROY

304
00:21:59,827 --> 00:22:00,398
My thrusts alone
may not be enough,

305
00:22:00,399 --> 00:22:00,696
but what of this?

306
00:22:00,697 --> 00:22:01,285
- [clanks]
- [ratchets, clicks]

307
00:22:01,286 --> 00:22:01,584
[Doma groans]

308
00:22:01,585 --> 00:22:02,058
[SHINOBU] Time to see
whether this toxin

309
00:22:02,059 --> 00:22:02,708
works on an Upper Rank.

310
00:22:02,709 --> 00:22:03,708
Sister, lend me
your strength, please.

311
00:22:03,709 --> 00:22:04,114
[retches]

312
00:22:04,115 --> 00:22:04,501
[straining] This poison.

313
00:22:04,502 --> 00:22:05,142
It's clearly far stronger
than the strain you used

314
00:22:05,143 --> 00:22:05,775
up on Rui's mountain. [wheezing]

315
00:22:05,776 --> 00:22:06,328
[SHINOBU] So they did
exchange information.

316
00:22:06,329 --> 00:22:06,847
This is the drawback
to using poison.

317
00:22:06,848 --> 00:22:07,664
[DOMA] He told me that
you've been changing concoction

318
00:22:07,665 --> 00:22:08,340
for each demon you face.
[straining]

319
00:22:08,341 --> 00:22:08,920
- [coughs, retches]
- [blood splatters]

320
00:22:08,921 --> 00:22:09,781
[wheezing]

321
00:22:09,782 --> 00:22:10,159
Oh, my.

322
00:22:10,160 --> 00:22:11,056
It would seem that I've already
neutralized all of your poison.

323
00:22:11,057 --> 00:22:11,328
How rude of me.

324
00:22:11,329 --> 00:22:12,057
And after you'd made it
just for me.

325
00:22:12,058 --> 00:22:12,558
That sword of yours,

326
00:22:12,559 --> 00:22:13,366
it makes quite an interesting
sound when you sheathe it.

327
00:22:13,367 --> 00:22:14,078
Is that where you change
what poison you use?

328
00:22:14,079 --> 00:22:14,781
Yay! This is fun!

329
00:22:14,782 --> 00:22:15,405
Who knew being poisoned
was so invigorating?

330
00:22:15,406 --> 00:22:15,765
It's almost addictive.

331
00:22:15,766 --> 00:22:16,266
What will the next formula
be like? [chuckles]

332
00:22:16,267 --> 00:22:17,048
Come on, let's give it a try.

333
00:22:17,049 --> 00:22:17,962
- [swishing]
- [rattling]

334
00:22:17,963 --> 00:22:18,401
Very well then,

335
00:22:18,402 --> 00:22:18,735
I'll oblige.

336
00:22:18,736 --> 00:22:19,666
See...

337
00:22:19,667 --> 00:22:20,325
...I'd already anticipated
this would happen.

338
00:22:20,326 --> 00:22:21,037
[Doma chuckling]
Is your next batch set?

339
00:22:21,038 --> 00:22:22,037
I'm ready whenever you are.

340
00:22:22,038 --> 00:22:23,077
I know I just said
to give it a try...

341
00:22:23,182 --> 00:22:24,181
...but you could at least
change up your offense.

342
00:22:24,182 --> 00:22:24,833
- [metallic clanking]
- [Doma chuckles]

343
00:22:24,834 --> 00:22:25,834
- [continues chuckling]
- [grunts]

344
00:22:26,558 --> 00:22:27,135
What's this?

345
00:22:27,136 --> 00:22:27,636
You seem to be
slower than earlier.

346
00:22:27,637 --> 00:22:27,952
So sad.

347
00:22:27,953 --> 00:22:28,646
[SHINOBU] Insect Breathing,
Dance of the Horsefly:

348
00:22:28,647 --> 00:22:29,647
Enticing Slash!

349
00:22:30,327 --> 00:22:31,221
Oh, my.
You were able to land a hit.

350
00:22:31,222 --> 00:22:31,801
The way you got through
all my defenses,

351
00:22:31,802 --> 00:22:32,108
it's amazing!

352
00:22:32,109 --> 00:22:32,416
I'm truly impressed.

353
00:22:32,417 --> 00:22:33,031
It's almost enough
to bring a tear to my eye.

354
00:22:33,032 --> 00:22:33,488
Come on,
what are you waiting for?

355
00:22:33,489 --> 00:22:34,296
Hurry up and attack me again,
before I stop the poison.

356
00:22:34,297 --> 00:22:34,832
Please? You're doing so well.

357
00:22:34,833 --> 00:22:35,210
Maybe the next attack kills me.

358
00:22:35,211 --> 00:22:36,159
[disgruntled sigh]

359
00:22:36,160 --> 00:22:37,160
[laughs] Yes! That's the spirit!

360
00:22:37,304 --> 00:22:38,013
Ever since I was a child,

361
00:22:38,014 --> 00:22:41,214
I was kind and clever.

362
00:22:42,028 --> 00:22:44,380
I always helped those
who were in need

363
00:22:44,606 --> 00:22:46,959
and led them
to the path of happiness.

364
00:22:47,909 --> 00:22:49,944
It was my duty after all.

365
00:22:51,617 --> 00:22:54,557
[DOMA'S FATHER] His eyes
have the colors of a rainbow.

366
00:22:55,597 --> 00:22:58,855
And this gray hair
is proof of his innocence.

367
00:22:59,895 --> 00:23:01,930
This child is truly special.

368
00:23:02,474 --> 00:23:03,914
Surely he can hear
the voices of the gods.

369
00:23:04,253 --> 00:23:06,914
[♪ slow piano notes playing]

370
00:23:07,254 --> 00:23:09,755
[DOMA] My parents were
hopelessly naive simpletons.

371
00:23:10,380 --> 00:23:12,121
You'd have to be

372
00:23:12,122 --> 00:23:15,922
in order to found a religion
like the Eternal Paradise Faith.

373
00:23:16,905 --> 00:23:18,558
I pitied them,

374
00:23:18,737 --> 00:23:22,223
so I always played along
with their make-believe ideas.

375
00:23:23,385 --> 00:23:26,379
I never once heard
the voice of the gods.

376
00:23:27,318 --> 00:23:30,088
At first, I didn't know
how to deal

377
00:23:30,312 --> 00:23:33,797
with the hordes of people
worshiping and praying to me.

378
00:23:34,781 --> 00:23:37,909
Seeing these grown-ups
come crying to a child

379
00:23:38,133 --> 00:23:41,127
saying they were suffering,
pleading for help,

380
00:23:41,306 --> 00:23:44,613
made me worry
if they were sick in the head.

381
00:23:45,909 --> 00:23:49,708
After nearly putting me to sleep
with their personal stories,

382
00:23:49,931 --> 00:23:51,495
they would bow to me,

383
00:23:51,674 --> 00:23:54,222
asking to be guided to paradise.

384
00:23:54,714 --> 00:23:55,714
I cried.

385
00:23:56,954 --> 00:23:59,168
"You poor things," I thought.

386
00:23:59,655 --> 00:24:01,735
"Paradise doesn't even exist.

387
00:24:02,444 --> 00:24:06,607
It's just a fairy tale
concocted by deluded humans.

388
00:24:07,714 --> 00:24:08,755
There are no gods or Buddhas."

389
00:24:11,974 --> 00:24:15,474
These people
had lived for decades,

390
00:24:15,608 --> 00:24:17,914
yet they still couldn't grasp
that simple truth.

391
00:24:18,348 --> 00:24:20,754
When you die,
you return to nothingness.

392
00:24:20,921 --> 00:24:22,425
All feeling ceases.

393
00:24:22,994 --> 00:24:24,275
Your heart stops.

394
00:24:24,835 --> 00:24:25,934
Your brain stops.

395
00:24:26,495 --> 00:24:28,035
You rot and return to the earth.

396
00:24:28,568 --> 00:24:31,770
Such is the fate
of every living creature.

397
00:24:33,993 --> 00:24:37,327
To be too foolish
to accept reality,

398
00:24:37,950 --> 00:24:40,173
what a hard life that must be.

399
00:24:41,195 --> 00:24:44,486
I want to bring happiness
to these pitiful people.

400
00:24:44,975 --> 00:24:46,709
I want to save them.

401
00:24:47,598 --> 00:24:52,089
I truly believe
that is my purpose here.

402
00:24:56,180 --> 00:24:57,180
[squelches]

403
00:24:57,336 --> 00:24:58,624
[blade rasps]

404
00:24:58,625 --> 00:25:01,115
- Aw. Still nothing.
- [metallic rattling]

405
00:25:01,338 --> 00:25:02,849
And that was number five.

406
00:25:03,072 --> 00:25:04,406
What will you do?

407
00:25:04,983 --> 00:25:07,474
The toxin's
getting less effective.

408
00:25:08,007 --> 00:25:10,720
How many more times
do you think you can adapt it?

409
00:25:11,342 --> 00:25:13,699
- Oh! Are you out of breath now?
- [panting]

410
00:25:14,276 --> 00:25:15,922
Look at all that sweat.

411
00:25:16,144 --> 00:25:17,144
Are you all right?

412
00:25:17,449 --> 00:25:20,500
[SHINOBU] So, this is the power
of an Upper Rank.

413
00:25:21,199 --> 00:25:23,247
None of my poisons are working.

414
00:25:24,207 --> 00:25:27,346
He's adapting too fast
to keep up with.

415
00:25:29,525 --> 00:25:31,924
Your alveoli must be dead now.

416
00:25:32,141 --> 00:25:34,060
[crystals tinkling]

417
00:25:34,235 --> 00:25:35,499
Painful.

418
00:25:35,716 --> 00:25:38,856
You did breathe it in,
my Blood Demon Art.

419
00:25:41,036 --> 00:25:43,870
[SHINOBU] He turns
his frozen blood into mist

420
00:25:44,087 --> 00:25:46,268
and disperses it with his fans.

421
00:25:46,443 --> 00:25:49,364
Even breathing around him
is dangerous now.

422
00:25:55,162 --> 00:25:56,296
[clangs]

423
00:25:56,470 --> 00:25:58,082
[ratchets, clicks]

424
00:25:58,083 --> 00:26:01,397
This time, I'll increase
the dose with multiple strikes!

425
00:26:02,269 --> 00:26:05,451
Insect Breathing,
Dance of the Dragonfly:

426
00:26:05,670 --> 00:26:07,151
♪

427
00:26:12,341 --> 00:26:14,608
Compound Eye Hexagon!

428
00:26:17,179 --> 00:26:18,532
I can't believe it!

429
00:26:18,749 --> 00:26:20,537
Such blazing speed!

430
00:26:20,755 --> 00:26:22,595
You might be the fastest Hashira
I've ever met.

431
00:26:25,128 --> 00:26:26,675
- [blood squelches]
- [gasps]

432
00:26:27,191 --> 00:26:29,816
[SHINOBU] He... got me.

433
00:26:30,050 --> 00:26:31,223
[grunts]

434
00:26:31,457 --> 00:26:33,146
Forget the poison.

435
00:26:33,380 --> 00:26:35,537
Why not try to decapitate me?

436
00:26:36,100 --> 00:26:38,726
With your speed,
you might have won.

437
00:26:39,757 --> 00:26:42,149
[laughs sarcastically]
Maybe not.

438
00:26:42,336 --> 00:26:44,541
I mean, you are small.

439
00:26:45,103 --> 00:26:46,744
[gasps, breathing shakily]

440
00:26:48,714 --> 00:26:51,194
[SHINOBU] Why are my hands
so small? I wonder.

441
00:26:53,355 --> 00:26:55,495
How come I was never able
to grow taller?

442
00:26:58,755 --> 00:27:02,595
If my stature
were just a little bigger,

443
00:27:02,944 --> 00:27:05,709
could I have been able to behead
and defeat a demon?

444
00:27:06,374 --> 00:27:09,675
The longer
your arms and legs are,

445
00:27:09,849 --> 00:27:11,540
the more muscles you have,

446
00:27:11,758 --> 00:27:14,143
which means more strength
in your attacks.

447
00:27:15,618 --> 00:27:17,267
[♪ tender music playing]

448
00:27:17,483 --> 00:27:20,216
My sister
was also of small frame,

449
00:27:20,433 --> 00:27:22,125
but she was taller than I.

450
00:27:24,251 --> 00:27:26,854
How I envy Mr. Himejima.

451
00:27:27,461 --> 00:27:29,934
Seeing someone like him
come to the rescue

452
00:27:30,151 --> 00:27:32,580
would give anyone relief.

453
00:27:35,616 --> 00:27:38,697
I know what my sister
really wanted to say,

454
00:27:39,434 --> 00:27:41,820
but didn't have the heart to.

455
00:27:44,900 --> 00:27:46,418
[DOMA] Oh, no!

456
00:27:46,635 --> 00:27:48,500
Have our games come to an end?

457
00:27:48,848 --> 00:27:50,409
That's too bad.

458
00:27:51,364 --> 00:27:53,402
[metallic rattling]

459
00:27:53,966 --> 00:27:57,046
[SHINOBU] "I don't think
you'll win against that demon."

460
00:27:57,610 --> 00:27:59,823
[voice breaking] That's what
you were going to say.

461
00:28:00,039 --> 00:28:02,339
But you stopped yourself,
didn't you?

462
00:28:02,816 --> 00:28:04,638
[KANAE] Pull yourself together.

463
00:28:10,234 --> 00:28:12,186
This is no time for tears.

464
00:28:13,835 --> 00:28:14,834
[SHINOBU] Sister.

465
00:28:14,835 --> 00:28:15,835
[KANAE] Stand up.

466
00:28:15,953 --> 00:28:17,739
[SHINOBU] I can't.
I've lost so much blood.

467
00:28:17,835 --> 00:28:22,134
My left lung is punctured
and I can't even breathe.

468
00:28:22,735 --> 00:28:24,494
You can and you will.

469
00:28:25,096 --> 00:28:28,797
Stand up.
You are a Hashira, Shinobu.

470
00:28:29,259 --> 00:28:31,157
[grunting softly]

471
00:28:31,805 --> 00:28:33,965
If you've made up your mind
to defeat him, then do so.

472
00:28:34,176 --> 00:28:35,665
No excuses.

473
00:28:36,982 --> 00:28:39,404
Win by whatever means you can.

474
00:28:39,915 --> 00:28:41,955
Remember your promise,

475
00:28:42,167 --> 00:28:43,613
to me and Kanao.

476
00:28:46,078 --> 00:28:47,310
[SHINOBU] Kanao.

477
00:28:50,243 --> 00:28:52,071
[DOMA] Forgive me.

478
00:28:52,284 --> 00:28:54,451
You must be suffering right now.

479
00:28:54,664 --> 00:28:56,576
[whimpering softly]

480
00:28:58,150 --> 00:28:59,254
[gasps]

481
00:28:59,467 --> 00:29:01,337
I know that you have it in you.

482
00:29:01,719 --> 00:29:03,038
Do your best.

483
00:29:04,015 --> 00:29:05,884
- Huh?
- [metallic rattling]

484
00:29:06,990 --> 00:29:08,435
[quivers]

485
00:29:09,158 --> 00:29:13,748
Wait. Are you... standing up?
[exclaims in amazement]

486
00:29:13,918 --> 00:29:15,321
Scary.

487
00:29:15,534 --> 00:29:18,774
Are you actually a human?

488
00:29:18,950 --> 00:29:22,890
I slashed your collarbone,
your lungs, and your ribs.

489
00:29:24,028 --> 00:29:26,087
At your diminutive size

490
00:29:26,305 --> 00:29:28,451
and the amount of blood
you've lost,

491
00:29:28,669 --> 00:29:30,553
how are you not dead right now?

492
00:29:30,771 --> 00:29:31,771
[coughs]

493
00:29:31,866 --> 00:29:33,224
See? Right there.

494
00:29:33,442 --> 00:29:36,245
There clearly is blood
gurgling in your lungs.

495
00:29:36,464 --> 00:29:38,915
The pain must be unimaginable.

496
00:29:39,354 --> 00:29:42,113
Surrender and I'll put an end
to your suffering.

497
00:29:42,331 --> 00:29:43,470
It'll be quick.

498
00:29:44,390 --> 00:29:46,316
It's too late for you.

499
00:29:46,535 --> 00:29:48,111
So, just let go.

500
00:29:48,330 --> 00:29:50,913
[SHINOBU] I'll make a go
for his neck this time

501
00:29:51,089 --> 00:29:54,373
and put everything I have left
into this strike!

502
00:29:55,029 --> 00:29:58,839
Insect Breathing,
Dance of the Centipede.

503
00:29:59,321 --> 00:30:00,459
[DOMA] Hmm?

504
00:30:00,678 --> 00:30:02,517
[SHINOBU]
Hundred-Legged Zigzag.

505
00:30:03,349 --> 00:30:05,232
[♪ dramatic music playing]

506
00:30:07,333 --> 00:30:08,472
[groans]

507
00:30:25,593 --> 00:30:28,439
[DOMA] It feels like
she's everywhere at once.

508
00:30:29,315 --> 00:30:31,811
Just her movement
destroyed the bridge.

509
00:30:32,643 --> 00:30:34,438
[squeaking]

510
00:30:34,657 --> 00:30:36,802
So fast. I can't follow her.

511
00:30:37,678 --> 00:30:38,904
[impact grunts]

512
00:30:43,195 --> 00:30:44,246
From below?

513
00:30:44,465 --> 00:30:45,516
[gasps]

514
00:30:48,362 --> 00:30:50,508
[Shinobu grunts]

515
00:30:53,529 --> 00:30:56,638
- [glass shatters]
- [♪ music swells, fades]

516
00:30:58,301 --> 00:30:59,965
[SHINOBU]
Back when I was a child...

517
00:31:01,497 --> 00:31:03,512
...I thought of happiness
like a road,

518
00:31:03,688 --> 00:31:06,052
one that stretched on
into the distance

519
00:31:06,270 --> 00:31:08,197
with no end in sight.

520
00:31:08,416 --> 00:31:09,818
[laughter]

521
00:31:10,036 --> 00:31:11,218
[blood splatters]

522
00:31:11,875 --> 00:31:14,546
It wasn't until it was destroyed

523
00:31:14,721 --> 00:31:16,692
that I finally realized

524
00:31:16,911 --> 00:31:20,721
the road beneath my feet
was but a thin sheet of glass.

525
00:31:20,939 --> 00:31:23,173
♪

526
00:31:23,391 --> 00:31:27,814
However, some haven't had
the glass broken yet.

527
00:31:28,689 --> 00:31:33,199
All I wanted after being saved
was to become stronger...

528
00:31:34,206 --> 00:31:38,410
...so that some day,
I could protect those people.

529
00:31:39,856 --> 00:31:43,708
So... we made a promise.

530
00:31:45,898 --> 00:31:51,459
To vanquish the demons
as many as we could, together.

531
00:31:52,116 --> 00:31:53,736
[♪ poignant music playing]

532
00:31:54,611 --> 00:31:57,501
In hopes that the pain
we suffered

533
00:31:57,720 --> 00:32:00,128
would never be felt by another.

534
00:32:08,755 --> 00:32:09,915
Even if I'm weak...

535
00:32:14,204 --> 00:32:16,085
...even if I can't
decapitate demons,

536
00:32:16,324 --> 00:32:18,627
if I can take down just one,

537
00:32:18,867 --> 00:32:21,170
I can save dozens of lives.

538
00:32:21,362 --> 00:32:23,474
And if that demon's
an Upper Rank,

539
00:32:24,241 --> 00:32:26,737
it could mean saving hundreds.

540
00:32:28,464 --> 00:32:30,024
It's not a matter
of can or cannot.

541
00:32:30,707 --> 00:32:33,700
This is something I have to do.

542
00:32:39,954 --> 00:32:40,954
Are you angry?

543
00:32:42,700 --> 00:32:45,803
[SHINOBU] Yes.
I am angry, Tanjiro.

544
00:32:45,997 --> 00:32:47,083
I'm furious.

545
00:32:47,743 --> 00:32:48,790
In fact...

546
00:32:49,644 --> 00:32:54,444
...I'm always angry.

547
00:32:54,679 --> 00:32:56,472
How could I not be?

548
00:32:58,974 --> 00:32:59,974
My parents were killed.

549
00:33:01,204 --> 00:33:02,564
My older sister was killed.

550
00:33:03,534 --> 00:33:06,950
My Tsuguko, other than Kanao,
were killed.

551
00:33:07,920 --> 00:33:09,691
And those poor girls.

552
00:33:10,366 --> 00:33:11,969
If it weren't for the demons...

553
00:33:12,475 --> 00:33:15,301
If it weren't for the demons
that killed their loved ones,

554
00:33:15,934 --> 00:33:18,934
they'd be living happily
with their families.

555
00:33:20,604 --> 00:33:21,734
[♪ discordant music playing]

556
00:33:21,979 --> 00:33:25,369
It's all so infuriating!

557
00:33:25,615 --> 00:33:28,120
Stop messing with me, damn it!

558
00:33:29,005 --> 00:33:33,279
Why the hell isn't my poison
working on this prick?

559
00:33:34,164 --> 00:33:35,164
You bastard!

560
00:33:35,340 --> 00:33:36,568
[exhales]

561
00:33:36,788 --> 00:33:38,719
[ice crackling]

562
00:33:46,442 --> 00:33:49,118
I'm moved! You did your best!

563
00:33:49,338 --> 00:33:51,401
Even though you're so weak.

564
00:33:51,620 --> 00:33:53,595
You must have worked
so incredibly hard

565
00:33:53,814 --> 00:33:55,701
to get to this point. [sobbing]

566
00:33:55,920 --> 00:33:57,895
You're weaker than your sister,

567
00:33:58,114 --> 00:34:00,440
and yet, you somehow
outlived her.

568
00:34:00,923 --> 00:34:04,039
[sniffles] It's a miracle
you survived this long.

569
00:34:04,258 --> 00:34:05,258
[body cracking]

570
00:34:05,442 --> 00:34:06,671
[coughs]

571
00:34:06,891 --> 00:34:08,076
Even when hope is gone,

572
00:34:08,295 --> 00:34:10,577
humans always fight
to the bitter end.

573
00:34:11,104 --> 00:34:13,035
Humans are so foolish.

574
00:34:13,253 --> 00:34:15,712
But that's what makes them
so beautiful.

575
00:34:16,633 --> 00:34:19,266
I deem you worthy
of becoming part of me.

576
00:34:19,749 --> 00:34:23,128
[sobbing] You and I
shall share eternity!

577
00:34:26,243 --> 00:34:28,217
Do you have any last words?

578
00:34:28,788 --> 00:34:30,060
I'm listening.

579
00:34:34,888 --> 00:34:37,784
Rot in hell, you bastard!

580
00:34:41,821 --> 00:34:44,103
[exclaims in horror] Master!

581
00:34:47,131 --> 00:34:48,579
[bones crunching]

582
00:34:49,412 --> 00:34:52,397
[exclaims in anguish]

583
00:34:52,616 --> 00:34:54,591
[bones crunching]

584
00:35:00,251 --> 00:35:01,656
[clangs]

585
00:35:04,552 --> 00:35:06,132
[clatters]

586
00:35:06,878 --> 00:35:08,501
[quivering]

587
00:35:09,335 --> 00:35:12,320
[screaming in agony]

588
00:35:13,065 --> 00:35:15,083
♪

589
00:35:16,093 --> 00:35:18,814
[ZENITSU] I can't shake
the feeling he's here.

590
00:35:19,033 --> 00:35:20,306
He must be.

591
00:35:20,700 --> 00:35:23,290
He's got a score to settle
with me, too.

592
00:35:30,662 --> 00:35:32,066
The people we love,

593
00:35:32,286 --> 00:35:35,577
the people we hold dear
are so precious.

594
00:35:36,060 --> 00:35:38,649
We take for granted
that they'll always be there.

595
00:35:39,131 --> 00:35:43,125
However, that's just
a selfish delusion.

596
00:35:43,344 --> 00:35:44,404
Flower Breathing...

597
00:35:44,887 --> 00:35:47,041
[ZENITSU] Because the thought
of living without them

598
00:35:47,260 --> 00:35:49,018
is simply unbearable.

599
00:35:49,238 --> 00:35:50,336
...Fourth Form:

600
00:35:50,996 --> 00:35:53,236
Crimson Hanagoromo!

601
00:35:53,456 --> 00:35:55,082
[shatters]

602
00:35:56,268 --> 00:35:57,367
[grunts]

603
00:36:00,004 --> 00:36:03,607
[DOMA] Wow!
You nearly got me there.

604
00:36:06,683 --> 00:36:09,495
[ZENITSU] "They'll always be
alive and close by."

605
00:36:10,638 --> 00:36:13,319
It's a naive thought, I know,

606
00:36:13,934 --> 00:36:15,955
but we all wanna believe it.

607
00:36:19,075 --> 00:36:22,503
Would you mind holding off
your attacks for just a second?

608
00:36:22,722 --> 00:36:25,623
- I'm trying to absorb her.
- [flesh squelching]

609
00:36:28,435 --> 00:36:30,588
[seething]

610
00:36:33,137 --> 00:36:34,631
[DOMA] How strange.

611
00:36:34,850 --> 00:36:37,355
You're not taking the bait,
are you?

612
00:36:38,058 --> 00:36:40,124
What she did earlier,

613
00:36:40,344 --> 00:36:42,760
that motion she made
with her fingers.

614
00:36:43,244 --> 00:36:46,231
Was that her warning you
of my powers?

615
00:36:46,715 --> 00:36:49,571
I'm impressed she thought
to do that so quickly.

616
00:36:50,055 --> 00:36:51,813
Good job you did it.

617
00:36:52,383 --> 00:36:54,273
Too bad it doesn't matter.

618
00:36:54,757 --> 00:36:56,778
- [flesh squelching]
- [clatters]

619
00:36:56,998 --> 00:37:00,030
Well, in case
you were wondering,

620
00:37:00,558 --> 00:37:03,765
your master was tastier
than I imagined.

621
00:37:03,985 --> 00:37:05,083
[slurps]

622
00:37:05,611 --> 00:37:07,412
And now, you're here.

623
00:37:07,633 --> 00:37:10,884
It's just one feast
after another, it seems.

624
00:37:11,675 --> 00:37:14,839
Ah, this truly is...

625
00:37:15,454 --> 00:37:16,454
a wonderful night.

626
00:37:17,078 --> 00:37:20,336
[seething]

627
00:37:30,154 --> 00:37:31,538
You can't hide.

628
00:37:32,118 --> 00:37:33,501
Come out.

629
00:37:34,349 --> 00:37:36,804
Have some dignity and face me.

630
00:37:39,393 --> 00:37:42,338
[DEMON] Sounds like someone
ought to teach you some manners.

631
00:37:42,561 --> 00:37:44,703
Did you forget
that I'm your senior?

632
00:37:45,284 --> 00:37:48,853
You look a little stronger
than the last time I saw ya.

633
00:37:49,568 --> 00:37:53,629
It's too bad you still reek
of being a pathetic weakling.

634
00:37:56,307 --> 00:37:57,334
[clatters]

635
00:37:57,512 --> 00:37:58,761
UPPER SIX

636
00:37:58,985 --> 00:38:02,305
It's been a while,
hasn't it... Zenitsu?

637
00:38:02,524 --> 00:38:04,150
[chuckles]

638
00:38:05,115 --> 00:38:06,565
[ZENITSU] Kaigaku.

639
00:38:06,741 --> 00:38:08,981
You don't get my respect.

640
00:38:09,377 --> 00:38:10,914
You're a demon.

641
00:38:11,134 --> 00:38:12,847
You'll be treated as such.

642
00:38:20,710 --> 00:38:21,764
[Nakime plucking biwa strings]

643
00:38:21,940 --> 00:38:23,214
- [rumbles]
- [Tanjiro gasps]

644
00:38:23,434 --> 00:38:24,434
[grunts]

645
00:38:26,377 --> 00:38:28,924
Water Breathing, Ninth Form:

646
00:38:30,725 --> 00:38:33,098
Splashing Water Flow, Turbulent!

647
00:38:34,196 --> 00:38:35,558
[grunts]

648
00:38:35,777 --> 00:38:36,831
Stay focused!

649
00:38:37,051 --> 00:38:38,105
All right!

650
00:38:39,336 --> 00:38:41,444
This place is insane.

651
00:38:41,663 --> 00:38:44,124
The building keeps shifting
and rearranging itself

652
00:38:44,299 --> 00:38:45,837
as if it's alive.

653
00:38:46,056 --> 00:38:48,735
I can tell that
it's trying to separate us.

654
00:38:49,834 --> 00:38:52,513
We have to regroup
with the other Corps members

655
00:38:52,733 --> 00:38:54,973
and stay together
till we reach Muzan!

656
00:38:58,883 --> 00:39:00,816
[cawing]

657
00:39:01,255 --> 00:39:02,968
[cawing]

658
00:39:03,188 --> 00:39:04,637
Attention!

659
00:39:04,857 --> 00:39:06,921
Shinobu Kocho is dead!

660
00:39:07,580 --> 00:39:10,040
She fought valiantly
against Upper Two

661
00:39:10,260 --> 00:39:11,797
but was defeated!

662
00:39:19,090 --> 00:39:21,682
- [gasps]
- [muted silence]

663
00:39:24,801 --> 00:39:26,997
[♪ poignant music playing]

664
00:39:28,402 --> 00:39:30,555
[inaudible laughter]

665
00:39:43,777 --> 00:39:45,622
[seething]

666
00:39:49,224 --> 00:39:51,157
[cawing]

667
00:39:53,441 --> 00:39:54,847
[GIYU] Strange.

668
00:39:55,023 --> 00:39:57,350
There's a piece of paper
wrapped around its neck.

669
00:39:57,878 --> 00:39:59,722
How are the crows already here?

670
00:40:00,732 --> 00:40:03,544
[♪ epic dramatic music playing]

671
00:40:04,204 --> 00:40:05,204
Shinobu is dead,

672
00:40:05,420 --> 00:40:07,324
but we must push forward.

673
00:40:07,712 --> 00:40:10,265
Think only of what must be done
for victory.

674
00:40:10,784 --> 00:40:11,909
[KUINA, KANATA] Right.

675
00:40:14,158 --> 00:40:15,543
And what about the others?

676
00:40:15,758 --> 00:40:17,965
I need reports
on their whereabouts.

677
00:40:19,436 --> 00:40:21,123
[KANATA]
Center of the 40th vertical

678
00:40:21,340 --> 00:40:23,026
and 12th horizontal levels.

679
00:40:23,199 --> 00:40:24,670
[fight grunts]

680
00:40:24,886 --> 00:40:26,660
The Corps members
are fighting off

681
00:40:26,876 --> 00:40:29,601
what appears to be
at least ten demons.

682
00:40:31,376 --> 00:40:34,706
[fight grunts]

683
00:40:36,437 --> 00:40:39,422
However, more than 30 demons
are moving in their direction

684
00:40:39,638 --> 00:40:40,936
from behind the walls.

685
00:40:47,078 --> 00:40:49,112
[KIRIYA]
Using Mr. Yushiro's eyes,

686
00:40:49,328 --> 00:40:51,664
we're able to see
Blood Demon Arts,

687
00:40:51,880 --> 00:40:54,909
something that isn't possible
to do with the human eye.

688
00:40:55,816 --> 00:40:57,980
Each red light
is a Blood Demon Art.

689
00:40:58,196 --> 00:41:01,311
The more intense they glow,
the more potent their power.

690
00:41:02,176 --> 00:41:04,815
In this place, the entire area,

691
00:41:04,988 --> 00:41:08,103
buildings and all, must also be
a Blood Demon Art.

692
00:41:08,838 --> 00:41:11,823
There's seemingly
no end in sight to it.

693
00:41:14,246 --> 00:41:16,235
What incredible power!

694
00:41:17,576 --> 00:41:19,047
A demon labyrinth

695
00:41:19,263 --> 00:41:21,773
with the ability
to branch out endlessly.

696
00:41:24,801 --> 00:41:26,617
And here we lie at its center,

697
00:41:26,790 --> 00:41:29,516
trapped within the walls
of this infinite castle.

698
00:41:30,208 --> 00:41:31,852
[KAKUSHI 1] This one's finished.

699
00:41:33,669 --> 00:41:36,999
[KIRIYA] However, it's not as if
we've been caught off guard.

700
00:41:37,216 --> 00:41:38,643
KAKUSHI

701
00:41:38,644 --> 00:41:41,864
My father prepared
for this day meticulously.

702
00:41:42,504 --> 00:41:44,388
With Gyomei's cooperation,

703
00:41:44,575 --> 00:41:46,158
he had the Hashira
within arm's reach

704
00:41:46,346 --> 00:41:47,589
to mobilize at any time.

705
00:41:47,778 --> 00:41:50,113
To prevent the Corps members
from being isolated,

706
00:41:50,302 --> 00:41:52,525
he sent the Kasugai Crows
to gather them into groups

707
00:41:52,713 --> 00:41:54,031
and waited.

708
00:41:54,370 --> 00:41:57,497
He enlisted the aid
of Ms. Tamayo and Mr. Yushiro.

709
00:41:57,648 --> 00:41:58,778
And finally,

710
00:41:59,117 --> 00:42:01,114
to ensure that
their plan would succeed,

711
00:42:01,528 --> 00:42:03,750
my sisters and our parents

712
00:42:04,202 --> 00:42:06,274
readily sacrificed their lives.

713
00:42:08,949 --> 00:42:10,267
We cannot lose,

714
00:42:10,720 --> 00:42:12,076
no matter what!

715
00:42:14,750 --> 00:42:17,011
[♪ music intensifies]

716
00:42:17,576 --> 00:42:19,158
Amongst the Blood Demon Arts,

717
00:42:19,309 --> 00:42:21,984
there are five traces of power
that tower over the rest

718
00:42:22,172 --> 00:42:23,754
as if flaunting their strength.

719
00:42:24,319 --> 00:42:26,353
These must be Upper Ranks.

720
00:42:26,994 --> 00:42:28,312
One of them is at the same spot

721
00:42:28,501 --> 00:42:30,346
where Shinobu
was last seen fighting.

722
00:42:30,836 --> 00:42:32,117
Found another!

723
00:42:32,306 --> 00:42:34,716
Upper Six and Zenitsu have just
encountered each other!

724
00:42:34,905 --> 00:42:36,110
An Upper Rank!

725
00:42:36,299 --> 00:42:37,427
Is he alone?

726
00:42:37,428 --> 00:42:39,388
[KUINA] He is.
It looks to be a one-on-one!

727
00:42:39,576 --> 00:42:41,912
[KIRIYA] A Hinoe can't beat
an Upper Rank by themself.

728
00:42:42,100 --> 00:42:43,100
Send backup!

729
00:42:47,825 --> 00:42:48,881
[KAIGAKU] Hmm.

730
00:42:49,069 --> 00:42:50,727
What, you're frozen in fear?

731
00:42:50,915 --> 00:42:52,572
Guess some things never change.

732
00:42:52,761 --> 00:42:54,569
Once a coward, always a coward.

733
00:42:55,436 --> 00:42:57,206
Did you ever become a Hashira?

734
00:42:57,394 --> 00:42:59,014
[scoffs] Guess not.

735
00:42:59,165 --> 00:43:00,408
That's too bad.

736
00:43:00,596 --> 00:43:04,213
Got any new techniques?
Or still just First Form?

737
00:43:05,117 --> 00:43:06,511
For an Upper Rank bottom feeder

738
00:43:06,699 --> 00:43:08,394
who's nothing more
than a spare blade,

739
00:43:08,583 --> 00:43:10,391
you're sure acting
awfully proud.

740
00:43:11,144 --> 00:43:13,593
[Kaigaku sarcastically]
Wow! [laughs]

741
00:43:13,781 --> 00:43:16,343
Who taught you to talk
like that? New friends?

742
00:43:16,757 --> 00:43:18,791
[ZENITSU] Why the hell
did you become a demon?

743
00:43:19,206 --> 00:43:21,089
[laughs] You'd never understand.

744
00:43:21,278 --> 00:43:23,312
You were supposed to succeed
Thunder Breathing!

745
00:43:23,463 --> 00:43:24,593
But you tarnished it!

746
00:43:25,874 --> 00:43:26,874
Huh?

747
00:43:27,073 --> 00:43:29,468
[ZENITSU]
After you became a demon,

748
00:43:29,718 --> 00:43:30,914
he...

749
00:43:32,810 --> 00:43:34,806
He committed seppuku!

750
00:43:35,355 --> 00:43:36,802
[♪ poignant music playing]

751
00:43:37,051 --> 00:43:38,399
[voice breaking] Even worse,

752
00:43:39,047 --> 00:43:40,993
he did it by himself.

753
00:43:42,389 --> 00:43:44,735
He was all alone!

754
00:43:46,131 --> 00:43:48,078
Because of that,
no one was there

755
00:43:48,326 --> 00:43:49,974
to put him out of his misery.

756
00:43:50,223 --> 00:43:53,715
He bled out
and died a painful death.

757
00:43:53,964 --> 00:43:55,811
It's your fault!

758
00:43:56,060 --> 00:43:59,502
Gramps died the most
agonizing death possible

759
00:43:59,752 --> 00:44:01,997
all because
the Thunder Breathing rights

760
00:44:02,247 --> 00:44:03,394
produced a demon!

761
00:44:05,340 --> 00:44:07,834
Why the hell should I care?

762
00:44:08,334 --> 00:44:11,128
Gramps died? So what?

763
00:44:11,376 --> 00:44:12,824
Want me to cry?

764
00:44:13,024 --> 00:44:15,718
Did you expect me
to give it to him?

765
00:44:15,966 --> 00:44:17,812
Well, I don't.

766
00:44:17,813 --> 00:44:21,305
In fact, I don't care for anyone
who doesn't appreciate me.

767
00:44:21,555 --> 00:44:23,451
No matter what,

768
00:44:23,700 --> 00:44:25,596
this is who I am.

769
00:44:25,846 --> 00:44:29,188
Take the side
of whoever knows my worth.

770
00:44:29,437 --> 00:44:30,835
[laughs]

771
00:44:31,632 --> 00:44:34,277
If the old geezer
really did die in agony,

772
00:44:34,526 --> 00:44:36,273
then I couldn't be happier.

773
00:44:36,522 --> 00:44:39,964
I slaved away
for that ungrateful bastard.

774
00:44:40,214 --> 00:44:42,609
And what does he do to repay me?

775
00:44:42,808 --> 00:44:44,754
He makes you my co-successor

776
00:44:44,954 --> 00:44:47,099
instead of just letting me
carry the torch!

777
00:44:47,299 --> 00:44:48,895
I hope he rots!

778
00:44:49,544 --> 00:44:51,939
Former Hashira or not,

779
00:44:52,188 --> 00:44:55,930
I would never shed a tear
over some senile geezer.

780
00:44:56,179 --> 00:44:59,173
[laughs boorishly]

781
00:45:01,866 --> 00:45:04,910
[ZENITSU] Gramps knew
exactly what he was doing.

782
00:45:05,508 --> 00:45:09,152
We were made co-successors
because we're weak.

783
00:45:09,400 --> 00:45:11,895
I was only able to use
the First Form

784
00:45:12,145 --> 00:45:15,188
while you could use
everything but First Form.

785
00:45:15,937 --> 00:45:18,232
I can't help
but feel sorry for Gramps

786
00:45:18,481 --> 00:45:21,075
that he has two
useless successors!

787
00:45:21,325 --> 00:45:23,221
[KAIGAKU]
Don't lump us together!

788
00:45:23,470 --> 00:45:25,665
I'm nothing like you!

789
00:45:26,264 --> 00:45:31,154
Thunder Breathing, Fourth Form:
Distant Thunder!

790
00:45:31,402 --> 00:45:33,697
[♪ intense dramatic music
playing]

791
00:45:35,195 --> 00:45:36,741
[gasps]

792
00:45:40,035 --> 00:45:41,695
You're so slow, scum.

793
00:45:41,914 --> 00:45:44,245
- [groans]
- [blood splatters]

794
00:45:47,368 --> 00:45:50,094
[KAIGAKU]
What the hell? He got me.

795
00:45:50,315 --> 00:45:51,766
His speed is unreal.

796
00:45:51,986 --> 00:45:54,405
He never moved like that.

797
00:45:54,581 --> 00:45:56,164
He's changed.

798
00:45:57,704 --> 00:46:00,035
But he's not the only one.

799
00:46:03,993 --> 00:46:06,149
[wet squelching]

800
00:46:10,635 --> 00:46:13,890
There's no shame in kneeling
down before the powerful

801
00:46:14,109 --> 00:46:15,472
if it means surviving.

802
00:46:15,956 --> 00:46:17,848
As long as you're alive,

803
00:46:18,067 --> 00:46:19,739
you can still win.

804
00:46:21,102 --> 00:46:24,313
Only once you die have you lost.

805
00:46:24,840 --> 00:46:28,140
Even if you have to beg
on your hands and knees.

806
00:46:28,711 --> 00:46:32,010
Even if you're without a home
and have to drink from a puddle.

807
00:46:32,494 --> 00:46:35,014
Even if they condemn you
for stealing money.

808
00:46:36,051 --> 00:46:37,405
As long as you're alive,

809
00:46:37,631 --> 00:46:39,931
there's still a future
where you can win.

810
00:46:40,428 --> 00:46:44,219
Believing that
is all that's kept me going.

811
00:46:46,249 --> 00:46:48,731
[KOKUSHIBO]
Forfeit your humanity

812
00:46:48,957 --> 00:46:52,477
and limitless power
will be within reach.

813
00:46:52,973 --> 00:46:56,267
Should my Lord
choose to acknowledge you,

814
00:46:56,493 --> 00:46:59,878
demon blood
shall course through your veins.

815
00:47:01,728 --> 00:47:03,082
[Kaigaku quivers]

816
00:47:03,804 --> 00:47:05,588
The stronger the swordsman,

817
00:47:05,795 --> 00:47:08,784
the longer it takes for him
to become a demon.

818
00:47:09,574 --> 00:47:13,265
It took me three days
to fully transform.

819
00:47:13,792 --> 00:47:16,648
Turning a breathing technique
user into a demon

820
00:47:16,868 --> 00:47:18,406
is no small feat.

821
00:47:18,626 --> 00:47:20,251
Doing such a thing will require

822
00:47:20,471 --> 00:47:23,152
an exorbitant amount
of my Lord's blood.

823
00:47:23,942 --> 00:47:25,919
And though it is rare,

824
00:47:26,096 --> 00:47:27,852
some people,
for whatever reason,

825
00:47:28,029 --> 00:47:30,401
are physically incapable
of becoming demons.

826
00:47:30,620 --> 00:47:32,027
Huh?

827
00:47:32,202 --> 00:47:35,103
[KOKUSHIBO] I'm curious to see
how you will fare.

828
00:47:35,279 --> 00:47:36,816
UPPER ONE

829
00:47:37,300 --> 00:47:38,486
[quivers]

830
00:47:38,705 --> 00:47:41,210
You must appreciate this blood.

831
00:47:41,430 --> 00:47:46,395
Even holding it as you are now
is an honor you cannot fathom.

832
00:47:46,614 --> 00:47:48,811
Should you spill a single drop,

833
00:47:49,031 --> 00:47:51,887
I'll have you dismembered
in an instant

834
00:47:52,106 --> 00:47:54,172
before it touches the ground.

835
00:47:54,347 --> 00:47:55,578
[gasps in horror]

836
00:47:56,325 --> 00:47:57,951
[breathing shakily]

837
00:47:59,445 --> 00:48:03,794
[KAIGAKU] Even now,
I remember the terror I felt.

838
00:48:04,014 --> 00:48:07,924
Like every cell in my body
was screaming in anguish.

839
00:48:10,517 --> 00:48:12,801
Compared to what I felt then,

840
00:48:13,021 --> 00:48:14,427
this is nothing.

841
00:48:14,603 --> 00:48:16,976
- He's just a punk.
- [clatters]

842
00:48:17,195 --> 00:48:18,513
He might be stronger,

843
00:48:18,689 --> 00:48:20,579
but he's not on par
with an Upper Rank.

844
00:48:21,501 --> 00:48:25,763
Zenitsu Agatsuma
is and always will be trash.

845
00:48:25,983 --> 00:48:27,741
He's a despicable crybaby

846
00:48:27,960 --> 00:48:30,333
without a shred of dignity
or valor!

847
00:48:30,553 --> 00:48:32,398
Somebody, help!

848
00:48:32,617 --> 00:48:36,967
I fell in a pitfall
and twisted my ankle!

849
00:48:37,670 --> 00:48:39,472
[KAIGAKU] The disrespect!

850
00:48:39,691 --> 00:48:43,251
As if I'd be co-successor
with that sniveling loser!

851
00:48:43,822 --> 00:48:45,755
[JIGORO] Here you are, Kaigaku.

852
00:48:46,283 --> 00:48:48,875
- [ZENITSU] Hey, Gramps?
- [KAIGAKU] Hmm?

853
00:48:49,051 --> 00:48:52,171
It looks a little big on me,
don't you think?

854
00:48:52,390 --> 00:48:54,499
- Maybe I'll grow into it...
- [KAIGAKU] I'm supposed to be

855
00:48:54,719 --> 00:48:57,091
- that idiot's equal?
- [both laughing]

856
00:48:58,234 --> 00:49:00,826
That's gotta be
some kind of sick joke!

857
00:49:01,002 --> 00:49:02,144
[seething]

858
00:49:02,671 --> 00:49:05,132
The old bastard deserved to die!

859
00:49:05,351 --> 00:49:07,460
And if you miss him so dearly,

860
00:49:07,681 --> 00:49:10,009
then I'll see to it
you join him!

861
00:49:11,284 --> 00:49:14,271
[ZENITSU] I was only ever able
to learn the First Form.

862
00:49:14,491 --> 00:49:18,182
However, you were able to learn
everything but the First Form.

863
00:49:19,412 --> 00:49:20,861
[♪ tender music playing]

864
00:49:21,082 --> 00:49:22,312
Gramps knew that.

865
00:49:22,707 --> 00:49:25,783
His solution
was having us both succeed

866
00:49:26,002 --> 00:49:27,584
the Thunder Breathing technique.

867
00:49:30,220 --> 00:49:31,934
But you denied him that.

868
00:49:32,549 --> 00:49:34,922
You became a demon

869
00:49:35,142 --> 00:49:36,987
purely to reject him.

870
00:49:37,954 --> 00:49:38,954
- [crackling]
- It's coming!

871
00:49:39,133 --> 00:49:41,895
Thunder Breathing, Second Form:

872
00:49:42,474 --> 00:49:43,899
Rice Spirit!

873
00:49:44,122 --> 00:49:46,083
[♪ dramatic synth music playing]

874
00:49:46,306 --> 00:49:48,934
[ZENITSU] He attacked five times
in one breath.

875
00:49:49,558 --> 00:49:51,875
- [Kaigaku yells]
- [effort grunts, strains]

876
00:49:52,097 --> 00:49:53,879
How many people
have you devoured?

877
00:49:54,102 --> 00:49:57,087
You can't even tell right
from wrong anymore!

878
00:49:57,310 --> 00:50:00,206
I'm more aware of those
than I've ever been!

879
00:50:01,454 --> 00:50:02,453
What's the matter?

880
00:50:02,454 --> 00:50:05,429
Aren't you supposed to be
the old geezer's favorite?

881
00:50:05,931 --> 00:50:07,440
- [grunts]
- If you are,

882
00:50:07,650 --> 00:50:09,535
then show me
what he passed down to you!

883
00:50:09,745 --> 00:50:12,930
It's the only technique
you've got, so use it!

884
00:50:13,139 --> 00:50:14,186
[Zenitsu grunts]

885
00:50:15,444 --> 00:50:18,419
Go all out.
Use everything you got.

886
00:50:18,586 --> 00:50:20,263
- [groans angrily]
- And don't you dare hold back

887
00:50:20,473 --> 00:50:22,525
- for a second!
- [determined grunt]

888
00:50:27,177 --> 00:50:28,685
[ZENITSU] Thunder Breathing...

889
00:50:30,989 --> 00:50:32,331
...First Form...

890
00:50:32,708 --> 00:50:33,708
[scoffs]

891
00:50:34,217 --> 00:50:36,061
...Thunderclap and Flash.

892
00:50:38,826 --> 00:50:40,251
[effort grunts]

893
00:50:40,460 --> 00:50:41,801
[laughs boisterously]

894
00:50:42,011 --> 00:50:45,070
As if a basic attack
like charging me head-on

895
00:50:45,278 --> 00:50:46,746
would ever find its mark.

896
00:50:46,955 --> 00:50:48,463
Don't make me laugh!

897
00:50:50,224 --> 00:50:53,664
Thunder Breathing,

898
00:50:53,881 --> 00:50:57,059
Third Form: Thunder Swarm!

899
00:50:59,236 --> 00:51:01,282
[grunting]

900
00:51:02,545 --> 00:51:04,983
[ZENITSU] He's attacking me
from every angle at once.

901
00:51:05,158 --> 00:51:06,420
[KAIGAKU] What's the matter?

902
00:51:06,637 --> 00:51:08,684
Don't tell me
you're done already!

903
00:51:09,902 --> 00:51:11,688
[ZENITSU]
Thunder Breathing, First Form:

904
00:51:11,905 --> 00:51:14,344
Thunderclap and Flash:
Eight Fold!

905
00:51:18,827 --> 00:51:21,396
- That's not gonna work!
- [Zenitsu grunts]

906
00:51:21,918 --> 00:51:25,054
Thunder Breathing, Fifth Form:

907
00:51:27,404 --> 00:51:28,972
Heat Lightning!

908
00:51:29,451 --> 00:51:31,932
- Ah!
- Gotcha!

909
00:51:32,585 --> 00:51:36,112
How does the bite of my Blood
Demon Art-enhanced sword feel?

910
00:51:36,287 --> 00:51:38,942
- [electricity crackling]
- Each strike on contact

911
00:51:39,160 --> 00:51:41,597
leaves a wound
that burns your skin.

912
00:51:42,208 --> 00:51:45,821
This proves those who recognize
my talents and value are right!

913
00:51:46,343 --> 00:51:49,608
And those that dismiss
or condemn me are wrong!

914
00:51:50,175 --> 00:51:53,215
Do you get it now?
This is the power I have!

915
00:51:53,711 --> 00:51:55,964
My power as a demon that is!

916
00:51:56,459 --> 00:51:58,714
All you know how to do
is use First Form,

917
00:51:58,939 --> 00:52:01,915
yet that geezer chose
to make you his successor!

918
00:52:02,139 --> 00:52:04,799
And, boy,
what a mistake that was!

919
00:52:11,290 --> 00:52:12,687
So, that's it.

920
00:52:12,913 --> 00:52:15,527
This is the path
that you've chosen to take.

921
00:52:17,105 --> 00:52:18,480
[weakly] I already knew.

922
00:52:19,109 --> 00:52:20,445
I knew, but...

923
00:52:22,352 --> 00:52:23,999
[sword scraping]

924
00:52:25,602 --> 00:52:28,549
With this strike, I'll end this.

925
00:52:28,766 --> 00:52:30,022
You're finished!

926
00:52:30,239 --> 00:52:31,756
- [crackling]
- Thunder Breathing...

927
00:52:31,973 --> 00:52:35,526
- [rumbling]
- ...Sixth Form:

928
00:52:38,603 --> 00:52:41,898
- [crackling]
- [♪ music intensifies]

929
00:52:42,938 --> 00:52:45,581
Rumble and Flash!

930
00:52:45,798 --> 00:52:49,526
That strike I landed will keep
crackling through your flesh!

931
00:52:49,742 --> 00:52:53,513
This is the power that I gained
by becoming a demon.

932
00:52:53,729 --> 00:52:55,073
Get it now?

933
00:52:55,289 --> 00:52:57,630
I've long surpassed
Thunder Breathing!

934
00:52:59,407 --> 00:53:01,574
[laughs boisterously]

935
00:53:01,790 --> 00:53:03,308
You and I aren't equals.

936
00:53:03,524 --> 00:53:04,738
And we never have been.

937
00:53:05,258 --> 00:53:06,991
I'm better than all of you.

938
00:53:07,988 --> 00:53:09,332
Guess the old bastard

939
00:53:09,549 --> 00:53:11,412
shouldn't have put
his trust in you after all.

940
00:53:11,629 --> 00:53:14,229
[laughs boisterously]

941
00:53:15,920 --> 00:53:18,433
[JIGORO] Come on,
be more like Kaigaku!

942
00:53:18,910 --> 00:53:22,507
He's your senior,
so follow his example, you hear?

943
00:53:22,723 --> 00:53:24,761
Hang on. Isn't the First Form

944
00:53:24,934 --> 00:53:27,361
pretty much the entire basis
of Thunder Breathing?

945
00:53:27,578 --> 00:53:29,962
Yeah, and it's the only one
he can't do.

946
00:53:30,178 --> 00:53:32,259
You know what that means,
don't ya?

947
00:53:32,476 --> 00:53:34,599
That even though
he's mastered other forms,

948
00:53:34,773 --> 00:53:36,116
he's still a weakling.

949
00:53:36,332 --> 00:53:37,849
Yep, exactly.

950
00:53:37,850 --> 00:53:40,190
The way he shows off, though?
He's got such an ego.

951
00:53:40,406 --> 00:53:42,748
[BOY 1] No way
he becomes a Hashira.

952
00:53:42,964 --> 00:53:44,871
[BOY 2] Yeah,
he'll die before then.

953
00:53:45,088 --> 00:53:46,088
[♪ gentle music playing]

954
00:53:46,214 --> 00:53:48,121
What did I do to deserve that?

955
00:53:49,595 --> 00:53:52,455
I heard you went and punched
someone from a higher rank.

956
00:53:52,889 --> 00:53:55,793
Don't go around making trouble,
you trash!

957
00:53:56,009 --> 00:53:59,390
It's embarrassing even being
seen in the same room as you.

958
00:54:01,903 --> 00:54:05,154
[ZENITSU] I was fully aware
that you hated me, Kaigaku.

959
00:54:05,371 --> 00:54:08,968
And to be perfectly honest,
I hated you, too.

960
00:54:10,095 --> 00:54:14,082
Even so, I couldn't help
but respect you as well.

961
00:54:14,602 --> 00:54:17,723
You never stopped
working towards your goals.

962
00:54:18,589 --> 00:54:20,627
Despite our differences,

963
00:54:20,800 --> 00:54:23,054
I looked up to you
as an example.

964
00:54:23,573 --> 00:54:25,957
You really were a special guy.

965
00:54:27,561 --> 00:54:29,251
It wasn't just me.

966
00:54:29,468 --> 00:54:31,765
Gramps thought
you were remarkable, too.

967
00:54:32,762 --> 00:54:36,315
But I guess you weren't
satisfied with that, were you?

968
00:54:37,009 --> 00:54:38,656
No matter the day,

969
00:54:38,872 --> 00:54:42,730
the only sound that came
from you was discontent.

970
00:54:42,946 --> 00:54:44,332
[soft tinkling]

971
00:54:44,333 --> 00:54:46,977
It was like the box
where you kept your joy

972
00:54:47,194 --> 00:54:48,815
had a hole in it.

973
00:54:50,496 --> 00:54:53,176
And that joy kept leaking out.

974
00:54:54,675 --> 00:54:56,764
If the hole isn't mended,

975
00:54:57,264 --> 00:54:59,989
happiness will always be
out of reach.

976
00:55:02,488 --> 00:55:05,804
Gramps,
I'm sorry we're fighting...

977
00:55:06,803 --> 00:55:08,302
...but he and I

978
00:55:08,938 --> 00:55:11,482
must walk separate paths.

979
00:55:17,886 --> 00:55:20,157
- [clangs]
- [crackling]

980
00:55:21,385 --> 00:55:22,385
[KAIGAKU] Huh?

981
00:55:22,882 --> 00:55:24,721
He's still holding on?

982
00:55:24,722 --> 00:55:25,722
[electricity crackling]

983
00:55:25,872 --> 00:55:28,095
[♪ synth music playing]

984
00:55:31,814 --> 00:55:32,849
[power surging]

985
00:55:33,040 --> 00:55:34,152
What the hell?

986
00:55:41,703 --> 00:55:42,738
[ZENITSU] Brother...

987
00:55:43,505 --> 00:55:44,865
- ...I'm sorry.
- [gasps]

988
00:55:45,500 --> 00:55:47,944
[♪ music intensifies]

989
00:56:06,028 --> 00:56:10,231
Thunder Breathing, Seventh Form:

990
00:56:10,426 --> 00:56:12,087
[roaring]

991
00:56:13,505 --> 00:56:14,585
God of Fire Thunder.

992
00:56:22,293 --> 00:56:23,928
[KAIGAKU] That...

993
00:56:24,255 --> 00:56:26,170
was so fast.

994
00:56:26,684 --> 00:56:29,254
That move. What was it?

995
00:56:29,628 --> 00:56:31,403
Unbelievable.

996
00:56:31,637 --> 00:56:34,533
How come I've never seen
that technique until now?

997
00:56:35,515 --> 00:56:37,035
Damn you. Damn you!

998
00:56:37,256 --> 00:56:40,301
I always knew that stupid geezer
liked you more than me!

999
00:56:40,521 --> 00:56:43,346
Why else would he only
teach you that technique?!

1000
00:56:43,566 --> 00:56:45,244
You're wrong.

1001
00:56:45,465 --> 00:56:46,465
[gasps]

1002
00:56:46,612 --> 00:56:48,023
[♪ gentle music playing]

1003
00:56:48,024 --> 00:56:49,922
[ZENITSU] Gramps was never
that kind of person.

1004
00:56:51,026 --> 00:56:53,674
This technique
is something I made.

1005
00:56:54,291 --> 00:56:57,381
I created it all by myself.

1006
00:56:58,308 --> 00:56:59,941
My hope was...

1007
00:57:00,647 --> 00:57:06,163
...that one day, I'd be able
to use it to fight by your side.

1008
00:57:09,298 --> 00:57:12,034
[KAIGAKU]
How is this even possible?

1009
00:57:12,563 --> 00:57:15,300
Thunder Breathing
only has six techniques,

1010
00:57:15,477 --> 00:57:18,345
and yet he was able
to create a seventh?

1011
00:57:19,095 --> 00:57:22,891
Him? The one who can only
use the First Form?

1012
00:57:24,215 --> 00:57:27,261
He's inferior to me
in every way!

1013
00:57:27,481 --> 00:57:28,673
[groans angrily]

1014
00:57:28,894 --> 00:57:33,674
I can't accept it.
I won't accept it!

1015
00:57:34,195 --> 00:57:40,575
This must be
some kind of twisted joke!

1016
00:57:41,099 --> 00:57:48,099
Someone like me losing to him?

1017
00:57:51,659 --> 00:57:57,936
I must be going insane!

1018
00:58:01,908 --> 00:58:04,628
Wait!

1019
00:58:06,930 --> 00:58:11,529
With his strength depleted,

1020
00:58:11,950 --> 00:58:17,282
I can still have the last laugh.

1021
00:58:17,805 --> 00:58:24,079
This fall will kill him
and he can't stop it.

1022
00:58:25,858 --> 00:58:32,858
I'll be taking him to hell
with me.[laughs maliciously]

1023
00:58:36,106 --> 00:58:39,975
[YUSHIRO]
Those who never give to others

1024
00:58:40,499 --> 00:58:45,833
are never able to receive
in return.

1025
00:58:46,355 --> 00:58:47,354
Huh?

1026
00:58:47,355 --> 00:58:48,144
People who have
nothing but desire

1027
00:58:48,145 --> 00:58:48,987
are no different than those
who have nothing at all.

1028
00:58:48,988 --> 00:58:49,988
And one cannot create anything
out of nothing.

1029
00:58:50,264 --> 00:58:51,264
Dying alone is pathetic,
wouldn't you say?

1030
00:58:52,717 --> 00:58:53,478
[screaming in anguish]

1031
00:58:53,479 --> 00:58:54,479
[fizzles out]

1032
00:58:56,239 --> 00:58:56,910
[gasps]

1033
00:58:56,911 --> 00:58:57,650
- [birds chirping]
- [leaves rustling]

1034
00:58:57,651 --> 00:58:58,058
Where am I?

1035
00:58:58,059 --> 00:58:59,059
- [stream trickling]
- [birds chirping]

1036
00:58:59,888 --> 00:59:00,520
[gasps]

1037
00:59:00,521 --> 00:59:01,056
Gramps!

1038
00:59:01,057 --> 00:59:01,745
[♪ tender music playing]

1039
00:59:01,746 --> 00:59:02,115
I'm sorry!

1040
00:59:02,116 --> 00:59:02,881
I... I couldn't get along
with Kaigaku!

1041
00:59:02,882 --> 00:59:03,774
I even tried
writing him letters, but...

1042
00:59:03,775 --> 00:59:04,565
But he never wrote me back.
And... [sobs]

1043
00:59:04,566 --> 00:59:04,999
...if it weren't for me,

1044
00:59:05,000 --> 00:59:05,714
he might not have ended up
the way he did.

1045
00:59:05,715 --> 00:59:06,755
I'm really sorry!

1046
00:59:06,756 --> 00:59:07,756
Forgive me!

1047
00:59:07,894 --> 00:59:11,956
I wasn't able to pay you back
for everything!

1048
00:59:12,208 --> 00:59:16,395
I really wanted you
to see me as a Hashira,

1049
00:59:16,647 --> 00:59:19,021
to make you proud.

1050
00:59:19,335 --> 00:59:20,335
I'm sorry.

1051
00:59:20,503 --> 00:59:21,747
I failed you, Gramps!

1052
00:59:23,999 --> 00:59:26,353
[sobbing] I understand
if you hate me now.

1053
00:59:26,824 --> 00:59:28,875
Please, just say something.
Anything!

1054
00:59:29,043 --> 00:59:30,043
[effort grunting]

1055
00:59:30,355 --> 00:59:33,335
Damn it! What's this
grabbing my leg?

1056
00:59:34,602 --> 00:59:36,656
Gramps! I just...

1057
00:59:36,875 --> 00:59:39,061
I need-- [grunts]

1058
00:59:40,503 --> 00:59:41,684
Damn it!

1059
00:59:41,903 --> 00:59:43,782
[effort grunting]

1060
00:59:44,001 --> 00:59:45,313
[JIGORO] Zenitsu.

1061
00:59:45,531 --> 00:59:46,531
[Zenitsu gasps softly]

1062
00:59:52,963 --> 00:59:56,897
Listen to me, lad.
You are my pride and joy.

1063
01:00:15,432 --> 01:00:17,006
[♪ music fades]

1064
01:00:20,153 --> 01:00:22,558
[MURATA] Well? Can you save him?

1065
01:00:22,777 --> 01:00:24,351
He's someone that I know.

1066
01:00:24,569 --> 01:00:27,410
I can't watch him die.
Please tell me there's a way!

1067
01:00:27,629 --> 01:00:29,728
Keep your voice down.
You're not helping.

1068
01:00:29,946 --> 01:00:32,438
Just watch out
for enemy ambushes.

1069
01:00:32,657 --> 01:00:34,886
At least then you'll actually be
doing something useful.

1070
01:00:35,105 --> 01:00:36,503
[grunting angrily]

1071
01:00:36,504 --> 01:00:39,301
Excuse me? And just
who the hell are you, huh?

1072
01:00:39,476 --> 01:00:41,924
I better not find out
you're a lower rank than I am!

1073
01:00:42,143 --> 01:00:45,596
I'm a demon. I don't care
about your hierarchy.

1074
01:00:46,427 --> 01:00:48,657
This'll slow
the Blood Demon Art.

1075
01:00:48,875 --> 01:00:50,580
But if these cracks
keep spreading,

1076
01:00:50,798 --> 01:00:53,115
it'll travel all the way
to his eyes.

1077
01:00:53,815 --> 01:00:55,215
Hey, can you hear me?

1078
01:00:55,695 --> 01:00:56,917
[groans]

1079
01:00:57,616 --> 01:00:59,362
[all three exclaim]

1080
01:00:59,537 --> 01:01:02,156
Your bedside manner
really sucks, you know that?

1081
01:01:02,375 --> 01:01:03,902
I'm also using a hemostatic,

1082
01:01:04,120 --> 01:01:05,823
but I still can't get
the bleeding to stop.

1083
01:01:06,041 --> 01:01:07,350
What did I say?!

1084
01:01:07,351 --> 01:01:09,228
Don't listen to him.
You're gonna be fine.

1085
01:01:09,404 --> 01:01:10,669
I swear
you'll pull through this!

1086
01:01:10,887 --> 01:01:12,066
Yeah, you can do it!

1087
01:01:12,284 --> 01:01:14,118
Fight on! Fight on!

1088
01:01:14,336 --> 01:01:16,126
The only reason
you're alive right now

1089
01:01:16,344 --> 01:01:17,698
is because
the Upper Rank you fought

1090
01:01:17,916 --> 01:01:20,099
still hadn't mastered
his own techniques.

1091
01:01:20,579 --> 01:01:22,544
That was lucky for you.

1092
01:01:23,111 --> 01:01:24,727
If you'd fought him
a year from now,

1093
01:01:24,945 --> 01:01:26,604
you would have died instantly.

1094
01:01:27,302 --> 01:01:28,482
[Murata groaning]

1095
01:01:28,699 --> 01:01:30,402
Could you stop
with the doom and gloom?

1096
01:01:30,577 --> 01:01:32,498
Consider his feelings!

1097
01:01:32,716 --> 01:01:35,990
[breathing heavily]

1098
01:01:39,090 --> 01:01:42,276
Hey, don't pretend like
I'm the one in the wrong here.

1099
01:01:44,197 --> 01:01:45,901
What? What are you pointing at?

1100
01:01:46,118 --> 01:01:48,520
[YUSHIRO] Your screaming let
the demons know we're here.

1101
01:01:48,694 --> 01:01:50,484
[all screaming]

1102
01:01:50,659 --> 01:01:52,013
Don't say I didn't warn you.

1103
01:01:52,230 --> 01:01:53,714
[snarling]

1104
01:01:53,715 --> 01:01:57,425
Hey, it was Yushiro, right?
Take care of Agatsuma!

1105
01:01:57,950 --> 01:01:59,740
- Charge!
- [all grunting]

1106
01:02:01,573 --> 01:02:04,586
Murata, please take care of them
quickly, okay?

1107
01:02:04,760 --> 01:02:06,768
I'm gonna give you
such an earful later!

1108
01:02:06,987 --> 01:02:09,083
- Damn.
- [demon snarling]

1109
01:02:09,781 --> 01:02:12,182
Water Breathing, Second Form:

1110
01:02:12,400 --> 01:02:15,325
Water Wheel! [yells]

1111
01:02:16,679 --> 01:02:18,163
We're gonna head them off.

1112
01:02:18,381 --> 01:02:19,779
Follow my lead, everyone!

1113
01:02:19,996 --> 01:02:22,049
[all yelling]

1114
01:02:22,266 --> 01:02:23,708
- [footsteps receding]
- [grunts]

1115
01:02:29,820 --> 01:02:32,003
[♪ foreboding music playing]

1116
01:02:36,761 --> 01:02:38,202
This is bad.

1117
01:02:38,420 --> 01:02:40,079
They're gonna run into "him."

1118
01:02:43,178 --> 01:02:45,493
[TANJIRO] We haven't encountered
any Upper Ranks.

1119
01:02:45,929 --> 01:02:48,418
Are we still that far
from Muzan?

1120
01:02:48,635 --> 01:02:50,643
I hope the others are all right.

1121
01:02:53,743 --> 01:02:55,228
Miss Shinobu...

1122
01:02:56,057 --> 01:02:58,240
we're going to win this battle.

1123
01:02:58,459 --> 01:03:01,035
For you. For everyone!

1124
01:03:02,213 --> 01:03:03,828
- [loud crash]
- [gasps]

1125
01:03:04,003 --> 01:03:05,881
That jolt! What was that?

1126
01:03:06,360 --> 01:03:07,583
Mr. Giyu!

1127
01:03:07,801 --> 01:03:08,801
Stay there!

1128
01:03:09,023 --> 01:03:10,901
- Keep calm.
- [grunts]

1129
01:03:12,255 --> 01:03:13,815
[TANJIRO]
Is someone else fighting?

1130
01:03:14,027 --> 01:03:15,940
Are we about to lose
another comrade?

1131
01:03:16,153 --> 01:03:18,703
- [♪ intriguing music playing]
- [loud thuds]

1132
01:03:21,721 --> 01:03:24,613
No, it's something else.

1133
01:03:24,825 --> 01:03:26,065
And it's coming this way.

1134
01:03:27,082 --> 01:03:28,187
[sniffs]

1135
01:03:28,674 --> 01:03:31,150
This... This scent.

1136
01:03:39,905 --> 01:03:42,249
[GIYU] Above us!
Get back, Tanjiro!

1137
01:03:43,133 --> 01:03:44,283
[grunts]

1138
01:03:46,406 --> 01:03:48,440
[DEMON] Long time no see.

1139
01:03:50,075 --> 01:03:52,950
It's commendable
you got this far.

1140
01:03:53,570 --> 01:03:56,089
Especially for a puny insect.

1141
01:03:56,311 --> 01:03:57,311
UPPER THREE

1142
01:03:57,726 --> 01:04:00,689
Don't you agree, Tanjiro?!

1143
01:04:00,866 --> 01:04:01,971
[Tanjiro seething]

1144
01:04:03,120 --> 01:04:05,906
Akaza!

1145
01:04:07,940 --> 01:04:10,550
[♪ low tense music playing]

1146
01:04:13,733 --> 01:04:15,281
[heavy burbling]

1147
01:04:32,040 --> 01:04:34,207
[breathing heavily]

1148
01:04:39,027 --> 01:04:41,813
[TAMAYO] This place...
If I had to guess,

1149
01:04:42,034 --> 01:04:44,024
this fleshy cocoon
is breaking down

1150
01:04:44,244 --> 01:04:45,395
and disposing the drug

1151
01:04:45,571 --> 01:04:48,446
that's rescinding
his demon form.

1152
01:04:49,065 --> 01:04:51,764
Muzan Kibutsuji,

1153
01:04:51,980 --> 01:04:56,424
I had sworn to destroy you
by any means necessary.

1154
01:04:57,028 --> 01:05:01,256
Yet, at this moment,
I am powerless to do so.

1155
01:05:01,946 --> 01:05:03,284
[loud thump]

1156
01:05:03,456 --> 01:05:05,397
[grunting]

1157
01:05:08,418 --> 01:05:12,344
Soon enough,
I'll be absorbed as well.

1158
01:05:13,164 --> 01:05:14,673
Please, someone. Anyone!

1159
01:05:14,795 --> 01:05:15,795
Come quickly!

1160
01:05:16,337 --> 01:05:18,031
I beg you!

1161
01:05:21,108 --> 01:05:23,293
[fight grunts]

1162
01:05:25,122 --> 01:05:27,352
[♪ intense music playing]

1163
01:05:32,704 --> 01:05:37,283
[KIRIYA] According to Father,
if Muzan should die,

1164
01:05:37,284 --> 01:05:39,505
the other demons
will also perish.

1165
01:05:40,715 --> 01:05:44,648
By that logic, it's clear
that Muzan is still alive.

1166
01:05:45,903 --> 01:05:47,416
At this very moment,

1167
01:05:47,631 --> 01:05:50,355
Ms. Tamayo must be
suppressing his powers.

1168
01:05:51,262 --> 01:05:52,775
If she weren't,

1169
01:05:53,122 --> 01:05:56,018
he would surely be aware
of Yushiro's watchful gaze.

1170
01:05:57,055 --> 01:05:59,692
Before Muzan's powers
are fully restored,

1171
01:05:59,865 --> 01:06:03,064
we must do whatever it takes
to see that he's defeated.

1172
01:06:04,880 --> 01:06:06,306
I have to wonder, though,

1173
01:06:06,522 --> 01:06:09,764
inside of this
infinite castle...

1174
01:06:10,715 --> 01:06:13,049
...will we really
be able to find him

1175
01:06:13,266 --> 01:06:14,822
and put an end to it all?

1176
01:06:20,139 --> 01:06:22,127
No need to be nervous.

1177
01:06:22,689 --> 01:06:25,066
You're doing a fine job,
my child.

1178
01:06:27,012 --> 01:06:30,210
Muzan will surely reveal himself
once more,

1179
01:06:30,903 --> 01:06:33,409
just as he did when he found me.

1180
01:06:35,614 --> 01:06:40,283
When it comes to this man,
that's simply his nature.

1181
01:06:41,018 --> 01:06:42,703
[gasps]

1182
01:06:45,772 --> 01:06:47,545
[KIRIYA] I understand, Father.

1183
01:06:48,279 --> 01:06:50,916
I will see to it
our plan succeeds.

1184
01:06:52,343 --> 01:06:54,937
We must find him before
the Corps members' strength

1185
01:06:55,152 --> 01:06:56,318
is fully depleted,

1186
01:06:56,319 --> 01:06:58,524
and settle this
once and for all.

1187
01:06:58,914 --> 01:07:00,081
[Gyomei grunts]

1188
01:07:04,576 --> 01:07:05,787
[distorted grunting]

1189
01:07:08,856 --> 01:07:11,017
- [grunting]
- [KAKUSHI 1] Protect them!

1190
01:07:11,233 --> 01:07:12,487
[KAKUSHI 2] Everybody, group up!

1191
01:07:12,703 --> 01:07:13,914
We have to form a wall!

1192
01:07:14,129 --> 01:07:15,945
Get their attention
off the Hashira!

1193
01:07:16,161 --> 01:07:18,366
Please, sir!
Go on ahead without us!

1194
01:07:18,927 --> 01:07:20,960
You as well! We got this!

1195
01:07:21,175 --> 01:07:22,300
Are you certain?

1196
01:07:22,904 --> 01:07:25,282
- [both grunting]
- [groans]

1197
01:07:26,839 --> 01:07:28,135
[thuds]

1198
01:07:30,556 --> 01:07:33,280
We are!
Just defeat Kibutsuji!

1199
01:07:33,453 --> 01:07:34,620
Please, sir!

1200
01:07:35,225 --> 01:07:36,608
Very well, then.

1201
01:07:36,824 --> 01:07:39,418
I will put my faith
in your efforts here.

1202
01:07:39,634 --> 01:07:40,634
Tokito!

1203
01:07:42,278 --> 01:07:43,748
[KAKUSHI 1] All right!

1204
01:07:43,749 --> 01:07:46,517
Let's show them the fruits
of our Hashira training!

1205
01:07:46,734 --> 01:07:47,858
[ALL] Right!

1206
01:07:48,075 --> 01:07:50,021
[♪ epic cinematic music playing]

1207
01:07:51,450 --> 01:07:53,613
[fight grunts]

1208
01:07:54,954 --> 01:07:57,114
[KIRIYA] Everyone, thank you.

1209
01:07:57,638 --> 01:08:00,828
I know Father would be proud
to see you giving it your all.

1210
01:08:06,467 --> 01:08:08,652
[♪ melancholic music playing]

1211
01:08:11,319 --> 01:08:13,591
- [whimpering]
- [KIRIYA] Stop that!

1212
01:08:14,291 --> 01:08:16,215
You must keep your hands moving.

1213
01:08:16,826 --> 01:08:19,055
Right now, we need to focus.

1214
01:08:20,804 --> 01:08:21,804
[KANATA] Yes.

1215
01:08:24,810 --> 01:08:28,031
Master Kiriya
is quite impressive.

1216
01:08:29,147 --> 01:08:30,865
It's clear
he's still in mourning

1217
01:08:31,080 --> 01:08:32,712
over the loss of the Master,

1218
01:08:32,884 --> 01:08:34,902
yet his duty is unwavering.

1219
01:08:35,588 --> 01:08:38,896
He's led the Demon Slayer Corps
rather splendidly.

1220
01:08:40,355 --> 01:08:43,190
Wouldn't you agree, Mr. Rengoku?

1221
01:08:44,135 --> 01:08:45,724
I would, indeed.

1222
01:08:47,098 --> 01:08:49,804
These children
are still young in years,

1223
01:08:50,019 --> 01:08:52,938
but their resolve
is anything but childish.

1224
01:08:54,098 --> 01:08:56,117
I swear to protect them.

1225
01:08:56,632 --> 01:08:59,080
Just as Kyojuro did before me,

1226
01:08:59,553 --> 01:09:02,086
I will risk my own life
to do so.

1227
01:09:06,295 --> 01:09:08,656
[Nezuko whimpers in pain]

1228
01:09:15,185 --> 01:09:18,190
[SAKONJI] I didn't think
she would suffer this much.

1229
01:09:19,264 --> 01:09:22,700
The Master was working
with a demon named Tamayo

1230
01:09:22,914 --> 01:09:25,148
who delivered this antidote.

1231
01:09:25,362 --> 01:09:28,154
I've administered it
as she instructed.

1232
01:09:29,399 --> 01:09:31,074
Even so,

1233
01:09:31,075 --> 01:09:34,924
will Nezuko be able to turn
back into a human, I wonder?

1234
01:09:35,459 --> 01:09:38,760
If Nezuko
does become human again,

1235
01:09:38,938 --> 01:09:42,195
Muzan's grand scheme
will collapse.

1236
01:09:42,417 --> 01:09:43,756
His thousand-year quest

1237
01:09:43,934 --> 01:09:46,388
for a vessel
which can resist the sun

1238
01:09:46,611 --> 01:09:48,084
will be no more.

1239
01:09:48,619 --> 01:09:51,519
And all of the progress
he's made

1240
01:09:51,741 --> 01:09:54,240
will be wound back like a clock.

1241
01:09:55,845 --> 01:09:59,949
In the many years that we've had
to endure this nightmare,

1242
01:10:00,173 --> 01:10:02,091
Nezuko is the only demon

1243
01:10:02,314 --> 01:10:05,080
who has been able
to live in the sunlight.

1244
01:10:05,303 --> 01:10:07,355
[♪ melancholic music playing]

1245
01:10:10,522 --> 01:10:12,664
[heart beating]

1246
01:10:14,002 --> 01:10:15,563
[inhales deeply]

1247
01:10:16,813 --> 01:10:18,329
[sighs wearily]

1248
01:10:21,185 --> 01:10:23,281
"The final battle."

1249
01:10:23,504 --> 01:10:26,582
These words
echo in my mind.

1250
01:10:28,456 --> 01:10:29,794
[gulps, sighs]

1251
01:10:30,330 --> 01:10:32,114
And each time they do,

1252
01:10:32,337 --> 01:10:35,638
I can't help but tremble
as my heart beats louder.

1253
01:10:36,665 --> 01:10:39,964
This battle may finally
reach its conclusion tonight.

1254
01:10:41,051 --> 01:10:46,864
I never dreamed that I'd be
alive to witness it myself.

1255
01:10:48,384 --> 01:10:49,384
Tanjiro,

1256
01:10:49,606 --> 01:10:51,963
I sometimes
think back to the day

1257
01:10:52,185 --> 01:10:54,853
when you brought
your demon sister to me.

1258
01:10:55,298 --> 01:10:57,209
Ever since then,

1259
01:10:57,432 --> 01:11:01,745
it feels like a giant wheel
of fate has been slowly turning.

1260
01:11:02,857 --> 01:11:06,947
Perhaps it would be best to
compare the sum of our battles

1261
01:11:07,169 --> 01:11:09,837
to a giant dormant machine.

1262
01:11:10,059 --> 01:11:14,061
You and Nezuko are the small
cogs that have joined together

1263
01:11:14,283 --> 01:11:16,106
and awoken it from its slumber.

1264
01:11:16,728 --> 01:11:21,797
What was once frozen in place
has now been set into motion.

1265
01:11:22,019 --> 01:11:24,064
[♪ intriguing music playing]

1266
01:11:24,553 --> 01:11:26,815
- [moaning]
- Don't give up, Nezuko.

1267
01:11:28,318 --> 01:11:30,971
Keep up the fight, Tanjiro.

1268
01:11:31,678 --> 01:11:34,906
You both have to pull through,
no matter what!

1269
01:11:35,438 --> 01:11:37,162
[TANJIRO] Hinokami Kagura:

1270
01:11:37,692 --> 01:11:38,754
Fire Wheel!

1271
01:11:38,975 --> 01:11:40,965
[♪ epic dramatic music playing]

1272
01:11:41,496 --> 01:11:43,219
Go through!

1273
01:11:43,220 --> 01:11:45,918
If I can't even sever his arm,
I'll never sever his head!

1274
01:11:46,139 --> 01:11:48,217
[yelling]

1275
01:11:49,013 --> 01:11:50,296
[flesh squelches]

1276
01:11:50,738 --> 01:11:52,285
[blood splatters]

1277
01:11:52,507 --> 01:11:53,506
DESTROY

1278
01:11:53,507 --> 01:11:54,761
I got one.

1279
01:11:54,762 --> 01:11:56,620
I was able
to dodge his attack, too.

1280
01:11:56,797 --> 01:11:58,034
I can do this!

1281
01:11:58,565 --> 01:11:59,565
I couldn't aim for his head,

1282
01:11:59,784 --> 01:12:01,147
but this time, for sure!

1283
01:12:02,290 --> 01:12:04,840
Hinokami Kagura: Fake Rainbow!

1284
01:12:05,060 --> 01:12:06,060
[fizzles out]

1285
01:12:08,181 --> 01:12:10,071
[high-pitched ringing]

1286
01:12:12,182 --> 01:12:14,205
- [panting]
- [sword clatters]

1287
01:12:15,699 --> 01:12:17,678
[flesh squelching]

1288
01:12:17,897 --> 01:12:19,216
Huh?

1289
01:12:20,667 --> 01:12:22,205
[GIYU] Tanjiro.

1290
01:12:22,382 --> 01:12:24,932
You've really sharpened
your skills, haven't you?

1291
01:12:25,855 --> 01:12:27,614
It wouldn't be an exaggeration

1292
01:12:27,833 --> 01:12:30,384
to say he's at the level
of a Hashira now.

1293
01:12:31,614 --> 01:12:35,835
To think that he'd do this well
against Upper Three.

1294
01:12:36,055 --> 01:12:38,077
[♪ enchanting folk music
playing]

1295
01:12:41,198 --> 01:12:42,649
That day...

1296
01:12:43,440 --> 01:12:46,254
...I remember a boy
who felt completely helpless

1297
01:12:46,694 --> 01:12:48,980
as he collapsed
onto the cold snow,

1298
01:12:49,507 --> 01:12:52,321
begging through tears
for his sister's life.

1299
01:13:00,191 --> 01:13:02,345
But you are helpless no longer.

1300
01:13:02,829 --> 01:13:05,730
You have the strength
to fight not only for your life,

1301
01:13:06,214 --> 01:13:08,544
but also
for what's precious to you.

1302
01:13:10,215 --> 01:13:11,934
[AKAZA] "This boy is not weak.

1303
01:13:12,815 --> 01:13:14,115
Don't insult him."

1304
01:13:15,005 --> 01:13:18,961
I must admit that Kyojuro
was right when he said that.

1305
01:13:19,554 --> 01:13:21,195
You are certainly not weak.

1306
01:13:21,415 --> 01:13:23,987
In fact, I commend you.

1307
01:13:26,823 --> 01:13:29,261
Technique Development...

1308
01:13:29,482 --> 01:13:31,521
[♪ intense rock music playing]

1309
01:13:33,516 --> 01:13:36,929
Now, let's kick things off,
shall we?

1310
01:13:37,549 --> 01:13:39,721
It's time we had some fun.

1311
01:13:45,395 --> 01:13:47,477
- [rumbling]
- [heavy creaking]

1312
01:14:08,664 --> 01:14:09,949
[exhales sharply]

1313
01:14:16,420 --> 01:14:18,016
[grunts]

1314
01:14:26,969 --> 01:14:30,072
[GIYU]
Water Breathing, Third Form:

1315
01:14:30,249 --> 01:14:31,711
Flowing Dance!

1316
01:14:32,642 --> 01:14:34,636
You're a Water Hashira.

1317
01:14:34,858 --> 01:14:36,543
How lucky for me!

1318
01:14:36,764 --> 01:14:37,984
It's been 50 years
since I fought one.

1319
01:14:42,341 --> 01:14:43,987
[debris clattering]

1320
01:14:45,943 --> 01:14:49,679
Destructive Death: Disorder!

1321
01:14:51,502 --> 01:14:54,259
Water Breathing, Eleventh Form:

1322
01:14:55,059 --> 01:14:56,482
Dead Calm.

1323
01:15:01,507 --> 01:15:04,309
[AKAZA] I've never seen
that move before.

1324
01:15:04,842 --> 01:15:07,111
Perhaps the last
Water Hashira I killed

1325
01:15:07,332 --> 01:15:09,334
never had a chance to use it!

1326
01:15:09,557 --> 01:15:12,625
[TANJIRO] Hinokami Kagura:
Raging Sun!

1327
01:15:14,804 --> 01:15:15,804
He vanished!

1328
01:15:17,105 --> 01:15:18,105
Behind me!

1329
01:15:18,260 --> 01:15:19,285
Fake Rain Kagura!

1330
01:15:20,186 --> 01:15:23,292
[GIYU] Water Breathing,
Second Form: Water Wheel.

1331
01:15:25,746 --> 01:15:26,746
[yells]

1332
01:15:32,113 --> 01:15:33,573
[TANJIRO] Hinokami Kagura:

1333
01:15:34,381 --> 01:15:35,467
Flame Dance!

1334
01:15:35,468 --> 01:15:38,107
[AKAZA] Destructive Death,
Leg Type: Crown Splitter!

1335
01:15:38,573 --> 01:15:40,406
[TANJIRO]
I blocked it with my sword.

1336
01:15:43,481 --> 01:15:45,003
His move barely grazed me

1337
01:15:45,159 --> 01:15:46,649
and still did
this kind of damage?

1338
01:15:49,786 --> 01:15:51,091
[AKAZA] How marvelous!

1339
01:15:52,053 --> 01:15:54,725
That elegant sword skill
you're using is magnificent!

1340
01:15:54,880 --> 01:15:56,775
I must know now.
What is your name?

1341
01:15:56,930 --> 01:15:58,110
I want to remember you!

1342
01:15:59,601 --> 01:16:01,776
I don't have a name
to give to a demon like you.

1343
01:16:01,931 --> 01:16:03,857
I hate talking,
so don't speak to me!

1344
01:16:04,416 --> 01:16:05,416
Is that so?

1345
01:16:05,565 --> 01:16:07,367
You're not much
for small talk, are you?

1346
01:16:07,522 --> 01:16:10,411
Well, I happen to quite
enjoy it, so I'll ask you again.

1347
01:16:10,815 --> 01:16:11,815
What is your name?

1348
01:16:12,270 --> 01:16:16,383
[grunting]

1349
01:16:18,850 --> 01:16:23,236
- [impact grunts]
- [crumbles]

1350
01:16:25,064 --> 01:16:31,735
[AKAZA]
Destructive Death, Leg Type:

1351
01:16:32,190 --> 01:16:36,576
Explosive Flurry!

1352
01:16:44,434 --> 01:16:49,461
[yelling]

1353
01:17:01,065 --> 01:17:02,065
- [impact grunts]
- [TANJIRO] Mr. Giyu!

1354
01:17:02,645 --> 01:17:03,705
I see. That's his name.

1355
01:17:03,940 --> 01:17:06,153
Thank you for letting me know.

1356
01:17:09,495 --> 01:17:10,614
Hinokami Kagura!

1357
01:17:10,831 --> 01:17:13,744
Destructive Death:
Eight-Layered Demon Core!

1358
01:17:13,918 --> 01:17:16,049
Burning Bones, Summer Sun!

1359
01:17:22,613 --> 01:17:24,439
[panting]

1360
01:17:30,961 --> 01:17:32,874
[AKAZA] Excellent form!

1361
01:17:33,048 --> 01:17:36,830
To improve this much in such
a short time is impressive.

1362
01:17:37,004 --> 01:17:38,004
I'll give you my praise.

1363
01:17:38,226 --> 01:17:39,874
It seems obvious to me

1364
01:17:40,053 --> 01:17:42,903
that Kyojuro must have
really inspired you.

1365
01:17:43,126 --> 01:17:47,314
The night we met, you were
merely a weak, mournful child,

1366
01:17:47,536 --> 01:17:49,051
crumpled on the ground.

1367
01:17:49,274 --> 01:17:51,545
Not even worthy of being killed.

1368
01:17:51,768 --> 01:17:53,683
- But just look at you now!
- [cracking]

1369
01:17:53,906 --> 01:17:57,915
This leap in your abilities,
it's like you've been reborn!

1370
01:17:58,138 --> 01:18:00,321
My heart won't stop racing.

1371
01:18:00,544 --> 01:18:02,726
I'm truly overjoyed!

1372
01:18:02,949 --> 01:18:04,597
[snickers]

1373
01:18:05,355 --> 01:18:07,375
The night Kyojuro died,
I was glad that it happened.

1374
01:18:08,543 --> 01:18:09,543
[exclaims in disbelief]

1375
01:18:10,072 --> 01:18:11,599
How tragic would it have been

1376
01:18:11,824 --> 01:18:13,891
if he had never gotten
any stronger.

1377
01:18:14,565 --> 01:18:16,812
Such a stubborn man,
not letting go

1378
01:18:17,036 --> 01:18:20,048
of those worthless values
of staying human.

1379
01:18:21,306 --> 01:18:23,148
How dare you!

1380
01:18:30,519 --> 01:18:34,294
Shut up! Just shut up!

1381
01:18:37,485 --> 01:18:40,630
Don't you dare
even speak his name!

1382
01:18:41,754 --> 01:18:43,058
[AKAZA] What's the matter?

1383
01:18:43,282 --> 01:18:45,709
I'm only paying the man
a compliment.

1384
01:18:45,934 --> 01:18:47,596
I'm being sincere.

1385
01:18:47,821 --> 01:18:49,619
These are high words of praise.

1386
01:18:49,843 --> 01:18:50,922
[TANJIRO] You're wrong.

1387
01:18:51,146 --> 01:18:53,213
All you're doing
is insulting him!

1388
01:18:53,394 --> 01:18:55,865
You're just spitting
on his memory!

1389
01:18:56,090 --> 01:18:57,573
On all of us!

1390
01:18:58,607 --> 01:19:01,438
You couldn't be
more wrong, Tanjiro.

1391
01:19:01,618 --> 01:19:06,291
As you'll recall, the only thing
I despise is weak human beings.

1392
01:19:06,786 --> 01:19:09,842
Only a feeble weakling
is deserving of my scorn

1393
01:19:10,022 --> 01:19:11,190
and no one else.

1394
01:19:12,224 --> 01:19:13,224
That's right.

1395
01:19:13,399 --> 01:19:16,466
The mere sight of them
makes my skin crawl.

1396
01:19:16,685 --> 01:19:18,263
They make me retch!

1397
01:19:19,271 --> 01:19:21,550
Through the laws of nature,
they are weeded out

1398
01:19:21,769 --> 01:19:24,004
from this world
just as they should be.

1399
01:19:24,925 --> 01:19:27,825
Everything you just said
is wrong!

1400
01:19:35,526 --> 01:19:42,526
[AKAZA] Huh?

1401
01:19:53,945 --> 01:19:54,945
The fact
you're even alive right now,

1402
01:19:55,036 --> 01:19:56,036
isn't that proof enough?

1403
01:19:56,236 --> 01:19:57,547
As an infant,
we're all helpless.

1404
01:19:57,637 --> 01:19:58,637
We can't live
without someone else's help.

1405
01:19:58,820 --> 01:19:59,819
You're no different, Akaza.

1406
01:19:59,820 --> 01:20:00,893
Even if you don't remember,

1407
01:20:00,894 --> 01:20:01,803
there was a time
when you were protected

1408
01:20:01,804 --> 01:20:02,476
and cared for by someone.

1409
01:20:02,477 --> 01:20:03,131
I know it!

1410
01:20:03,132 --> 01:20:04,132
That's why you're alive.

1411
01:20:05,825 --> 01:20:06,971
The strong should aid
and protect the weak.

1412
01:20:06,972 --> 01:20:07,990
And in turn,
the weak become strong

1413
01:20:08,173 --> 01:20:09,428
and aid and protect
those weaker than themselves!

1414
01:20:09,665 --> 01:20:11,065
That is the law of nature.

1415
01:20:12,705 --> 01:20:15,585
Akaza, I can't tolerate
your way of thinking.

1416
01:20:15,851 --> 01:20:16,851
Here on out,

1417
01:20:16,945 --> 01:20:19,425
I won't let you
do as you please!

1418
01:20:22,223 --> 01:20:23,223
[AKAZA] I get it now.

1419
01:20:24,656 --> 01:20:27,066
I have a disgust for this boy
that's almost primal in nature.

1420
01:20:27,479 --> 01:20:29,572
Even if he's stronger,
that feeling hasn't faded.

1421
01:20:32,249 --> 01:20:33,417
[MAN] No matter who they are,

1422
01:20:33,538 --> 01:20:35,120
everyone begins life
as a newborn.

1423
01:20:35,242 --> 01:20:37,091
We learn by getting help
from those around us.

1424
01:20:37,480 --> 01:20:39,013
We are not competing
with others.

1425
01:20:39,135 --> 01:20:41,082
The only opponent
you have in life is yourself.

1426
01:20:41,447 --> 01:20:43,710
Just focus on becoming stronger
than you were yesterday.

1427
01:20:44,342 --> 01:20:46,387
If you can stay this path
for a decade or even two,

1428
01:20:46,508 --> 01:20:47,507
that would be commendable.

1429
01:20:47,508 --> 01:20:48,503
And before you know it,

1430
01:20:48,504 --> 01:20:50,624
you will be helping others
in turn.

1431
01:20:51,366 --> 01:20:53,501
[breathing shakily]

1432
01:20:57,214 --> 01:20:58,328
[gasps]

1433
01:20:59,163 --> 01:21:00,462
[TANJIRO] What was that?

1434
01:21:00,463 --> 01:21:02,226
He just swung his fist
at nothing.

1435
01:21:08,817 --> 01:21:10,766
Tanjiro.

1436
01:21:11,694 --> 01:21:14,432
You still repulse me to my core.

1437
01:21:14,663 --> 01:21:15,822
[♪ rock music playing]

1438
01:21:15,823 --> 01:21:18,423
Destructive Death,
Crushing Type:

1439
01:21:18,655 --> 01:21:21,068
Ten Thousand Leaves
Flashing Willow!

1440
01:21:24,363 --> 01:21:26,452
[TANJIRO]
This speed, it's blinding!

1441
01:21:26,683 --> 01:21:29,329
No, it's not just his speed.

1442
01:21:29,561 --> 01:21:32,902
It's his precision,
his aura, and also--

1443
01:21:35,873 --> 01:21:36,986
[grunts]

1444
01:21:38,146 --> 01:21:40,607
Destructive Death, Leg Type.

1445
01:21:40,792 --> 01:21:41,999
[TANJIRO] Below.

1446
01:21:43,994 --> 01:21:46,362
[AKAZA] Flying Planet
Thousand Wheels!

1447
01:21:52,673 --> 01:21:55,318
[TANJIRO] Even if I could
anticipate his strikes,

1448
01:21:55,550 --> 01:21:58,660
they're so powerful,
I can't completely deflect them.

1449
01:21:58,845 --> 01:22:00,934
His techniques are so precise,

1450
01:22:01,166 --> 01:22:04,508
they can pierce through any
opening, no matter how small.

1451
01:22:07,570 --> 01:22:10,216
It's like a magnet
is attracting his attacks

1452
01:22:10,447 --> 01:22:12,351
straight toward my weak points.

1453
01:22:12,582 --> 01:22:15,646
But how? What's happening?

1454
01:22:15,878 --> 01:22:18,199
What could be
causing this behavior?

1455
01:22:18,662 --> 01:22:20,936
Come on. Think.

1456
01:22:22,283 --> 01:22:24,092
What's the answer?!

1457
01:22:24,324 --> 01:22:27,713
There must be a clue
in what Akaza's said or done.

1458
01:22:27,944 --> 01:22:30,172
[Akaza grunts] Hyah!

1459
01:22:31,286 --> 01:22:34,998
[TANJIRO] Hinokami Kagura:
Solar Heat Haze!

1460
01:22:43,259 --> 01:22:44,791
[blood spurts]

1461
01:22:45,394 --> 01:22:48,318
[chuckles]
What an interesting move.

1462
01:22:48,550 --> 01:22:52,309
I dodged it at first, but then
the blade seemed to extend.

1463
01:22:52,541 --> 01:22:55,047
I don't know what kind of swing
you put behind it,

1464
01:22:55,279 --> 01:22:56,857
but the tip of your blade
wavered

1465
01:22:57,089 --> 01:23:00,616
like it was in a heat haze.
How fascinating!

1466
01:23:03,912 --> 01:23:06,047
- [grunts]
- [glass shattering]

1467
01:23:07,578 --> 01:23:09,852
[debris crumbling]

1468
01:23:11,755 --> 01:23:15,514
[TANJIRO]
Hinokami Kagura: Dance!

1469
01:23:16,349 --> 01:23:17,741
[clangs]

1470
01:23:17,927 --> 01:23:19,041
My sword!

1471
01:23:20,109 --> 01:23:21,593
He'll break it!

1472
01:23:22,846 --> 01:23:25,353
[effort grunts]

1473
01:23:26,745 --> 01:23:28,648
That was a strong headbutt.

1474
01:23:30,458 --> 01:23:32,732
[TANJIRO] Damn you!
Let go of me!

1475
01:23:34,171 --> 01:23:35,841
No good.[straining]

1476
01:23:36,027 --> 01:23:38,162
I can't get him
to loosen his grip.

1477
01:23:42,617 --> 01:23:44,427
[water splashing]

1478
01:23:49,764 --> 01:23:50,971
[grunts softly]

1479
01:23:51,203 --> 01:23:52,641
Mr. Giyu!

1480
01:23:53,152 --> 01:23:55,148
[Giyu sighs]

1481
01:23:56,632 --> 01:23:59,418
You're starting
to get on my nerves.

1482
01:23:59,603 --> 01:24:02,480
Thanks to you,
my back is killing me now.

1483
01:24:03,037 --> 01:24:06,425
I'm not fond of being hurled
like a rag doll.

1484
01:24:06,657 --> 01:24:08,467
I'm gonna make you pay.

1485
01:24:09,349 --> 01:24:11,112
♪

1486
01:24:11,716 --> 01:24:15,986
Personally, I'd rather not draw
my sword if I can help it.

1487
01:24:16,496 --> 01:24:19,605
And I have a hard time
justifying using deadly force

1488
01:24:19,791 --> 01:24:21,090
if unnecessary.

1489
01:24:22,436 --> 01:24:24,385
But at this moment,

1490
01:24:24,618 --> 01:24:28,144
I'm against an opponent that
demands everything from me.

1491
01:24:28,331 --> 01:24:29,862
In the short time we fought,

1492
01:24:30,093 --> 01:24:32,600
my senses have been
pushed past their limits.

1493
01:24:33,714 --> 01:24:36,730
My dormant senses
have been rudely awakened

1494
01:24:36,916 --> 01:24:40,165
and are dragging me forward
towards the enemy.

1495
01:24:41,047 --> 01:24:44,944
I now know how much
it expands one's potential

1496
01:24:45,177 --> 01:24:47,172
to have one's back
against the wall

1497
01:24:47,405 --> 01:24:49,075
with their sword raised

1498
01:24:49,307 --> 01:24:51,163
in the face of death.

1499
01:24:54,458 --> 01:24:55,758
Mr. Giyu.

1500
01:25:02,023 --> 01:25:03,694
[♪ intense music playing]

1501
01:25:13,950 --> 01:25:17,014
[AKAZA] A mark appeared
and his movements have gotten...

1502
01:25:17,245 --> 01:25:18,499
Faster!

1503
01:25:23,371 --> 01:25:27,084
[GIYU] Water Breathing,
Fourth Form: Striking Tide!

1504
01:25:28,152 --> 01:25:30,148
[grunts softly, chuckles]

1505
01:25:35,485 --> 01:25:36,645
[grunts]

1506
01:25:42,399 --> 01:25:44,163
[TANJIRO] They're both so fast.

1507
01:25:44,396 --> 01:25:47,087
Mr. Giyu's speed increased
with the mark,

1508
01:25:47,273 --> 01:25:49,454
but Akaza adapted to it
instantly.

1509
01:25:52,099 --> 01:25:54,791
Don't tell me
that's all you're capable of!

1510
01:25:55,023 --> 01:25:57,065
[Giyu groans angrily]

1511
01:25:59,154 --> 01:26:01,706
[both grunting]

1512
01:26:04,444 --> 01:26:08,528
Show me more!
Don't you dare hold back!

1513
01:26:39,251 --> 01:26:43,104
[GIYU]
Tenth Form: Constant Flux!

1514
01:26:51,132 --> 01:26:52,803
[yelling]

1515
01:27:01,295 --> 01:27:04,916
Seventh Form:
Drop Ripple Thrust!

1516
01:27:05,148 --> 01:27:07,886
Destructive Death: Disorder!

1517
01:27:19,210 --> 01:27:22,133
[TANJIRO] Mr. Giyu! Akaza!

1518
01:27:24,455 --> 01:27:25,455
Calm down!

1519
01:27:26,268 --> 01:27:28,393
[weapons clanging]

1520
01:27:29,478 --> 01:27:31,874
Think. Don't panic.

1521
01:27:32,100 --> 01:27:34,406
Whatever you do,
don't lose focus.

1522
01:27:35,084 --> 01:27:36,755
[grunts]

1523
01:27:36,756 --> 01:27:39,966
Why is it that Akaza's attacks
are always so accurate?

1524
01:27:40,916 --> 01:27:45,121
How is he able to respond
to attacks from his blind spots?

1525
01:27:46,025 --> 01:27:47,025
Think!

1526
01:27:50,950 --> 01:27:52,762
[AKAZA] Your fighting spirit
has been tempered

1527
01:27:52,952 --> 01:27:54,273
like quality steel.

1528
01:27:54,424 --> 01:27:55,556
Your name?

1529
01:27:56,123 --> 01:27:57,218
[gasps]

1530
01:27:58,048 --> 01:27:59,935
[TANJIRO]
Back when he fought Mr. Rengoku,

1531
01:28:00,124 --> 01:28:03,145
I remember Akaza using the words
"fighting spirit."

1532
01:28:04,352 --> 01:28:06,013
What did he mean by that?

1533
01:28:06,202 --> 01:28:08,543
Is he able to sense things
through fighting spirit?

1534
01:28:09,034 --> 01:28:11,234
The same way I can sense things
through scent?

1535
01:28:31,555 --> 01:28:32,715
Wherever the enemy's aiming at,

1536
01:28:32,884 --> 01:28:34,818
I get this weird
tingling feeling.

1537
01:28:35,028 --> 01:28:38,308
So, that's how you knew Gyutaro
was attacking you from behind.

1538
01:28:38,517 --> 01:28:40,452
You sure are incredible,
Inosuke.

1539
01:28:40,621 --> 01:28:42,260
[laughs boisterously]

1540
01:28:42,471 --> 01:28:45,246
Well, my skin is tougher
than most people's.

1541
01:28:45,414 --> 01:28:47,054
And whether
it's from behind or not,

1542
01:28:47,264 --> 01:28:48,274
if someone's looking at me,

1543
01:28:48,484 --> 01:28:49,955
I know just
where they're lookin'.

1544
01:28:50,166 --> 01:28:51,469
Could you show me?

1545
01:28:51,680 --> 01:28:53,908
[laughs] Sure thing!

1546
01:28:54,623 --> 01:28:56,095
[determined grunt]

1547
01:28:58,576 --> 01:29:00,216
- It's my right shoulder.
- [gasps]

1548
01:29:00,426 --> 01:29:01,982
You really got it.
That's amazing!

1549
01:29:02,528 --> 01:29:04,841
It's even easier to know
someone's looking at me

1550
01:29:05,052 --> 01:29:06,397
if they had killing intent.

1551
01:29:06,607 --> 01:29:09,720
Since anyone who can harm me
is bad news,

1552
01:29:09,929 --> 01:29:12,410
killing intent kind of
feels like it's stabbing me

1553
01:29:12,579 --> 01:29:13,840
through the skin, you know?

1554
01:29:14,724 --> 01:29:15,724
[TANJIRO] That's right.

1555
01:29:15,947 --> 01:29:18,505
Inosuke was able
to sense the invisible

1556
01:29:18,730 --> 01:29:21,288
using only his honed
sense of touch.

1557
01:29:22,050 --> 01:29:25,461
Think back.
What else did we talk about...

1558
01:29:26,224 --> 01:29:27,435
that day?

1559
01:29:27,614 --> 01:29:29,499
Where things get real tricky

1560
01:29:29,679 --> 01:29:32,641
is when someone who doesn't have
killing intent or hostility

1561
01:29:32,820 --> 01:29:33,896
is looking at me,

1562
01:29:34,121 --> 01:29:36,319
- like that tiny hag!
- Huh?

1563
01:29:36,903 --> 01:29:38,203
[INOSUKE] That old hag

1564
01:29:38,204 --> 01:29:40,089
from the house
with the wisteria mark

1565
01:29:40,314 --> 01:29:41,480
was sneaky.

1566
01:29:41,705 --> 01:29:42,924
Before I knew it...

1567
01:29:43,103 --> 01:29:44,425
Huh?

1568
01:29:45,105 --> 01:29:47,584
...she'd be sitting right
behind me holding rice balls.

1569
01:29:51,867 --> 01:29:58,867
Calling her a "hag" isn't nice.
She's elderly.

1570
01:30:10,761 --> 01:30:17,761
- Elderly hag!
- Stop that!

1571
01:30:23,108 --> 01:30:30,108
Well, that got me thinkin'.

1572
01:30:34,697 --> 01:30:41,697
If I could hide my killing
intent, then I'd be a ninja.

1573
01:30:55,860 --> 01:31:02,860
I'd be able to sneak up
on anybody.

1574
01:31:09,208 --> 01:31:16,208
- [chuckles excitedly]
- Sure.

1575
01:31:21,555 --> 01:31:28,555
But, Inosuke,
she was only sneaky

1576
01:31:37,173 --> 01:31:44,173
'cause she didn't have
the intent of harming you.

1577
01:31:53,045 --> 01:32:00,045
And I think beheading a demon
without killing intent

1578
01:32:08,918 --> 01:32:15,719
would be impossible.

1579
01:32:19,245 --> 01:32:20,245
[INOSUKE] Hmm.

1580
01:32:20,653 --> 01:32:22,218
Yeah, you're probably right.

1581
01:32:22,389 --> 01:32:24,566
A half-hearted strike
without any killing intent

1582
01:32:24,737 --> 01:32:27,391
would never be strong enough
to cut through a demon's neck.

1583
01:32:28,106 --> 01:32:29,808
[TANJIRO]
It was a casual conversation

1584
01:32:29,978 --> 01:32:31,918
but I think Inosuke
was on to something.

1585
01:32:33,653 --> 01:32:35,933
What is it that
Akaza supposedly senses?

1586
01:32:36,070 --> 01:32:37,839
What does he mean
by "fighting spirit"?

1587
01:32:38,009 --> 01:32:39,269
Is it killing intent?

1588
01:32:39,438 --> 01:32:40,493
Is it the will to fight?

1589
01:32:40,664 --> 01:32:41,787
The time spent training?

1590
01:32:41,957 --> 01:32:43,046
Or maybe the amount?

1591
01:32:43,795 --> 01:32:44,815
Is it like the way

1592
01:32:44,816 --> 01:32:46,245
I can anticipate movements
through scent?

1593
01:32:47,300 --> 01:32:48,967
There must be something I can do

1594
01:32:49,376 --> 01:32:50,771
to disrupt his compass!

1595
01:32:53,188 --> 01:32:54,188
[♪ rock music playing]

1596
01:32:58,599 --> 01:33:00,403
Hinokami Kagura: Dance!

1597
01:33:02,070 --> 01:33:04,385
Just one problem
with your attack.

1598
01:33:04,554 --> 01:33:05,848
You're wide open!

1599
01:33:07,856 --> 01:33:09,013
[TANJIRO] His fist!

1600
01:33:13,539 --> 01:33:14,628
[grunts]

1601
01:33:18,099 --> 01:33:19,358
[panting]

1602
01:33:19,529 --> 01:33:20,528
Fighting spirit.

1603
01:33:20,529 --> 01:33:22,217
Instincts. Compass.

1604
01:33:22,353 --> 01:33:23,579
Perception.

1605
01:33:23,748 --> 01:33:26,437
Striking with killing intent.
Sensing the invisible.

1606
01:33:26,607 --> 01:33:28,139
Executing the impossible.

1607
01:33:28,514 --> 01:33:29,514
I see.

1608
01:33:30,340 --> 01:33:31,340
So, that's it.

1609
01:33:32,467 --> 01:33:33,500
- [birds chirping]
- [leaves rustling]

1610
01:33:34,884 --> 01:33:36,081
[laughter]

1611
01:33:39,283 --> 01:33:40,398
Um, Father?
What do you think about

1612
01:33:40,501 --> 01:33:41,575
when you dance
the Hinokami Kagura?

1613
01:33:41,844 --> 01:33:43,723
If it's too tiring for you,
I can take your place next year.

1614
01:33:43,992 --> 01:33:45,087
I don't want you
to overwork yourself.

1615
01:33:45,809 --> 01:33:46,809
Thank you, Tanjiro.

1616
01:33:47,007 --> 01:33:48,205
But to be honest,
I haven't found the Kagura

1617
01:33:48,308 --> 01:33:49,837
to be the least bit tiring
over the last few years.

1618
01:33:49,926 --> 01:33:50,926
I can't quite explain it,

1619
01:33:51,055 --> 01:33:52,624
but back when I learned it
from your grandfather years ago,

1620
01:33:52,625 --> 01:33:54,544
even though I was younger,
healthier and stronger than now,

1621
01:33:54,545 --> 01:33:56,012
I found it to be
far more tiring back then.

1622
01:33:56,865 --> 01:33:57,864
[♪ poignant music playing]

1623
01:33:57,865 --> 01:33:59,048
[TANJIRO] For generations,
the Kagura was performed

1624
01:33:59,151 --> 01:34:00,370
by the Kamado family
at the start of each year.

1625
01:34:00,618 --> 01:34:01,617
It was an exhausting performance

1626
01:34:01,618 --> 01:34:02,952
that would last
from sunset till dawn.

1627
01:34:03,530 --> 01:34:04,727
There are 12 different forms
that must be repeated

1628
01:34:04,728 --> 01:34:05,727
over and over again,

1629
01:34:05,728 --> 01:34:06,917
thousands of times
before daybreak.

1630
01:34:08,060 --> 01:34:09,059
I think my exhaustion

1631
01:34:09,060 --> 01:34:10,097
was the result
of unnecessary movement.

1632
01:34:10,098 --> 01:34:11,125
Using the correct movements

1633
01:34:11,213 --> 01:34:12,514
and breathing patterns
are vital to the dance.

1634
01:34:12,865 --> 01:34:14,228
It's what allows you
to produce maximum strength

1635
01:34:14,229 --> 01:34:15,178
while using minimal actions.

1636
01:34:15,179 --> 01:34:16,521
Once you've mastered
your breathing and movement,

1637
01:34:16,624 --> 01:34:17,822
your mind will become
transparent.

1638
01:34:18,153 --> 01:34:19,153
Transparent?

1639
01:34:19,254 --> 01:34:20,254
But before any of that,

1640
01:34:20,383 --> 01:34:21,416
you must memorize
the moves of the dance

1641
01:34:21,519 --> 01:34:23,005
and slowly ingrain them
into your muscle memory.

1642
01:34:23,006 --> 01:34:24,658
In doing so,
you'll open up your five senses

1643
01:34:24,762 --> 01:34:25,855
and become aware
of the shape of your own body,

1644
01:34:25,856 --> 01:34:26,939
vessel by vessel.

1645
01:34:27,467 --> 01:34:28,913
That was the truly
strenuous part.

1646
01:34:29,016 --> 01:34:30,524
All you can think is that
even if you go on struggling,

1647
01:34:30,627 --> 01:34:31,626
you'll never succeed.

1648
01:34:31,627 --> 01:34:32,626
After you've learned
all these things

1649
01:34:32,627 --> 01:34:33,456
and committed them to memory,

1650
01:34:33,457 --> 01:34:34,861
you'll understand how to remove
what you don't need,

1651
01:34:34,965 --> 01:34:36,699
only leaving behind in your body
what is required of you,

1652
01:34:36,803 --> 01:34:37,802
closing off the rest.

1653
01:34:37,803 --> 01:34:38,802
Closing?

1654
01:34:38,803 --> 01:34:39,922
You know how people
often close their eyes

1655
01:34:40,025 --> 01:34:41,024
when they're trying
to hear better?

1656
01:34:41,025 --> 01:34:42,025
In that same way,

1657
01:34:42,193 --> 01:34:43,192
you'll pick out the things
you need the most

1658
01:34:43,193 --> 01:34:44,382
in the movement
while eliminating the rest.

1659
01:34:44,651 --> 01:34:46,448
Eventually, you will be able
to open and close the vessels

1660
01:34:46,551 --> 01:34:48,080
and muscles in your body,
as if it were second nature.

1661
01:34:48,183 --> 01:34:49,567
The same way you blink
without a second thought.

1662
01:34:49,697 --> 01:34:50,697
When that happens,

1663
01:34:50,826 --> 01:34:52,396
a path illuminated
by a bright light will open.

1664
01:34:52,995 --> 01:34:54,853
If your mind is as clear
as possible, you'll begin to see

1665
01:34:54,854 --> 01:34:56,052
the Transparent World
before you.

1666
01:34:56,155 --> 01:34:57,207
But this domain
can only be reached

1667
01:34:57,208 --> 01:34:58,207
by pushing yourself
past your limits,

1668
01:34:58,208 --> 01:34:59,398
despite the suffering
that may be required.

1669
01:34:59,667 --> 01:35:00,667
Will I ever get to see it?

1670
01:35:00,947 --> 01:35:02,578
If you work tirelessly,
then that's for you to decide.

1671
01:35:02,930 --> 01:35:03,929
There. All done.

1672
01:35:03,930 --> 01:35:05,004
[TANJIRO] Thank you.

1673
01:35:08,215 --> 01:35:11,065
Ten days before my father died,

1674
01:35:11,291 --> 01:35:14,005
an incident where a bear
began attacking people

1675
01:35:14,231 --> 01:35:16,267
happened on
a neighboring mountain.

1676
01:35:16,765 --> 01:35:19,523
We lit bonfires around the house

1677
01:35:19,750 --> 01:35:22,509
and set up multiple ropes
lined with bells.

1678
01:35:34,496 --> 01:35:35,763
Hmm?

1679
01:35:41,825 --> 01:35:42,825
[TANJURO] Tanjiro.

1680
01:35:47,122 --> 01:35:48,772
[TANJIRO] Yes, Father?

1681
01:35:49,727 --> 01:35:51,072
[TANJURO] Come with me.

1682
01:35:52,115 --> 01:35:54,068
[Tanjiro grunting, panting]

1683
01:36:03,575 --> 01:36:04,921
[grunts]

1684
01:36:23,327 --> 01:36:25,454
[breathing unsteadily]

1685
01:36:26,279 --> 01:36:28,450
[♪ dramatic sting]

1686
01:36:32,704 --> 01:36:37,088
[loud growling]

1687
01:36:40,127 --> 01:36:43,166
[TANJURO] I understand
you must be very hungry.

1688
01:36:43,382 --> 01:36:46,422
But I'm afraid I can't allow you
to come any closer.

1689
01:36:47,594 --> 01:36:50,762
If anyone were to try
and cause harm to my family,

1690
01:36:50,979 --> 01:36:53,411
I would be forced
to show you no mercy.

1691
01:36:53,931 --> 01:36:56,232
If you disregard this warning...

1692
01:36:59,184 --> 01:37:02,092
...I'll have no choice
but to take your life.

1693
01:37:03,004 --> 01:37:04,567
- [roaring]
- [bells tinkling]

1694
01:37:05,045 --> 01:37:06,520
[thuds]

1695
01:37:06,738 --> 01:37:07,738
[gasps]

1696
01:37:11,339 --> 01:37:13,336
[bells tinkling]

1697
01:37:13,553 --> 01:37:17,156
[TANJIRO] The bear's head that
was as thick as a human torso

1698
01:37:17,373 --> 01:37:20,195
dropped to the ground
with the sound of the bells.

1699
01:37:22,105 --> 01:37:24,362
My eyes couldn't follow it.

1700
01:37:24,579 --> 01:37:26,099
But if I'm not mistaken,

1701
01:37:26,315 --> 01:37:29,484
my father slashed it twice
in the blink of an eye.

1702
01:37:31,091 --> 01:37:32,740
He must have.

1703
01:37:32,957 --> 01:37:35,822
His ax wouldn't have been
able to cut through otherwise.

1704
01:37:37,298 --> 01:37:40,858
All the while,
my father's scent never wavered.

1705
01:37:41,032 --> 01:37:43,333
Before and after
beheading the bear,

1706
01:37:43,549 --> 01:37:46,936
he emitted no fear,
no killing intent.

1707
01:37:54,142 --> 01:37:56,139
I hope that you were watching.

1708
01:37:57,180 --> 01:37:59,959
A day might come
where you have to do the same.

1709
01:38:00,133 --> 01:38:01,825
[wind blowing]

1710
01:38:02,955 --> 01:38:03,955
[TANJIRO] My father
wasn't the type of person

1711
01:38:04,305 --> 01:38:06,475
to flaunt his strength.

1712
01:38:07,595 --> 01:38:08,695
I realized later on,

1713
01:38:08,917 --> 01:38:12,835
that night, he wanted me
to see it in action.

1714
01:38:14,082 --> 01:38:16,664
The movements necessary
to be able to see

1715
01:38:16,887 --> 01:38:19,380
the Transparent World
he spoke of.

1716
01:38:21,518 --> 01:38:26,148
I'm sure my father, grandfather,
and great-grandfather

1717
01:38:26,638 --> 01:38:28,864
all learned the same way.

1718
01:38:30,556 --> 01:38:33,050
Whatever you do, never give up.

1719
01:38:33,273 --> 01:38:35,365
Always stay calm and focused.

1720
01:38:36,033 --> 01:38:39,016
Any wall you come up against
can be shattered

1721
01:38:39,595 --> 01:38:41,776
if you just work tirelessly.

1722
01:38:43,514 --> 01:38:44,735
[TANJIRO] I understand, Father.

1723
01:38:44,956 --> 01:38:46,327
In that moment...

1724
01:38:46,902 --> 01:38:48,273
that's why I was able to dodge

1725
01:38:48,450 --> 01:38:51,458
Akaza's inescapable blow
to my side.

1726
01:38:54,288 --> 01:38:56,101
If I hadn't moved in time,

1727
01:38:56,323 --> 01:38:58,623
I'm positive that strike
would have killed me.

1728
01:38:59,330 --> 01:39:01,985
When I was alternating moves
with Mr. Giyu,

1729
01:39:02,205 --> 01:39:04,594
weaving my attacks
in between each of his,

1730
01:39:05,125 --> 01:39:08,619
I was protected from being hit
by those lethal blows.

1731
01:39:09,105 --> 01:39:10,475
But in that instant,

1732
01:39:10,476 --> 01:39:13,041
even Mr. Giyu
couldn't make it in time.

1733
01:39:14,324 --> 01:39:19,410
However, for whatever reason,
I knew dodging was possible.

1734
01:39:19,897 --> 01:39:22,639
And for just a split second,

1735
01:39:22,861 --> 01:39:24,585
I was able to see it.

1736
01:39:26,355 --> 01:39:27,514
That world.

1737
01:39:29,631 --> 01:39:31,952
[♪ enchanting music playing]

1738
01:39:32,155 --> 01:39:33,655
The Transparent World.

1739
01:39:36,079 --> 01:39:39,465
Even his body
started to look transparent.

1740
01:39:40,608 --> 01:39:44,635
The same is when Hantengu
was hiding inside his own heart.

1741
01:39:45,138 --> 01:39:48,432
I don't know
if I saw him or smelled him.

1742
01:39:53,145 --> 01:39:54,145
Dodge.

1743
01:39:54,362 --> 01:39:57,365
I used only the senses
that would let me do that.

1744
01:39:57,887 --> 01:40:01,630
Without thinking, my body
moved faster than ever before.

1745
01:40:02,891 --> 01:40:06,373
When I'm inside the Transparent
World my father spoke of,

1746
01:40:06,590 --> 01:40:09,724
my battle instincts
improve drastically.

1747
01:40:11,725 --> 01:40:13,945
I can see my opponent's lungs

1748
01:40:14,162 --> 01:40:16,338
and the blood moving
throughout their body.

1749
01:40:16,861 --> 01:40:19,297
I can see
my own muscles contracting

1750
01:40:19,514 --> 01:40:22,604
faster and clearer than before.

1751
01:40:25,650 --> 01:40:27,870
If I close off
the fighting spirit

1752
01:40:28,087 --> 01:40:30,568
that Akaza
must be detecting me with,

1753
01:40:30,785 --> 01:40:32,396
I can go for his neck.

1754
01:40:32,875 --> 01:40:34,658
[screeches]

1755
01:40:45,363 --> 01:40:46,887
[TANJIRO] See it.

1756
01:40:47,104 --> 01:40:48,453
See it!

1757
01:40:48,671 --> 01:40:50,585
[exhales]

1758
01:40:50,802 --> 01:40:51,891
[♪ rock music playing]

1759
01:40:52,065 --> 01:40:53,327
It looks like
you've thrown about

1760
01:40:53,544 --> 01:40:55,459
every last Water Form at me.

1761
01:40:56,069 --> 01:40:58,635
Enough is enough,
wouldn't you say?

1762
01:40:59,201 --> 01:41:01,029
I'm putting an end to this.

1763
01:41:01,247 --> 01:41:04,206
But you have my respect
for lasting so long!

1764
01:41:05,728 --> 01:41:06,860
[GIYU] What?

1765
01:41:07,948 --> 01:41:09,950
In the middle of my downswing...

1766
01:41:11,430 --> 01:41:13,257
...he hit it from the side.

1767
01:41:14,911 --> 01:41:16,651
And snapped my sword!

1768
01:41:17,217 --> 01:41:19,524
- Goodbye, Giyu.
- [impact grunts]

1769
01:41:23,657 --> 01:41:25,442
[flesh squelching]

1770
01:41:26,399 --> 01:41:29,010
[muted silence]

1771
01:41:29,793 --> 01:41:30,925
[thuds]

1772
01:41:31,099 --> 01:41:32,970
[♪ intense dramatic music
playing]

1773
01:41:43,110 --> 01:41:46,112
- [exhales]
- [flame roaring]

1774
01:41:48,810 --> 01:41:51,987
[GIYU] He stopped the attack
by cutting off his fist.

1775
01:41:52,205 --> 01:41:53,804
His breathing is different.

1776
01:41:54,024 --> 01:41:55,528
And his appearance...

1777
01:41:56,810 --> 01:41:59,287
I've been saved by Tanjiro.

1778
01:42:00,702 --> 01:42:02,648
[AKAZA]
All of the cells in my body

1779
01:42:02,825 --> 01:42:04,372
down to the ones in my hair

1780
01:42:04,594 --> 01:42:07,601
are screaming at me to kill him
as soon as possible.

1781
01:42:09,326 --> 01:42:12,421
I don't know what kind of change
he underwent, but...

1782
01:42:13,704 --> 01:42:15,393
...he's dangerous.

1783
01:42:16,953 --> 01:42:19,075
[GIYU] His focus is on Tanjiro.

1784
01:42:20,184 --> 01:42:21,871
Now's my chance.

1785
01:42:26,310 --> 01:42:29,195
[AKAZA] Technique Development,
Final Form:

1786
01:42:29,772 --> 01:42:32,347
Blue Silver Chaotic Afterglow!

1787
01:42:35,455 --> 01:42:37,835
[GIYU] His attack speed
boosted again,

1788
01:42:38,054 --> 01:42:39,588
and the force is increased.

1789
01:42:40,070 --> 01:42:43,752
My only chance now
is with Dead Calm!

1790
01:43:05,620 --> 01:43:08,513
[TANJIRO] This must be
what Father was talking about.

1791
01:43:08,995 --> 01:43:11,795
This is it.
The Transparent World.

1792
01:43:22,004 --> 01:43:25,404
Strange. It feels like
time is passing by so slowly.

1793
01:43:27,143 --> 01:43:31,964
Or maybe... their movements
just look slower now.

1794
01:43:32,142 --> 01:43:34,195
[♪ intense music continues]

1795
01:43:35,265 --> 01:43:36,648
[groans]

1796
01:43:38,077 --> 01:43:40,084
[GIYU] It's no use.

1797
01:43:40,264 --> 01:43:43,253
A hundred strikes at once
is unavoidable.

1798
01:43:43,789 --> 01:43:45,439
Even with Dead Calm,

1799
01:43:45,663 --> 01:43:48,340
I still wasn't able
to block all of them.

1800
01:43:49,679 --> 01:43:51,553
[AKAZA] Stand proud, Giyu.

1801
01:43:51,776 --> 01:43:54,543
Most wouldn't have been
able to survive that.

1802
01:43:54,722 --> 01:43:57,577
You must have evaded
my fatal blows.

1803
01:43:58,380 --> 01:44:02,485
There's no need for you to die
like Kyojuro and Tanjiro did.

1804
01:44:02,709 --> 01:44:05,654
Give up your pride
and become a demon, Giyu.

1805
01:44:07,439 --> 01:44:10,965
[GIYU] Tanjiro's behind him
and he hasn't noticed?

1806
01:44:11,544 --> 01:44:14,133
- [Akaza speaking indistinctly]
- Is he masking his presence?

1807
01:44:14,356 --> 01:44:15,873
Now's our chance!

1808
01:44:16,721 --> 01:44:18,417
Tanjiro, do it!

1809
01:44:18,639 --> 01:44:20,960
If you have the strength,
behead him.

1810
01:44:21,451 --> 01:44:23,414
Before he notices you,

1811
01:44:23,638 --> 01:44:25,021
go for it!

1812
01:44:25,244 --> 01:44:29,037
Akaza!
Prepare to be decapitated!

1813
01:44:29,260 --> 01:44:30,375
[AKAZA] Huh?

1814
01:44:35,017 --> 01:44:37,650
[GIYU] He willingly
gave himself away!

1815
01:44:38,275 --> 01:44:39,275
[AKAZA] He's still alive?

1816
01:44:39,784 --> 01:44:41,866
I never would have thought
someone like him

1817
01:44:42,052 --> 01:44:44,227
could survive
an attack like that.

1818
01:44:44,829 --> 01:44:46,634
Well, it doesn't matter.

1819
01:44:46,866 --> 01:44:49,273
After all, my Destructive Death,
Compass Needle

1820
01:44:49,505 --> 01:44:50,985
can detect any attack!

1821
01:44:51,495 --> 01:44:54,775
The stronger my opponent's
fighting spirit is,

1822
01:44:55,005 --> 01:44:57,923
the greater
my Compass Needle's reaction.

1823
01:44:59,405 --> 01:45:00,701
[quivers]

1824
01:45:01,304 --> 01:45:02,544
What is this?

1825
01:45:03,505 --> 01:45:05,204
What is this odd presence
he's emitting?

1826
01:45:05,424 --> 01:45:07,232
It feels like
he's turned himself

1827
01:45:07,452 --> 01:45:09,128
into some other creature.

1828
01:45:09,304 --> 01:45:10,450
It's like...

1829
01:45:11,905 --> 01:45:14,463
...his fighting spirit is gone.

1830
01:45:14,682 --> 01:45:15,829
But how?

1831
01:45:16,049 --> 01:45:18,651
I have to calm down. Focus!

1832
01:45:19,136 --> 01:45:20,502
[grunts]

1833
01:45:21,297 --> 01:45:22,751
[flame roaring]

1834
01:45:25,087 --> 01:45:27,160
[TANJIRO] Hinokami Kagura:

1835
01:45:27,381 --> 01:45:29,805
Setting Sun Transformation.

1836
01:45:30,026 --> 01:45:32,054
[♪ intriguing music playing]

1837
01:45:32,892 --> 01:45:35,052
[tinkling]

1838
01:45:48,146 --> 01:45:49,424
[gasps]

1839
01:45:51,585 --> 01:45:54,318
[Akaza straining]
This can't be possible.

1840
01:45:56,920 --> 01:45:59,345
[Tanjiro exhales]

1841
01:46:01,417 --> 01:46:03,754
[AKAZA] In the last
several hundred years,

1842
01:46:03,930 --> 01:46:07,281
I've never once seen a human
without any fighting spirit.

1843
01:46:07,765 --> 01:46:10,808
Even newborn children
had traces of it.

1844
01:46:11,381 --> 01:46:13,938
And yet, in that instant,

1845
01:46:14,115 --> 01:46:15,922
his fighting spirit vanished

1846
01:46:16,099 --> 01:46:18,832
as if it were never there
to begin with.

1847
01:46:21,962 --> 01:46:24,256
It's as if
I was facing an anomaly

1848
01:46:24,475 --> 01:46:26,063
that shouldn't even exist.

1849
01:46:26,239 --> 01:46:28,841
So, my senses
were thrown into confusion.

1850
01:46:29,281 --> 01:46:32,368
My Compass Needle
detected nothing.

1851
01:46:32,940 --> 01:46:34,396
[tinkling]

1852
01:46:34,616 --> 01:46:37,526
But that's not the biggest issue
at hand here.

1853
01:46:37,746 --> 01:46:39,334
When on the battlefield,

1854
01:46:39,510 --> 01:46:42,023
there's no telling
what could come your way.

1855
01:46:42,243 --> 01:46:44,756
It's vital that you're able
to deal with the unexpected

1856
01:46:44,977 --> 01:46:46,344
at a moment's notice.

1857
01:46:46,829 --> 01:46:49,122
And I'm able to do that!

1858
01:46:49,738 --> 01:46:52,692
Or at least... I thought so.

1859
01:46:53,618 --> 01:46:56,396
But during that short battle,

1860
01:46:56,617 --> 01:47:00,938
he was able to grasp something
and use it to surpass my speed.

1861
01:47:01,466 --> 01:47:03,935
Whatever it was he learned
was able to shatter

1862
01:47:04,156 --> 01:47:06,316
centuries' worth
of martial arts techniques

1863
01:47:06,537 --> 01:47:08,388
with a single head-on attack.

1864
01:47:09,094 --> 01:47:12,155
Within those eyes of his,
there was no hatred, no rage,

1865
01:47:12,372 --> 01:47:15,288
no killing intent
or fighting spirit.

1866
01:47:15,941 --> 01:47:18,902
He must have somehow seen
what I'd been looking for:

1867
01:47:19,119 --> 01:47:23,342
the domain that lies
within the realm of the highest.

1868
01:47:25,040 --> 01:47:27,608
None other than
the selfless state.

1869
01:47:29,742 --> 01:47:32,397
For some time now,
I've had a vague sense

1870
01:47:32,615 --> 01:47:34,486
that this state of mind existed.

1871
01:47:34,922 --> 01:47:37,534
And yet, even after
all these centuries,

1872
01:47:37,752 --> 01:47:39,362
I've yet to attain it.

1873
01:47:46,850 --> 01:47:47,894
[gasps]

1874
01:47:48,504 --> 01:47:49,904
[AKAZA] Not yet!

1875
01:47:50,093 --> 01:47:51,418
I can still fight!

1876
01:47:51,606 --> 01:47:53,764
I will continue
to become stronger!

1877
01:48:00,176 --> 01:48:03,360
[TANJIRO] This is bad.
He's reattaching his head!

1878
01:48:03,852 --> 01:48:06,050
[effort grunting]

1879
01:48:07,754 --> 01:48:10,041
- [thuds]
- [gasps]

1880
01:48:12,776 --> 01:48:15,243
[AKAZA] I can't die here.

1881
01:48:16,678 --> 01:48:18,560
Not like this.

1882
01:48:21,655 --> 01:48:22,755
I have to become stronger.

1883
01:48:27,620 --> 01:48:34,620
Stronger than anyone else
in the whole world!

1884
01:48:35,834 --> 01:48:36,834
Stronger!

1885
01:48:37,155 --> 01:48:38,470
- [thuds]
- [fizzles out]

1886
01:48:38,630 --> 01:48:40,843
I have to find a way
to become stronger.

1887
01:48:42,383 --> 01:48:43,383
[clatters]

1888
01:48:46,103 --> 01:48:47,103
[body thuds]

1889
01:48:47,804 --> 01:48:48,804
[TANJIRO] That's it. It's over.

1890
01:48:50,520 --> 01:48:51,972
We won!

1891
01:48:52,941 --> 01:48:54,263
[sighs in relief]

1892
01:48:54,658 --> 01:48:56,595
[grunts in pain]

1893
01:48:56,991 --> 01:48:58,665
So lightheaded.

1894
01:49:00,514 --> 01:49:02,715
My muscles are cramping up.

1895
01:49:02,934 --> 01:49:04,916
My body's reached its limit.

1896
01:49:07,556 --> 01:49:10,418
Tanjiro, are you all ri--
[gasps]

1897
01:49:11,255 --> 01:49:12,775
His body
hasn't disintegrated yet.

1898
01:49:12,999 --> 01:49:15,504
Does... Does this mean...

1899
01:49:15,997 --> 01:49:17,070
Tan--

1900
01:49:17,742 --> 01:49:19,218
[♪ intense music playing]

1901
01:49:19,443 --> 01:49:20,607
[grunts]

1902
01:49:27,722 --> 01:49:31,615
[TANJIRO] He's moving!
His body is still intact!

1903
01:49:31,839 --> 01:49:33,942
The severed part is closing up!

1904
01:49:35,195 --> 01:49:37,119
[strained grunting]

1905
01:49:37,343 --> 01:49:39,088
I can't see straight.

1906
01:49:39,312 --> 01:49:41,012
I can't.

1907
01:49:44,190 --> 01:49:45,442
[impact grunts]

1908
01:49:50,634 --> 01:49:52,021
[strained gasping]

1909
01:49:52,244 --> 01:49:54,930
No. No way.

1910
01:49:55,153 --> 01:49:57,436
Slashing his neck
didn't kill him!

1911
01:49:57,615 --> 01:50:00,414
Is there some kind of condition
like with Gyutaro and Daki?

1912
01:50:00,911 --> 01:50:02,317
That can't be it.

1913
01:50:02,543 --> 01:50:06,215
His head disintegrated,
yet he hasn't given up!

1914
01:50:06,714 --> 01:50:10,204
It's like he's trying to evolve!

1915
01:50:12,108 --> 01:50:13,558
[impact grunts]

1916
01:50:16,732 --> 01:50:18,272
If we don't do something,

1917
01:50:18,499 --> 01:50:21,264
his head will stop
being his weak point like Muzan!

1918
01:50:21,945 --> 01:50:23,945
This battle isn't over yet.

1919
01:50:24,180 --> 01:50:26,059
I have to fight...

1920
01:50:26,905 --> 01:50:27,905
Tanjiro!

1921
01:50:28,080 --> 01:50:29,516
He's fainted.

1922
01:50:29,733 --> 01:50:31,083
Of course he has.

1923
01:50:31,300 --> 01:50:33,738
He's long since
passed his limit.

1924
01:50:38,570 --> 01:50:40,268
[grunts]

1925
01:50:43,359 --> 01:50:46,537
Water Breathing, Fourth Form:

1926
01:50:46,754 --> 01:50:49,018
[♪ epic music playing]

1927
01:50:49,235 --> 01:50:50,890
Striking Tide!

1928
01:50:55,852 --> 01:50:57,463
Ridiculous!

1929
01:50:57,680 --> 01:51:00,554
He lost his head and can still
regenerate that quickly?

1930
01:51:01,294 --> 01:51:03,427
[sword clanking]

1931
01:51:04,559 --> 01:51:06,691
[grunting]

1932
01:51:13,309 --> 01:51:16,225
[yelling]

1933
01:51:20,621 --> 01:51:22,581
- [coughs]
- [blood splatters]

1934
01:51:24,931 --> 01:51:27,282
I can't hear out of my left ear,

1935
01:51:27,500 --> 01:51:29,415
and my right hand has gone numb.

1936
01:51:30,852 --> 01:51:34,378
I can still grip my sword,
but who knows for how long.

1937
01:51:43,085 --> 01:51:44,085
Wait!

1938
01:51:45,078 --> 01:51:46,111
I...

1939
01:51:46,706 --> 01:51:49,527
I'm here. I'm still alive!

1940
01:51:49,964 --> 01:51:53,985
If you wanna kill Tanjiro,
you'll have to defeat me first!

1941
01:51:58,140 --> 01:52:00,438
[AKAZA] An indomitable spirit.

1942
01:52:00,659 --> 01:52:02,029
It will never bend,

1943
01:52:02,207 --> 01:52:05,169
no matter what crisis
it finds itself in.

1944
01:52:05,964 --> 01:52:08,661
We don't fight the way
samurai do.

1945
01:52:08,881 --> 01:52:10,782
We don't carry weapons,

1946
01:52:11,003 --> 01:52:14,009
though we carry our convictions
like swords.

1947
01:52:15,556 --> 01:52:18,916
[MAN] Though we carry
our convictions like swords,

1948
01:52:19,623 --> 01:52:23,735
our battles are waged
with our fists.

1949
01:52:25,193 --> 01:52:28,332
[AKAZA] You are such an eyesore!

1950
01:52:31,161 --> 01:52:32,576
[soft thump]

1951
01:52:38,986 --> 01:52:40,576
[GIRL] Please stop.

1952
01:52:46,855 --> 01:52:47,855
[AKAZA] Who is that?

1953
01:52:53,459 --> 01:52:55,509
Mr. Hakuji,

1954
01:52:55,692 --> 01:52:57,423
please, that's enough!

1955
01:52:57,651 --> 01:52:59,064
[♪ poignant music playing]

1956
01:53:00,705 --> 01:53:03,505
[AKAZA] Let go.
Let go of my hand.

1957
01:53:05,125 --> 01:53:06,125
Just who are you?

1958
01:53:07,989 --> 01:53:11,401
Stop. You don't
have to keep going. [sniffles]

1959
01:53:11,629 --> 01:53:14,130
Let's leave this place together.

1960
01:53:14,494 --> 01:53:16,541
[AKAZA] I can't.

1961
01:53:16,723 --> 01:53:20,043
I've still got unfinished
business with those two.

1962
01:53:21,499 --> 01:53:23,592
[GIRL]
What do you mean by that?

1963
01:53:24,184 --> 01:53:25,800
[AKAZA]
I've got to become stronger.

1964
01:53:25,958 --> 01:53:26,958
I've got to!

1965
01:53:27,226 --> 01:53:29,445
I'll kill anyone
who gets in my way.

1966
01:53:30,062 --> 01:53:32,490
Why do you want that? [sniffles]

1967
01:53:32,645 --> 01:53:36,465
For what reason
do you need to become stronger?

1968
01:53:37,330 --> 01:53:39,678
[AKAZA] Because...
unless I'm strong enough,

1969
01:53:39,801 --> 01:53:41,581
I won't be able to bring
any more back home to him.

1970
01:53:42,792 --> 01:53:44,103
He needs medicine.

1971
01:53:45,264 --> 01:53:46,871
I must become stronger.

1972
01:53:47,291 --> 01:53:48,304
[grunts angrily]

1973
01:53:48,305 --> 01:53:50,110
If I don't, I won't be able to
get away with the money I stole.

1974
01:53:50,876 --> 01:53:51,889
If I happen to be caught,

1975
01:53:52,013 --> 01:53:53,249
I won't be able
to defend myself.

1976
01:53:54,065 --> 01:53:55,964
If I'm not strong enough,

1977
01:53:56,312 --> 01:54:01,842
the magistrate will catch me
and have me beaten and lashed.

1978
01:54:02,611 --> 01:54:05,970
[whipping]

1979
01:54:07,370 --> 01:54:09,679
[MAGISTRATE]
We've already given you

1980
01:54:10,030 --> 01:54:14,368
three tattoos on each arm
for stealing.

1981
01:54:14,719 --> 01:54:18,567
Next time,
we'll chop off your hand.

1982
01:54:18,917 --> 01:54:21,086
[Hakuji chuckling]

1983
01:54:25,426 --> 01:54:28,645
[laughing]

1984
01:54:31,443 --> 01:54:34,733
[ATTENDANT]
Bow your head and repent!

1985
01:54:35,084 --> 01:54:36,245
If you're gonna chop it off,
then do it!

1986
01:54:36,467 --> 01:54:39,220
Go ahead and take both of them
if you're really serious.

1987
01:54:39,443 --> 01:54:41,486
I'll just use my feet to steal.

1988
01:54:41,707 --> 01:54:44,551
You're not gonna catch me again,
so make it count!

1989
01:54:47,081 --> 01:54:50,591
[MAGISTRATE] To hear this from
someone at such a young age.

1990
01:54:50,813 --> 01:54:53,344
This boy of 11 has already
taken on punishments

1991
01:54:53,522 --> 01:54:55,832
that would make
a grown man faint.

1992
01:54:57,119 --> 01:54:59,119
You are a demon child!

1993
01:54:59,340 --> 01:55:01,383
Go and call me
whatever names you want.

1994
01:55:01,606 --> 01:55:04,138
"Demon child" suits me
just damn fine!

1995
01:55:04,359 --> 01:55:06,491
They say I already had teeth
when I was born,

1996
01:55:06,713 --> 01:55:07,734
so I guess I am.

1997
01:55:07,735 --> 01:55:09,823
- Be quiet!
- Dirty little punk!

1998
01:55:10,044 --> 01:55:13,020
[HAKUJI] Don't you mean
"demon child," you bastard?

1999
01:55:13,243 --> 01:55:15,375
[grunts]

2000
01:55:16,884 --> 01:55:17,950
Hmph!

2001
01:55:18,128 --> 01:55:21,548
SOUTH TOWN MAGISTRATE'S OFFICE

2002
01:55:21,770 --> 01:55:22,770
[birds calling]

2003
01:55:22,925 --> 01:55:23,924
[MAN 1] Hakuji!

2004
01:55:23,925 --> 01:55:25,827
[MAN 2] Oh! [panting]
There you are!

2005
01:55:26,030 --> 01:55:28,175
[voice breaking] When you were
caught for stealing again,

2006
01:55:28,378 --> 01:55:31,212
word about it made its way
back to your father.

2007
01:55:31,698 --> 01:55:34,046
He hung himself, Hakuji!

2008
01:55:34,451 --> 01:55:35,544
Huh?

2009
01:55:38,419 --> 01:55:40,524
[Hakuji's father weakly]
"Dear Hakuji,

2010
01:55:41,577 --> 01:55:43,521
live an honest life.

2011
01:55:44,087 --> 01:55:46,153
You can still start over."

2012
01:55:46,881 --> 01:55:48,906
- [wind blowing]
- [leaves rustling]

2013
01:55:50,728 --> 01:55:51,728
[♪ poignant music continues]

2014
01:55:51,862 --> 01:55:52,914
[paper fluttering]

2015
01:55:53,117 --> 01:55:55,101
[HAKUJI]
What kind of world is this?

2016
01:55:55,304 --> 01:55:58,025
Are the poor
not even allowed to live?

2017
01:57:07,695 --> 01:57:09,514
[voice breaking] Dad.

2018
01:57:10,636 --> 01:57:11,694
To hell with this rotten world.

2019
01:57:11,802 --> 01:57:12,802
To all of it![sobbing]

2020
01:57:14,048 --> 01:57:16,142
Every rotten human,
they can all burn in hell!

2021
01:57:16,250 --> 01:57:17,265
[grunts angrily]

2022
01:57:18,085 --> 01:57:19,769
Why do scumbags like them
get the privilege of living

2023
01:57:19,877 --> 01:57:21,410
when my father had to die
in such a horrible way?

2024
01:57:21,518 --> 01:57:22,727
He was never a burden to me.

2025
01:57:22,814 --> 01:57:23,814
So why would he feel that way?

2026
01:57:24,001 --> 01:57:25,663
You didn't do anything wrong,
Dad. You didn't!

2027
01:57:26,656 --> 01:57:27,779
I never cared
about getting beaten

2028
01:57:27,780 --> 01:57:28,779
after I was caught stealing.

2029
01:57:28,780 --> 01:57:30,651
Even if they beat me until every
bone in my body was broken,

2030
01:57:30,737 --> 01:57:31,736
I could take it all
for you, Dad.

2031
01:57:31,737 --> 01:57:32,485
For centuries even.

2032
01:57:32,486 --> 01:57:33,717
Learn your lesson!
Live an honest life!

2033
01:57:34,105 --> 01:57:35,594
[HAKUJI] Why don't you
shut the hell up, you scumbag?

2034
01:57:35,595 --> 01:57:36,594
Medicine's expensive.

2035
01:57:36,595 --> 01:57:37,927
The hell do you expect me
to do about that?

2036
01:57:38,640 --> 01:57:40,453
My dad's only getting thinner
and thinner by the day.

2037
01:57:40,993 --> 01:57:42,526
He's so malnourished,
you can see his bones.

2038
01:57:42,807 --> 01:57:44,491
I just want him to have
something better to eat.

2039
01:57:45,592 --> 01:57:46,952
I would have happily
given my life...

2040
01:57:47,902 --> 01:57:49,003
[voice breaking]
...if it meant saving his.

2041
01:57:52,026 --> 01:57:54,013
I'd have done anything...
for my father!

2042
01:57:55,459 --> 01:57:56,539
[breathing heavily]

2043
01:57:56,646 --> 01:57:57,984
- [clapping]
- Huh?

2044
01:57:57,985 --> 01:57:58,718
SORYU

2045
01:57:58,719 --> 01:57:59,711
[MAN] Well, well.
I am quite impressed.

2046
01:57:59,712 --> 01:58:00,920
I was called over
because someone said that

2047
01:58:00,921 --> 01:58:01,806
a child was about to be killed.

2048
01:58:01,807 --> 01:58:03,383
But you've laid out seven
grown-ups with your bare fists.

2049
01:58:03,469 --> 01:58:04,549
You've got some talent,
don't ya?

2050
01:58:04,657 --> 01:58:06,427
Not just anyone can take on
that many guys and still win.

2051
01:58:06,535 --> 01:58:07,766
[chuckling] That's the kind of
spunk I like to see.

2052
01:58:08,867 --> 01:58:09,903
[AKAZA] What's going on here?

2053
01:58:10,011 --> 01:58:11,011
Who is this man?

2054
01:58:11,415 --> 01:58:12,634
Could these be my memories?

2055
01:58:12,986 --> 01:58:15,943
How about you join my dojo?

2056
01:58:16,295 --> 01:58:17,375
I don't have any students
at the moment.

2057
01:58:17,841 --> 01:58:19,988
Stay out of my way,
you old fart!

2058
01:58:20,221 --> 01:58:21,621
You lookin' to die?

2059
01:58:21,855 --> 01:58:23,115
- Those tattoos.
- Uh?

2060
01:58:23,337 --> 01:58:24,801
You're a criminal from Edo.

2061
01:58:25,510 --> 01:58:27,419
I'm guessing
after being thrown out,

2062
01:58:27,641 --> 01:58:30,170
you eventually
found your way here.

2063
01:58:30,392 --> 01:58:32,256
I never asked for your opinion.

2064
01:58:32,477 --> 01:58:34,785
Now shut up
and get the hell out of my way!

2065
01:58:35,007 --> 01:58:38,512
[scoffs] All right.
Time to be reborn!

2066
01:58:39,400 --> 01:58:40,953
You ready?

2067
01:58:41,884 --> 01:58:46,278
That's it. Drop dead, old man!
[grunting]

2068
01:58:47,032 --> 01:58:48,319
[impact grunts]

2069
01:58:56,705 --> 01:58:59,234
[strained grunt, coughs, gasps]

2070
01:58:59,412 --> 01:59:00,610
[body thuds]

2071
01:59:04,382 --> 01:59:05,712
SORYU

2072
01:59:05,935 --> 01:59:07,753
[MAN] I'll give it to you.
You're tough.

2073
01:59:07,754 --> 01:59:08,776
DOJO

2074
01:59:08,952 --> 01:59:10,505
After that beating I gave you,

2075
01:59:10,683 --> 01:59:12,679
you came to
in less than an hour.

2076
01:59:13,745 --> 01:59:14,745
The name's Keizo.

2077
01:59:15,398 --> 01:59:17,315
I teach
the Soryu style of fighting

2078
01:59:17,533 --> 01:59:19,841
which uses only your bare hands.

2079
01:59:20,060 --> 01:59:23,021
Like I said, I don't have
any other students.

2080
01:59:23,501 --> 01:59:27,204
So I get by by doing whatever
odd jobs I can for people.

2081
01:59:29,818 --> 01:59:32,519
I have a daughter
who's in rather poor health.

2082
01:59:32,737 --> 01:59:34,958
I'd like you
to help look after her.

2083
01:59:35,437 --> 01:59:38,879
I'd be here if I could,
but I have to work.

2084
01:59:39,881 --> 01:59:42,321
My wife was pushed
to the edge of exhaustion

2085
01:59:42,538 --> 01:59:43,846
and drowned herself.

2086
01:59:44,847 --> 01:59:47,374
Life sure takes a bite
out of you, doesn't it?

2087
01:59:51,513 --> 01:59:53,473
If I were a more capable man,

2088
01:59:53,691 --> 01:59:56,261
my wife and daughter wouldn't
have suffered like this.

2089
01:59:59,267 --> 02:00:01,620
You said you knew
I was a criminal.

2090
02:00:01,837 --> 02:00:04,887
Are you really all right leaving
your daughter around me?

2091
02:00:06,281 --> 02:00:07,849
Why wouldn't I be?

2092
02:00:08,067 --> 02:00:10,637
I pummeled the criminal
out of you earlier, didn't I?

2093
02:00:10,855 --> 02:00:11,855
It's fine.

2094
02:00:12,729 --> 02:00:14,956
[♪ tender music playing]

2095
02:00:15,175 --> 02:00:17,140
[AKAZA] They are alike.

2096
02:00:24,786 --> 02:00:26,664
I get it now.

2097
02:00:27,975 --> 02:00:30,640
The reason
you disgusted me earlier.

2098
02:00:31,164 --> 02:00:32,562
It was because you would've

2099
02:00:32,563 --> 02:00:35,533
dredged up memories
of my worthless past.

2100
02:00:40,514 --> 02:00:42,214
[KEIZO]
This is my daughter, Koyuki.

2101
02:00:42,924 --> 02:00:44,439
[coughing]

2102
02:00:45,480 --> 02:00:48,321
[AKAZA] My worthless past.

2103
02:00:51,682 --> 02:00:53,243
Worthless.

2104
02:00:57,740 --> 02:01:00,817
[coughing]

2105
02:01:03,184 --> 02:01:05,304
Hakuji, I'm so sorry.

2106
02:01:06,240 --> 02:01:08,625
[chuckles] How are you feeling?

2107
02:01:08,859 --> 02:01:10,824
[coughing]

2108
02:01:11,057 --> 02:01:12,695
You okay being up?

2109
02:01:13,771 --> 02:01:15,501
[KOYUKI] Hmm.

2110
02:01:15,735 --> 02:01:19,150
Looks like you've got more color
in your cheeks this morning.

2111
02:01:19,383 --> 02:01:21,114
[chuckles] That's good.

2112
02:01:21,816 --> 02:01:22,985
Hmm.

2113
02:01:23,594 --> 02:01:25,075
- Huh?
- Oh, yeah. This boy.

2114
02:01:26,214 --> 02:01:27,815
His name is... [chuckles]

2115
02:01:28,038 --> 02:01:31,203
Well, I've asked him countless
times, and he won't say.

2116
02:01:31,382 --> 02:01:33,388
- Go on, get inside.
- [grunts]

2117
02:01:35,171 --> 02:01:36,465
Have a seat.

2118
02:01:38,247 --> 02:01:41,324
I wanna know his name
when I get back. Okay?

2119
02:01:53,184 --> 02:01:54,184
Um...

2120
02:01:54,621 --> 02:01:57,681
Your... Your face.

2121
02:01:58,293 --> 02:01:59,692
You're hurt.

2122
02:02:00,303 --> 02:02:02,009
Are you all right?

2123
02:02:05,113 --> 02:02:07,123
[AKAZA] "I'll make you better.

2124
02:02:07,341 --> 02:02:08,959
I'll save you.

2125
02:02:09,177 --> 02:02:10,751
Protect you."

2126
02:02:11,013 --> 02:02:15,604
In that past life, all I did
was spew a bunch of lies.

2127
02:02:16,041 --> 02:02:17,746
I was so pathetic.

2128
02:02:19,669 --> 02:02:22,117
[birds chirping]

2129
02:02:27,275 --> 02:02:29,723
[coughing]

2130
02:02:34,445 --> 02:02:35,445
Oh, thank you.

2131
02:02:36,943 --> 02:02:39,639
[HAKUJI] You don't have to
thank me every time, you know.

2132
02:02:39,853 --> 02:02:41,394
Just focus on resting.

2133
02:02:43,107 --> 02:02:46,959
I'm sorry for causing you
trouble like this.

2134
02:02:47,130 --> 02:02:49,057
It's fine. Really.

2135
02:02:50,898 --> 02:02:53,637
Koyuki, you want this closed?

2136
02:02:54,408 --> 02:02:57,790
Hmm. You can leave it open.

2137
02:02:59,673 --> 02:03:02,412
[HAKUJI] Koyuki was very
delicate and frail.

2138
02:03:03,783 --> 02:03:07,592
I would change out her towels
and nightgown and give her water

2139
02:03:07,764 --> 02:03:09,219
even throughout the night.

2140
02:03:09,776 --> 02:03:12,558
And whenever she needed
to use the lavatory,

2141
02:03:12,729 --> 02:03:14,870
obviously she was too weak
to be able to go

2142
02:03:15,084 --> 02:03:17,352
without needing assistance.

2143
02:03:20,349 --> 02:03:23,517
I was used to taking care
of the sick because of my dad,

2144
02:03:23,731 --> 02:03:27,241
and since I had an almost
inhuman physical endurance,

2145
02:03:27,412 --> 02:03:29,467
it really wasn't a big deal
for me.

2146
02:03:31,993 --> 02:03:34,348
[crows cawing]

2147
02:03:34,561 --> 02:03:36,830
Sorry to make you help me
all day.

2148
02:03:43,294 --> 02:03:46,077
[HAKUJI] Why do people
who are suffering from illness

2149
02:03:46,290 --> 02:03:48,516
always feel the need to say
they're sorry?

2150
02:03:49,373 --> 02:03:51,770
"Sorry to make you
do things for me."

2151
02:03:52,283 --> 02:03:54,851
"Sorry if my coughing's
bothering you."

2152
02:03:55,451 --> 02:03:58,533
"Sorry I can't put food
on the table like I should."

2153
02:04:00,588 --> 02:04:03,414
They didn't choose
to have to live this way.

2154
02:04:03,627 --> 02:04:05,639
Of course
they wanna breathe normally.

2155
02:04:05,811 --> 02:04:07,994
They can't help it
if they start coughing.

2156
02:04:09,235 --> 02:04:10,691
Out of everyone,

2157
02:04:10,905 --> 02:04:12,705
they're the ones
suffering the most.

2158
02:04:19,916 --> 02:04:26,440
Sorry again to make you do this.

2159
02:04:27,813 --> 02:04:32,621
Because of my sickness,

2160
02:04:33,194 --> 02:04:39,374
you're not able to do
your training,

2161
02:04:39,945 --> 02:04:45,554
or even go out and have fun.

2162
02:04:47,958 --> 02:04:53,223
[HAKUJI]
I don't care about having fun.

2163
02:04:53,681 --> 02:04:57,573
I never have.

2164
02:04:58,833 --> 02:05:05,833
As far as training goes,
I squeeze it in whenever I can,

2165
02:05:07,759 --> 02:05:11,306
so, it's fine.

2166
02:05:14,628 --> 02:05:17,602
Are you sure?

2167
02:05:19,320 --> 02:05:26,320
Even you need to take
a little break.

2168
02:05:29,505 --> 02:05:36,505
I hear there are fireworks
happening tonight.

2169
02:05:39,349 --> 02:05:43,357
You should go see them.

2170
02:05:46,789 --> 02:05:51,483
Fireworks, huh?

2171
02:05:52,054 --> 02:05:58,121
If you don't feel nauseous
at night,

2172
02:05:58,692 --> 02:06:05,692
I could carry you on my back
and go see them on the bridge.

2173
02:06:07,965 --> 02:06:08,965
Huh?

2174
02:06:10,134 --> 02:06:11,134
If you're not feeling up to it,

2175
02:06:11,322 --> 02:06:12,615
they'll do fireworks again
next year, and after that.

2176
02:06:12,710 --> 02:06:13,710
So, we can just go
when you're better.

2177
02:06:15,733 --> 02:06:16,733
[crying softly]

2178
02:06:17,350 --> 02:06:18,432
There was one thing
that was hard

2179
02:06:18,433 --> 02:06:19,307
about taking care of her.

2180
02:06:19,308 --> 02:06:20,429
And that was whenever she would
suddenly break out into tears

2181
02:06:20,525 --> 02:06:21,524
in the middle
of our conversations.

2182
02:06:21,525 --> 02:06:23,338
I can imagine how she felt,
bedridden and sick as she was,

2183
02:06:23,528 --> 02:06:24,592
but it still made me
uncomfortable.

2184
02:06:24,593 --> 02:06:25,258
[insects trilling]

2185
02:06:25,259 --> 02:06:26,304
SORYU

2186
02:06:29,670 --> 02:06:30,670
[impact grunts, wheezes]

2187
02:06:30,849 --> 02:06:32,083
[sighs] Ah, now I understand.

2188
02:06:32,084 --> 02:06:33,111
The symbol used for Hakuji,

2189
02:06:33,112 --> 02:06:33,889
it's the same as komainu.

2190
02:06:33,890 --> 02:06:34,821
[chuckles] That makes sense.

2191
02:06:34,822 --> 02:06:35,772
You and I really are the same,
after all.

2192
02:06:35,773 --> 02:06:37,103
We only thrive when we have
something to protect.

2193
02:06:37,104 --> 02:06:37,844
Just like the komainu

2194
02:06:37,845 --> 02:06:38,948
who protect the entrance
to the shrines. [chuckles]

2195
02:06:39,157 --> 02:06:40,156
[laughs heartily]

2196
02:06:40,157 --> 02:06:41,115
[♪ gentle music playing]

2197
02:06:41,116 --> 02:06:42,351
[HAKUJI] There was a story as to
how my master owned this land,

2198
02:06:42,446 --> 02:06:43,758
even though he wasn't a samurai
or anything like that.

2199
02:06:43,853 --> 02:06:45,298
He had rescued an elderly man
from a group of bandits.

2200
02:06:45,545 --> 02:06:46,544
The old man,
who had no living heirs,

2201
02:06:46,545 --> 02:06:47,544
was so impressed
by his Soryu technique

2202
02:06:47,545 --> 02:06:48,491
that he left him
not only his land,

2203
02:06:48,492 --> 02:06:49,492
but the dojo that lay upon it.

2204
02:06:50,641 --> 02:06:52,010
However, there were those
with envious eyes

2205
02:06:52,105 --> 02:06:53,341
who wished to have the land
and dojo all to themselves.

2206
02:06:53,645 --> 02:06:54,710
The Kenjutsu Dojo next door

2207
02:06:54,805 --> 02:06:55,926
started harassing
the Soryu Dojo.

2208
02:06:56,706 --> 02:06:58,037
Because of that,
the Soryu Dojo had a hard time

2209
02:06:58,132 --> 02:06:59,132
keeping any students.

2210
02:07:01,935 --> 02:07:06,035
But now, thanks to my training
here and caring for Koyuki...

2211
02:07:07,286 --> 02:07:10,547
...my heart has finally
found salvation.

2212
02:07:11,620 --> 02:07:13,853
[effort grunting]

2213
02:07:24,486 --> 02:07:27,033
[chuckles]

2214
02:07:30,205 --> 02:07:33,785
Three short years went by
and I turned 18.

2215
02:07:35,385 --> 02:07:36,565
Koyuki was 16.

2216
02:07:36,910 --> 02:07:38,859
She was almost never
bedridden anymore

2217
02:07:39,016 --> 02:07:40,713
and was now able
to live a normal life.

2218
02:07:41,562 --> 02:07:42,599
[chuckles]

2219
02:07:43,039 --> 02:07:44,038
[birds chirping]

2220
02:07:44,039 --> 02:07:45,366
Hakuji! Come here.

2221
02:07:45,931 --> 02:07:46,930
Yes, sir.

2222
02:07:46,931 --> 02:07:48,068
[insects trilling]

2223
02:07:48,195 --> 02:07:49,262
This dojo,

2224
02:07:49,263 --> 02:07:51,243
would you be willing
to take it over for me, Hakuji?

2225
02:07:51,746 --> 02:07:54,167
Koyuki's told me that
she's quite fond of you as well.

2226
02:07:54,858 --> 02:07:55,858
[exclaims in surprise]

2227
02:08:01,239 --> 02:08:03,502
[HAKUJI] As someone branded
with the tattoos of a criminal,

2228
02:08:03,659 --> 02:08:06,048
picturing any kind of future
for myself was hard enough.

2229
02:08:06,991 --> 02:08:10,134
But a future in which someone
could like a person like me?

2230
02:08:10,291 --> 02:08:11,643
I couldn't have even dreamed it.

2231
02:08:13,057 --> 02:08:14,944
My dad asked me
to lead an honest life,

2232
02:08:15,100 --> 02:08:16,484
something I never thought
was possible.

2233
02:08:16,861 --> 02:08:18,496
But perhaps it really is.

2234
02:08:19,533 --> 02:08:21,450
The faint hope
of being able to start over

2235
02:08:21,607 --> 02:08:23,085
began to swell within me

2236
02:08:23,241 --> 02:08:25,128
until it felt like
it was about to burst.

2237
02:08:28,806 --> 02:08:29,874
[♪ tender music playing]

2238
02:08:30,031 --> 02:08:31,791
But I could never have predicted
in that moment

2239
02:08:31,949 --> 02:08:33,237
that the two people
I wanted to protect

2240
02:08:33,395 --> 02:08:34,966
more than anything else
in this life...

2241
02:08:35,689 --> 02:08:37,512
...would end up
meeting the fate they did.

2242
02:08:41,064 --> 02:08:43,421
I had made a trip to Edo
to visit my dad's grave.

2243
02:08:43,988 --> 02:08:46,219
I wanted to let him know
that I was getting married.

2244
02:08:53,291 --> 02:08:56,089
I returned before even a full
day and night had passed.

2245
02:08:58,194 --> 02:09:00,269
Yet a sense of dread
came over me.

2246
02:09:00,992 --> 02:09:02,752
My chest started to feel tight

2247
02:09:02,910 --> 02:09:05,047
and a terrible feeling of nausea
overtook me.

2248
02:09:05,550 --> 02:09:06,550
[retches]

2249
02:09:06,870 --> 02:09:08,662
[MAN] Someone put poison
in the well!

2250
02:09:09,259 --> 02:09:10,391
[voice breaking]
The other school was so angry

2251
02:09:10,548 --> 02:09:11,805
they couldn't beat you
or Mr. Keizo,

2252
02:09:11,962 --> 02:09:13,440
they went and did this
out of spite!

2253
02:09:13,566 --> 02:09:15,294
It's atrocious. Unthinkable!

2254
02:09:15,451 --> 02:09:17,055
They even killed Koyuki!

2255
02:09:19,255 --> 02:09:20,542
[HAKUJI] Why?

2256
02:09:20,543 --> 02:09:22,932
Why is it whenever the ones I
care about are in mortal peril,

2257
02:09:23,090 --> 02:09:24,598
I'm never there for them?

2258
02:09:28,496 --> 02:09:29,496
[fireworks bursting in distance]

2259
02:09:29,910 --> 02:09:30,979
[crickets chirping]

2260
02:09:31,136 --> 02:09:33,242
I had even gone
and made a promise to her.

2261
02:09:34,751 --> 02:09:36,637
Are you sure
that I'm the one for you?

2262
02:09:38,146 --> 02:09:39,309
When we were children,

2263
02:09:39,623 --> 02:09:41,446
do you remember
when you talked to me

2264
02:09:41,603 --> 02:09:42,892
about seeing the fireworks?

2265
02:09:43,332 --> 02:09:46,476
- Huh? Uh... no, not really.
- [giggles softly]

2266
02:09:47,387 --> 02:09:49,336
Because of those little talks
we used to have,

2267
02:09:49,493 --> 02:09:51,285
there were a lot of things
which I took with me

2268
02:09:51,442 --> 02:09:52,825
that gave me hope
for the future.

2269
02:09:53,705 --> 02:09:56,188
You said even if we couldn't see
the fireworks that year,

2270
02:09:56,346 --> 02:09:58,734
we could go to the one
happening next year,

2271
02:09:58,891 --> 02:09:59,991
or the year after that.

2272
02:10:00,495 --> 02:10:02,852
The truth is,
I could never imagine a future

2273
02:10:03,009 --> 02:10:04,612
where I'd still be alive
a year later,

2274
02:10:04,770 --> 02:10:06,655
and certainly not
any longer than that.

2275
02:10:07,504 --> 02:10:09,076
My mother couldn't either.

2276
02:10:09,201 --> 02:10:11,339
I think that's why she ended up
taking her own life,

2277
02:10:11,716 --> 02:10:13,476
'cause she didn't
want to see me die.

2278
02:10:13,634 --> 02:10:14,827
Not just her.

2279
02:10:14,954 --> 02:10:16,902
I could tell my father
had given up hope, too,

2280
02:10:17,060 --> 02:10:18,191
deep down inside.

2281
02:10:19,008 --> 02:10:20,675
Because I was just so weak.

2282
02:10:21,649 --> 02:10:23,535
But you never treated me
that way.

2283
02:10:23,660 --> 02:10:25,483
You were able to see
a future for me.

2284
02:10:26,080 --> 02:10:28,627
You talked to me about
doing things as if...

2285
02:10:28,753 --> 02:10:30,859
As if it were obvious
that I'd still be here.

2286
02:10:31,015 --> 02:10:33,247
[crying softly]
That made me so very happy.

2287
02:10:41,451 --> 02:10:43,683
So, yes, I am sure
you're the one for me.

2288
02:10:45,160 --> 02:10:46,160
Would you...

2289
02:10:46,543 --> 02:10:48,083
Would you be my husband?

2290
02:10:48,366 --> 02:10:49,366
[distant explosion]

2291
02:10:52,944 --> 02:10:53,944
[fireworks bursting]

2292
02:10:54,056 --> 02:10:55,056
Yes.

2293
02:10:55,187 --> 02:10:57,073
I promise to become stronger
than anyone,

2294
02:10:57,545 --> 02:10:59,368
and protect you
for the rest of my life.

2295
02:11:00,373 --> 02:11:01,373
[exclaims]

2296
02:11:02,606 --> 02:11:04,994
[HAKUJI]
In the end, I was all talk.

2297
02:11:05,371 --> 02:11:07,635
I wasn't able to fulfill
any of my promises.

2298
02:11:08,012 --> 02:11:09,018
[chuckles]

2299
02:11:13,104 --> 02:11:14,676
[♪ foreboding music playing]

2300
02:11:16,687 --> 02:11:18,605
What do you want? [gasps]

2301
02:11:19,013 --> 02:11:20,239
You've got some nerve.

2302
02:11:20,396 --> 02:11:22,282
Wait. You're from the Soryu--

2303
02:11:22,911 --> 02:11:24,231
[screaming]

2304
02:11:24,357 --> 02:11:25,425
[♪ somber music playing]

2305
02:11:28,286 --> 02:11:29,575
[man grunts]

2306
02:11:31,806 --> 02:11:33,944
[Hakuji grunts, yells]

2307
02:11:34,101 --> 02:11:35,421
[groans angrily]

2308
02:11:39,161 --> 02:11:41,393
The family, the Soryu Dojo,
were recently poisoned.

2309
02:11:41,551 --> 02:11:43,091
And we believe
that a student of theirs

2310
02:11:43,217 --> 02:11:45,071
retaliated against
the Kenjutsu Dojo.

2311
02:11:45,228 --> 02:11:47,114
Sixty-seven people
were murdered inside.

2312
02:11:47,271 --> 02:11:49,063
He shattered their skulls
and crushed their organs,

2313
02:11:49,220 --> 02:11:50,220
all barehanded.

2314
02:11:50,509 --> 02:11:51,577
Not only were most of the bodies

2315
02:11:51,735 --> 02:11:53,401
mangled and mutilated
beyond recognition,

2316
02:11:53,558 --> 02:11:55,789
most had limbs missing
that we couldn't even locate.

2317
02:11:55,947 --> 02:11:57,518
Organs, limbs, brain matter,

2318
02:11:57,644 --> 02:11:58,996
even jaws and eyeballs
were found

2319
02:11:59,153 --> 02:12:01,290
strewn across the walls
and the ceiling of the premises.

2320
02:12:01,888 --> 02:12:04,057
This killer
was no ordinary human.

2321
02:12:05,062 --> 02:12:06,728
[wet squelching]

2322
02:12:07,702 --> 02:12:09,966
[breathing shakily]

2323
02:12:20,841 --> 02:12:22,382
[MUZAN] I heard
there was some commotion

2324
02:12:22,538 --> 02:12:23,765
about a demon sighting here,

2325
02:12:23,922 --> 02:12:25,619
even though I know
I never sent one.

2326
02:12:25,997 --> 02:12:28,071
So, I decided to come
see for myself.

2327
02:12:28,228 --> 02:12:29,674
Yet all I find is a human.

2328
02:12:30,083 --> 02:12:31,686
How utterly disappointing.

2329
02:12:32,471 --> 02:12:34,735
[HAKUJI] Move, or I'll kill you!

2330
02:12:35,583 --> 02:12:37,281
- [thuds]
- [splatters]

2331
02:12:38,287 --> 02:12:39,292
It just so happens

2332
02:12:39,449 --> 02:12:41,901
I was contemplating
creating 12 powerful demons.

2333
02:12:42,341 --> 02:12:43,945
I wonder if you'll be
able to withstand

2334
02:12:44,101 --> 02:12:45,799
the amount of blood
I'm about to give you.

2335
02:12:47,245 --> 02:12:48,245
You... [grunts]

2336
02:12:56,655 --> 02:13:03,655
...do whatever you want.

2337
02:13:24,871 --> 02:13:31,871
None of it matters.

2338
02:14:18,598 --> 02:14:25,598
[thunder rumbling]

2339
02:14:32,706 --> 02:14:39,706
[♪ somber music playing]

2340
02:14:49,801 --> 02:14:56,801
[grunting]

2341
02:15:12,594 --> 02:15:14,951
[AKAZA] After becoming a demon,
I lost my memories...

2342
02:15:15,423 --> 02:15:17,815
and once again,
started to seek out power.

2343
02:15:18,256 --> 02:15:19,621
- [thuds]
- [grunts]

2344
02:15:19,840 --> 02:15:21,030
- [flesh squelches]
- [grunts]

2345
02:15:27,987 --> 02:15:29,440
[clangs]

2346
02:15:30,321 --> 02:15:32,126
- [wet squelching]
- [sword clatters]

2347
02:15:33,227 --> 02:15:34,944
It's not enough!

2348
02:15:35,165 --> 02:15:36,838
It will never be enough!

2349
02:15:37,058 --> 02:15:38,776
[thunderclap]

2350
02:15:40,890 --> 02:15:44,192
Even though I had nothing
left to my name.

2351
02:15:44,368 --> 02:15:47,495
Even though I had nothing
worth fighting for anymore.

2352
02:15:49,784 --> 02:15:52,955
Even though my family
was no longer around

2353
02:15:53,175 --> 02:15:56,962
and I had no desire
to live in a world without them.

2354
02:15:59,517 --> 02:16:02,996
For over a century,
I committed senseless massacres

2355
02:16:03,215 --> 02:16:04,889
over and over again.

2356
02:16:05,813 --> 02:16:09,072
Thinking about it now,
it's pathetic.

2357
02:16:09,292 --> 02:16:10,789
It's absurd.

2358
02:16:11,671 --> 02:16:14,489
All those deaths
were meaningless.

2359
02:16:19,949 --> 02:16:22,063
Even if I died now,

2360
02:16:22,282 --> 02:16:25,673
I couldn't go where the other
three were waiting for me.

2361
02:16:26,863 --> 02:16:31,838
Damn you for dredging up
these memories. You bastard!

2362
02:16:33,732 --> 02:16:35,670
Pathetic humans,

2363
02:16:35,889 --> 02:16:39,060
clinging on to life
with their fragile bodies!

2364
02:16:40,206 --> 02:16:44,036
Even their strongest
eventually die

2365
02:16:44,212 --> 02:16:46,414
and vanish into thin air!

2366
02:16:47,075 --> 02:16:49,145
[flesh squelching]

2367
02:16:49,805 --> 02:16:51,324
[GIYU] He's still not dead?

2368
02:16:51,546 --> 02:16:53,222
You can't be serious.

2369
02:16:54,414 --> 02:16:57,149
I have to kill him
before it's too late.

2370
02:16:58,164 --> 02:17:02,400
If we let him regenerate,
there will be no stopping him.

2371
02:17:04,121 --> 02:17:05,577
- [loud thump]
- [gasps]

2372
02:17:07,562 --> 02:17:09,813
[grunts] I must have passed out.

2373
02:17:10,033 --> 02:17:11,313
What's going on?

2374
02:17:13,077 --> 02:17:17,093
His head's back!
But how is that even possible?!

2375
02:17:18,241 --> 02:17:20,359
I decapitated him!

2376
02:17:21,064 --> 02:17:23,447
[♪ intense music playing]

2377
02:17:26,579 --> 02:17:29,536
Destructive Death:
Annihilation Type.

2378
02:17:30,286 --> 02:17:32,448
Stop it!

2379
02:17:32,668 --> 02:17:35,272
[AKAZA] Seriously?
He can still move?

2380
02:17:35,493 --> 02:17:38,007
[TANJIRO] Mr. Giyu and I
are going to win!

2381
02:17:38,228 --> 02:17:42,023
Akaza, I'll behead you
as many times as it takes!

2382
02:17:44,935 --> 02:17:46,479
My sword!

2383
02:17:47,759 --> 02:17:50,230
[GIYU] It slipped
out of his hands.

2384
02:17:51,245 --> 02:17:52,877
[TANJIRO] I lost my grip.

2385
02:17:55,216 --> 02:17:56,495
[effort grunts]

2386
02:18:02,143 --> 02:18:03,997
[KEIZO] All right, young man.

2387
02:18:04,791 --> 02:18:06,511
Time to be reborn.

2388
02:18:08,673 --> 02:18:09,794
[AKAZA] I despise
those who are weak.

2389
02:18:11,899 --> 02:18:16,066
Weaklings... Instead of
fighting you fair and square,

2390
02:18:16,285 --> 02:18:18,654
they always resort
to cheap tricks.

2391
02:18:19,444 --> 02:18:21,286
They're atrocious.

2392
02:18:21,769 --> 02:18:23,918
They have no patience.

2393
02:18:24,137 --> 02:18:26,243
And they quickly grow desperate.

2394
02:18:26,419 --> 02:18:28,875
Just thinking about them
makes me sick.

2395
02:18:30,937 --> 02:18:34,621
I killed people
with my fists for protection.

2396
02:18:35,192 --> 02:18:38,920
I desecrated my master's
beloved Soryu with blood.

2397
02:18:40,237 --> 02:18:43,394
And I couldn't follow
my father's last wishes!

2398
02:18:45,807 --> 02:18:47,387
That's right.

2399
02:18:47,913 --> 02:18:50,369
The one I wanted to kill...

2400
02:18:52,081 --> 02:18:53,660
[clatters]

2401
02:18:55,853 --> 02:18:58,616
[TANJIRO] This couldn't be
worse. I dropped my sword!

2402
02:18:58,792 --> 02:19:00,458
[♪ foreboding music playing]

2403
02:19:00,678 --> 02:19:03,047
My fists aren't enough
to stop him!

2404
02:19:13,574 --> 02:19:16,075
He's about to unleash
the Annihilation Type move

2405
02:19:16,295 --> 02:19:18,049
he used on Mr. Rengoku!

2406
02:19:21,164 --> 02:19:24,409
I've got to take Mr. Giyu
with me out of the attack range!

2407
02:19:28,665 --> 02:19:31,296
[GIYU] Leave me! Save yourself!

2408
02:19:36,955 --> 02:19:39,017
[AKAZA] I've got to kill...

2409
02:19:41,473 --> 02:19:43,097
...that weakling

2410
02:19:43,579 --> 02:19:45,772
I've come to hate!

2411
02:20:04,591 --> 02:20:06,784
[♪ dramatic music playing]

2412
02:20:12,311 --> 02:20:13,934
[thudding]

2413
02:20:16,873 --> 02:20:19,023
[grunts, gasps]

2414
02:20:19,594 --> 02:20:21,743
[flesh squelching]

2415
02:20:25,910 --> 02:20:27,095
[blood spurts]

2416
02:20:29,025 --> 02:20:31,481
[TANJIRO]
He just attacked himself.

2417
02:20:34,245 --> 02:20:36,570
Why would he turn on himself
like that?

2418
02:20:37,535 --> 02:20:38,535
Why?

2419
02:20:40,187 --> 02:20:42,063
[♪ melancholic music playing]

2420
02:20:42,286 --> 02:20:43,849
For a second,

2421
02:20:43,850 --> 02:20:46,708
I could pick up the scent
of gratitude from him.

2422
02:20:48,003 --> 02:20:49,003
Why did he smile at me?

2423
02:20:54,244 --> 02:20:55,904
[AKAZA] That's enough! Stop it!

2424
02:20:56,023 --> 02:20:57,584
I don't want to regenerate!

2425
02:20:58,004 --> 02:20:59,264
Don't you get it?

2426
02:20:59,385 --> 02:21:00,725
The battle is over!

2427
02:21:05,243 --> 02:21:07,545
In that decisive moment, I lost.

2428
02:21:07,735 --> 02:21:10,071
That technique
he beheaded me with

2429
02:21:10,308 --> 02:21:12,500
was nothing short of perfection.

2430
02:21:13,882 --> 02:21:18,696
He anticipated my movements
and pivoted at the last second,

2431
02:21:18,934 --> 02:21:22,604
then struck me down before
I could unleash my attack.

2432
02:21:23,605 --> 02:21:24,605
It's over now.

2433
02:21:25,320 --> 02:21:30,153
Let me accept my fate
and go to hell.

2434
02:21:33,331 --> 02:21:35,346
[TANJIRO]
Where's he trying to go?

2435
02:21:41,701 --> 02:21:44,789
[gasps softly]
He stopped in his tracks.

2436
02:21:47,833 --> 02:21:49,130
[HAKUJI] Dad.

2437
02:21:51,055 --> 02:21:52,154
Are you feeling better now?

2438
02:21:59,620 --> 02:22:06,620
Are you in pain anymore?

2439
02:22:42,673 --> 02:22:49,673
No need to worry, son. I'm fine.

2440
02:23:27,455 --> 02:23:30,215
Thank you, Hakuji.

2441
02:23:31,712 --> 02:23:32,508
I'm sorry, Father.

2442
02:23:32,509 --> 02:23:33,449
I'm sorry I couldn't start over
like you wanted.

2443
02:23:33,450 --> 02:23:34,449
I failed you.

2444
02:23:34,450 --> 02:23:35,330
[KEIZO] Do not despair.

2445
02:23:35,331 --> 02:23:35,973
Regardless of
who you grow up to be,

2446
02:23:35,974 --> 02:23:36,925
you're still my son
and still my student.

2447
02:23:36,926 --> 02:23:37,808
Heaven may not accept you...

2448
02:23:37,809 --> 02:23:38,301
...but you needn't worry.

2449
02:23:38,302 --> 02:23:39,301
Our hearts will be with you.

2450
02:23:39,302 --> 02:23:40,126
Master.

2451
02:23:40,127 --> 02:23:40,607
[gasps]

2452
02:23:40,608 --> 02:23:41,571
Didn't you say you were seeking
to become stronger than anyone?

2453
02:23:41,572 --> 02:23:42,834
Don't tell me you intend
to let it end like this, Akaza.

2454
02:23:43,150 --> 02:23:44,149
[AKAZA] That's right.
I can't die here.

2455
02:23:44,150 --> 02:23:45,139
I have to get stronger!

2456
02:23:45,140 --> 02:23:45,690
So what if I got beheaded?

2457
02:23:45,691 --> 02:23:46,539
Who cares
if I win or lose the fight?

2458
02:23:46,540 --> 02:23:47,445
If I kill those
who stand in my way...

2459
02:23:47,446 --> 02:23:48,446
then there's still hope
for me to get stronger!

2460
02:23:48,669 --> 02:23:49,315
I made a promise!

2461
02:23:49,316 --> 02:23:50,316
I'm not about to break it!

2462
02:23:51,146 --> 02:23:52,145
[breathing shakily]

2463
02:23:52,146 --> 02:23:52,584
[♪ tender music playing]

2464
02:23:52,585 --> 02:23:53,181
Mr. Hakuji,

2465
02:23:53,182 --> 02:23:53,800
thank you so much.

2466
02:23:53,801 --> 02:23:54,801
You've done more than enough.

2467
02:23:55,253 --> 02:23:55,957
It's okay.

2468
02:23:55,958 --> 02:23:56,462
We're all right now.

2469
02:23:56,463 --> 02:23:56,886
Akaza!

2470
02:23:56,887 --> 02:23:57,887
[♪ epic cinematic music playing]

2471
02:23:58,368 --> 02:23:59,367
[wailing]

2472
02:23:59,368 --> 02:23:59,892
Sorry!

2473
02:23:59,893 --> 02:24:00,730
I'm sorry
I couldn't protect you!

2474
02:24:00,731 --> 02:24:01,730
I wasn't there
when you needed me to be!

2475
02:24:01,731 --> 02:24:05,154
I couldn't keep
a single promise I made.

2476
02:24:05,369 --> 02:24:09,065
I'm sorry. [sobbing] Please
try to forgive me, Koyuki.

2477
02:24:09,237 --> 02:24:12,374
I'm so sorry.
[continues sobbing]

2478
02:24:15,254 --> 02:24:18,795
I'm so happy you remembered us.

2479
02:24:19,020 --> 02:24:21,631
I can't tell you
how happy that makes me.

2480
02:24:22,307 --> 02:24:25,683
And to see you now
as the man that I once knew,

2481
02:24:25,909 --> 02:24:27,574
I'm so grateful.

2482
02:24:36,128 --> 02:24:39,191
Welcome home, Hakuji.

2483
02:24:43,693 --> 02:24:45,538
Hey, Hakuji.

2484
02:24:45,944 --> 02:24:47,339
Welcome home.

2485
02:24:56,345 --> 02:24:57,345
[HAKUJI] I'm back now.

2486
02:24:57,846 --> 02:25:00,226
I'm finally back home.

2487
02:25:03,190 --> 02:25:04,860
Welcome back home...

2488
02:25:05,821 --> 02:25:07,283
...my darling.

2489
02:25:11,375 --> 02:25:12,460
[gasps softly]

2490
02:25:13,629 --> 02:25:15,717
[♪ gentle music playing]

2491
02:25:33,796 --> 02:25:35,424
[Tanjiro breathing shakily]

2492
02:25:35,634 --> 02:25:36,634
He vanished.

2493
02:25:39,734 --> 02:25:41,103
[gasps]

2494
02:25:42,379 --> 02:25:44,020
[inhales deeply]

2495
02:25:45,023 --> 02:25:46,573
[exhales sharply]

2496
02:25:48,534 --> 02:25:50,859
It's over. Right?

2497
02:25:55,191 --> 02:25:56,650
Gotta hurry...

2498
02:25:57,699 --> 02:26:01,300
...and get to where
Ms. Tamayo is.

2499
02:26:02,303 --> 02:26:03,580
And then...

2500
02:26:10,875 --> 02:26:11,875
[grunts weakly] Tanjiro.

2501
02:26:17,807 --> 02:26:18,934
[exhales]

2502
02:26:21,185 --> 02:26:24,087
[Kasugai Crow cawing]

2503
02:26:24,910 --> 02:26:29,717
Tanjiro! Giyu!
Have defeated Upper Three!

2504
02:26:29,933 --> 02:26:33,701
They are unable to stay
conscious due to exhaustion!

2505
02:26:33,917 --> 02:26:35,303
They've passed out!

2506
02:26:40,674 --> 02:26:46,564
Tanjiro! Giyu!
Have defeated Upper Three!

2507
02:26:46,779 --> 02:26:48,382
Upper Three!

2508
02:26:53,059 --> 02:26:54,445
[♪ haunting
choral music playing]

2509
02:26:54,661 --> 02:26:56,438
[KOKUSHIBO] Akaza!

2510
02:26:56,653 --> 02:26:59,295
His presence has vanished.

2511
02:27:01,201 --> 02:27:03,972
What a baffling conclusion.

2512
02:27:06,918 --> 02:27:08,347
Akaza...

2513
02:27:09,733 --> 02:27:13,890
...what happened to your burning
ambition to defeat me?

2514
02:27:15,796 --> 02:27:20,170
To think you'd abandoned
everything you stood for...

2515
02:27:21,295 --> 02:27:25,064
...and turned your back
on the path to greatness.

2516
02:27:25,929 --> 02:27:27,705
[♪ music intensifies]

2517
02:27:31,775 --> 02:27:34,807
Your weakness appalls me.

2518
02:27:39,918 --> 02:27:41,001
Huh?

2519
02:27:41,997 --> 02:27:43,209
[exclaims]

2520
02:27:43,599 --> 02:27:44,768
This feeling.

2521
02:27:45,287 --> 02:27:47,843
Could Lord Akaza be dead?

2522
02:27:49,272 --> 02:27:50,701
Very strange.

2523
02:27:50,875 --> 02:27:54,165
Surely my imagination
must be running wild, right?

2524
02:27:54,685 --> 02:27:59,492
It almost felt like Lord Akaza
had turned into some creature.

2525
02:28:01,961 --> 02:28:04,732
But now that he's dead,
I guess it doesn't matter.

2526
02:28:04,906 --> 02:28:06,854
- [laughs]
- [rattling]

2527
02:28:07,894 --> 02:28:09,712
Let's see,

2528
02:28:09,886 --> 02:28:11,098
where was I?

2529
02:28:11,704 --> 02:28:13,827
Oh, I remember.

2530
02:28:14,304 --> 02:28:15,904
I had just asked for your name,
hadn't I?

2531
02:28:17,192 --> 02:28:19,226
[Kanao breathing shakily]

2532
02:28:30,584 --> 02:28:32,584
[KASUGAI CROW] Tanjiro! Giyu!

2533
02:28:32,794 --> 02:28:34,948
Have defeated Upper Three!

2534
02:28:35,160 --> 02:28:36,469
Upper Three!

2535
02:28:37,102 --> 02:28:38,327
Did you hear that?

2536
02:28:38,538 --> 02:28:41,706
Yes. Excellent work, Tomioka.

2537
02:28:42,212 --> 02:28:44,281
Excellent work, Kamado.

2538
02:28:44,958 --> 02:28:47,111
[♪ closing theme song playing]

2539
02:28:49,222 --> 02:28:52,601
Mr. Tomioka and Tanjiro.
They did it!

2540
02:28:52,813 --> 02:28:55,304
[IGURO] Now it's our turn
to follow their lead.

2541
02:28:55,811 --> 02:28:57,120
Right!

2542
02:29:04,257 --> 02:29:05,482
[demon snarling]

2543
02:29:11,099 --> 02:29:13,421
Hang in there, Agatsuma!

2544
02:29:17,306 --> 02:29:18,616
[cawing]

2545
02:29:18,827 --> 02:29:20,601
[INOSUKE] Start flapping
those wings faster,

2546
02:29:20,812 --> 02:29:22,163
or I'm gonna keep poking!

2547
02:29:22,670 --> 02:29:24,064
You're gonna use those wings

2548
02:29:24,275 --> 02:29:25,615
to show me where
the strongest demon is!

2549
02:29:25,859 --> 02:29:27,129
You hear me?

2550
02:29:27,667 --> 02:29:30,159
I'm coming through!

2551
02:29:30,697 --> 02:29:32,016
Hyah!

2552
02:29:32,260 --> 02:29:33,726
Now we're talkin'!

2553
02:29:33,971 --> 02:29:36,853
I'm sensing a powerful
demon over here.

2554
02:29:37,098 --> 02:29:38,662
[cawing]

2555
02:29:44,575 --> 02:29:45,575
Where is Big Brother?

2556
02:29:53,339 --> 02:29:54,878
Where are all the Upper Ranks?

2557
02:29:55,046 --> 02:29:56,618
Tell me! Come on!

2558
02:29:56,986 --> 02:29:59,095
I'm gonna bury you all!

2559
02:30:05,119 --> 02:30:06,557
[KANATA] The passageway
leading north

2560
02:30:06,725 --> 02:30:08,030
on the 88th level is clear.

2561
02:30:08,198 --> 02:30:09,336
No sign of Muzan.

2562
02:30:09,871 --> 02:30:11,276
[KUINA]
The 100th and 27th levels

2563
02:30:11,444 --> 02:30:13,318
in the southeast are clear.
No sign of Muzan.

2564
02:30:14,088 --> 02:30:15,360
He's in here.

2565
02:30:15,526 --> 02:30:16,525
He has to be.

2566
02:30:16,526 --> 02:30:17,769
But where is he?

2567
02:30:18,103 --> 02:30:19,843
[KANATA] There's no sign
of Muzan on any of the levels

2568
02:30:19,978 --> 02:30:21,718
from 90 to 100, either.

2569
02:30:23,057 --> 02:30:25,366
[KUINA] Covering the entire
100th and 33rd levels.

2570
02:30:25,533 --> 02:30:26,604
No sign of Muzan.

2571
02:30:27,742 --> 02:30:29,448
Our crows will find you.

2572
02:30:29,616 --> 02:30:31,590
You can only hide from us
for so long.

2573
02:30:32,025 --> 02:30:34,535
We'll search every inch
of this Infinity Castle.

2574
02:30:34,669 --> 02:30:37,681
Even if you try to run from us,
we will hunt you down.

2575
02:30:38,049 --> 02:30:39,288
[plucking]

2576
02:30:40,827 --> 02:30:41,931
FOUR

2577
02:30:42,366 --> 02:30:44,040
[continues plucking
biwa strings]

2578
02:30:48,926 --> 02:30:51,302
Multi-layered structures
are headed northeast.

2579
02:30:51,670 --> 02:30:54,480
Attention! The castle's
expanding in every direction.

2580
02:30:54,615 --> 02:30:55,853
Folding over themselves!

2581
02:30:56,020 --> 02:30:58,397
[Nakime plucking
biwa strings faster]

2582
02:30:58,965 --> 02:31:00,304
[BOTH] And becoming one!

2583
02:31:04,721 --> 02:31:06,729
[gasps] You can't be serious.

2584
02:31:07,599 --> 02:31:08,669
No.

2585
02:31:08,670 --> 02:31:09,670
It's fine.

2586
02:31:09,775 --> 02:31:11,180
We've come too far to lose.

2587
02:31:11,749 --> 02:31:13,289
Crows, push forward,

2588
02:31:13,456 --> 02:31:14,828
and find Muzan!

2589
02:31:18,476 --> 02:31:20,885
[MUZAN] Try all you want,
Demon Slayers!

2590
02:31:21,053 --> 02:31:22,558
But each one of you
will meet your end

2591
02:31:22,726 --> 02:31:23,964
before ever reaching me!

2592
02:31:24,232 --> 02:31:27,144
You may be feeling smug after
beheading one of my Upper Ranks,

2593
02:31:27,310 --> 02:31:30,289
but unless you could kill me,
your triumph is meaningless!

2594
02:31:30,925 --> 02:31:33,334
[laughs maliciously]

2595
02:31:33,502 --> 02:31:35,443
You're all going to die
the most pointless deaths

2596
02:31:35,610 --> 02:31:37,719
all the while
never seeing my face!

2597
02:31:37,886 --> 02:31:41,031
I can't think of a more fitting
end for the Demon Slayer Corps.

2598
02:31:41,433 --> 02:31:43,308
Mark my words.
When I'm done here,

2599
02:31:43,474 --> 02:31:45,483
I'm going to make you regret
the day you were born!

2600
02:31:46,320 --> 02:31:47,390
Just wait.

2601
02:31:47,558 --> 02:31:49,800
You're each going to squirm
and writhe in pain.

2602
02:31:49,967 --> 02:31:51,272
Draw your final breaths

2603
02:31:51,439 --> 02:31:53,681
because for every one
of you Demon Slayers,

2604
02:31:53,816 --> 02:31:56,426
there is no tomorrow!

2605
02:32:04,190 --> 02:32:05,362
[KASUGAI CROW 1] Please, Giyu.

2606
02:32:08,072 --> 02:32:09,578
Don't die!

2607
02:32:14,933 --> 02:32:17,878
[KASUGAI CROW 2] We can't
have you dying on us, Tanjiro.

2608
02:32:27,415 --> 02:32:29,155
[music ends]

2609
02:32:29,290 --> 02:32:30,829
[♪ closing theme song playing]

2610
02:33:35,050 --> 02:33:36,991
[song ends]

2611
02:33:37,991 --> 02:33:57,991
